8ff44821caf8394f0df126","sha":"111140268ac6e850738ff44821caf8394f0df126","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/commits/111140268ac6e850738ff44821caf8394f0df126"}],"sha":"1a0801d172c69718ea78e127f839662e3362f86b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/commits/1a0801d172c69718ea78e127f839662e3362f86b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50881320?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/itsSauraj","id":50881320,"login":"itsSauraj","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwODgxMzIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/commits/111140268ac6e850738ff44821caf8394f0df126/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T12:29:17Z","email":"sauraj.contact@gmail.com","name":"Saurabh Yadav"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T12:29:17Z","email":"sauraj.contact@gmail.com","name":"Saurabh Yadav"},"message":"fix(ui): pick ScrollArea axes with a prop, not by passing ScrollBar as a child\n\nThe horizontal scrollbar got stuck because it was being scrolled. `ScrollArea`\nrenders `{children}` INSIDE the viewport, so\n`<ScrollBar orientation=\"horizontal\" />` passed as a child landed in the scrolling\ncontent and slid away with the very thing it was measuring. A scrollbar has to be\na sibling of the viewport, and children cannot be.\n\nThe demo did exactly that, and the docs and the changeset both instructed it, so\nthe API was teaching its own bug.\n\nReplaced with `axis: ''y'' | ''x'' | ''both''`, defaulting to `''y''`. The component now\nrenders the bars itself, as siblings, and `ScrollBar` stays exported only for\ncomposing the primitive by hand.\n\n`axis` turns out to carry real meaning beyond which bar is drawn. Radix enables the\nviewport overflow per axis from whether a scrollbar for that axis is mounted, so\nthe default now leaves `overflow-x: hidden` instead of allowing silent sideways\ndrift, and `axis=\"x\"` gives a horizontal-only region that does not become a\nvertical scroll container. That last part matters here: an unnecessary scroll\ncontainer is exactly the dead-wheel-zone that took ScrollArea off the docs chrome.\n\n`type` now defaults to `''auto''` rather than Radix''s `''hover''`. A bar that only\nexists while the pointer is inside the box is indistinguishable from a broken one,\nand it hid the bug above rather than showing it. `''auto''` shows the bar whenever\nthe content overflows, which is also what makes the thumb''s position observable.\n\nVerified: format, lint, typecheck 7/7, build 4/4, size 6/6, package:check 10/10,\ntests 1014 icons + 500 ui + 453 tokens. `axis?:` is present in the source shipped\nat /r/scroll-area.json, the demo references ScrollBar nowhere, and both generated\ncode variants carry the prop.","tree":{"sha":"5e35e404a17c6706cc0d4a054b1ce2d6dabf5a2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/git/trees/5e35e404a17c6706cc0d4a054b1ce2d6dabf5a2c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/git/commits/111140268ac6e850738ff44821caf8394f0df126","verification":{"payload":"tree 5e35e404a17c6706cc0d4a054b1ce2d6dabf5a2c\nparent 46f03e2529c6f1a1525ea2c7b3acfb6097beec39\nauthor Saurabh Yadav <sauraj.contact@gmail.com> 1787142557 +0530\ncommitter Saurabh Yadav <sauraj.contact@gmail.com> 1787142557 +0530\n\nfix(ui): pick ScrollArea axes with a prop, not by passing ScrollBar as a child\n\nThe horizontal scrollbar got stuck because it was being scrolled. `ScrollArea`\nrenders `{children}` INSIDE the viewport, so\n`<ScrollBar orientation=\"horizontal\" />` passed as a child landed in the scrolling\ncontent and slid away with the very thing it was measuring. A scrollbar has to be\na sibling of the viewport, and children cannot be.\n\nThe demo did exactly that, and the docs and the changeset both instructed it, so\nthe API was teaching its own bug.\n\nReplaced with `axis: ''y'' | ''x'' | ''both''`, defaulting to `''y''`. The component now\nrenders the bars itself, as siblings, and `ScrollBar` stays exported only for\ncomposing the primitive by hand.\n\n`axis` turns out to carry real meaning beyond which bar is drawn. Radix enables the\nviewport overflow per axis from whether a scrollbar for that axis is mounted, so\nthe default now leaves `overflow-x: hidden` instead of allowing silent sideways\ndrift, and `axis=\"x\"` gives a horizontal-only region that does not become a\nvertical scroll container. That last part matters here: an unnecessary scroll\ncontainer is exactly the dead-wheel-zone that took ScrollArea off the docs chrome.\n\n`type` now defaults to `''auto''` rather than Radix''s `''hover''`. A bar that only\nexists while the pointer is inside the box is indistinguishable from a broken one,\nand it hid the bug above rather than showing it. `''auto''` shows the bar whenever\nthe content overflows, which is also what makes the thumb''s position observable.\n\nVerified: format, lint, typecheck 7/7, build 4/4, size 6/6, package:check 10/10,\ntests 1014 icons + 500 ui + 453 tokens. `axis?:` is present in the source shipped\nat /r/scroll-area.json, the demo references ScrollBar nowhere, and both generated\ncode variants carry the prop.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQHPBAABCAA5FiEEmTLsOhbjX1ndSoeT9vAKBAaqrIkFAmqFoZ0bFIAAAAAABAAO\nbWFudTIsMi41KzEuMTIsMiwxAAoJEPbwCgQGqqyJMcYL/A46KnbKuXXq8qm6WuSC\nT+qeh63s4yVkfiMOsKgq/VhENLIHC+swua+1Mpg+58Y2CDx18pc+Mz8jAkIYp3JN\n6thW3XGZIHNqtlCNOFZbRy+FnqjXTrtz8CjwA4MhbBicolwhJx/Zp9xBOvXo58Pt\nj1L/IsRtHEYuLvpa0TfJqqIZj/iIR380oTr7AfLLUs90ANCdIr3QR3nNnta3BldD\nafil1prrnQpbGTA3qaVwOMqYmDh9EqQzStv4/GkPYMGndKJG9nPl2O6/MhTNdjjN\nTx40Bxq4a2rv+FVfw+4ymSowgqvmJnb0QAstB9JvrmCgM5pazlo+w1itHbsd/bfU\nhER07lOiLUINGgk8hK03NdLh5a3zKsTZr68cyTQ/bXf2q1G2iS4M/sjUU++TT2Zv\ndvfd770NlzJHww1YbNKUmVYZIjK5SMrYtRFxsgG0bsbffdzQ9nRX95VdWP1FhInZ\n8QGa+QAOlLxwr4q9VA/LgwNmBju8gIbFP3sFe4lin6k2dg==\n=uJc6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T12:29:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50881320?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/itsSauraj","id":50881320,"login":"itsSauraj","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwODgxMzIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VeloBits/velobits-UI/commit/111140268ac6e850738ff44821caf8394f0df126","node_id":"C_kwDOTuZyj9oAKDExMTE0MDI2OGFjNmU4NTA3MzhmZjQ0ODIxY2FmODM5NGYwZGYxMjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VeloBits/velobits-UI/commit/46f03e2529c6f1a1525ea2c7b3acfb6097beec39","sha":"46f03e2529c6f1a1525ea2c7b3acfb6097beec39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/commits/46f03e2529c6f1a1525ea2c7b3acfb6097beec39"}],"sha":"111140268ac6e850738ff44821caf8394f0df126","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/commits/111140268ac6e850738ff44821caf8394f0df126"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50881320?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/itsSauraj","id":50881320,"login":"itsSauraj","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwODgxMzIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/commits/46f03e2529c6f1a1525ea2c7b3acfb6097beec39/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T12:28:52Z","email":"sauraj.contact@gmail.com","name":"Saurabh Yadav"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T12:28:52Z","email":"sauraj.contact@gmail.com","name":"Saurabh Yadav"},"message":"fix(build): hash the registry sources, which turbo was not looking at\n\n`@velobitsio/ui`''s sources are not in `packages/ui`. They live in\n`registry/velobits/`, because that directory is also what the shadcn CLI serves,\nand tsup''s entry map points up out of the package at it. Turbo''s default input set\nis the files inside the package, so none of the actual component sources were part\nof `@velobitsio/ui#build`''s hash.\n\nThe effect is worse than a missed rebuild. Editing a component leaves the hash\nunchanged, so turbo reports `cache hit, replaying logs` and RESTORES the previous\n`dist/**` over whatever is there. A correct build done seconds earlier is\noverwritten by a stale artifact:\n\n    rm -rf dist && npm run build -w @velobitsio/ui   # axis in the .d.ts: yes\n    npm run build                                    # cache hit, replaying\n                                                     # axis in the .d.ts: gone\n\nThat is how it was found: a new prop was in the source, in a hand-built `dist`,\nand absent from the types the docs app compiled against, three times in a row.\n\nIt is also a publishing hazard rather than only a nuisance. `release.yml` runs\n`turbo run build` immediately before `changeset publish`, so a component edited\nwithout touching any file inside `packages/ui` could ship the previous version of\nitself to npm, with a green build and a passing test run, since the tests import\nthe same stale `dist`.\n\n`globalDependencies` rather than per-package `inputs`: `registry/` is the source\nfor `packages/ui` AND is read directly by the docs codegen (`build-registry.ts`,\n`build-docs-data.ts`), so more than one package''s hash depends on it. Invalidating\ntokens and icons too is a few seconds of rebuild against silently shipping the\nwrong bytes.","tree":{"sha":"32215e099349d0b6ff353f51cefa4f4a8108855d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/git/trees/32215e099349d0b6ff353f51cefa4f4a8108855d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/git/commits/46f03e2529c6f1a1525ea2c7b3acfb6097beec39","verification":{"payload":"tree 32215e099349d0b6ff353f51cefa4f4a8108855d\nparent eb460077f2c3d778c55d4910e6c60022efd3db88\nauthor Saurabh Yadav <sauraj.contact@gmail.com> 1787142532 +0530\ncommitter Saurabh Yadav <sauraj.contact@gmail.com> 1787142532 +0530\n\nfix(build): hash the registry sources, which turbo was not looking at\n\n`@velobitsio/ui`''s sources are not in `packages/ui`. They live in\n`registry/velobits/`, because that directory is also what the shadcn CLI serves,\nand tsup''s entry map points up out of the package at it. Turbo''s default input set\nis the files inside the package, so none of the actual component sources were part\nof `@velobitsio/ui#build`''s hash.\n\nThe effect is worse than a missed rebuild. Editing a component leaves the hash\nunchanged, so turbo reports `cache hit, replaying logs` and RESTORES the previous\n`dist/**` over whatever is there. A correct build done seconds earlier is\noverwritten by a stale artifact:\n\n    rm -rf dist && npm run build -w @velobitsio/ui   # axis in the .d.ts: yes\n    npm run build                                    # cache hit, replaying\n                                                     # axis in the .d.ts: gone\n\nThat is how it was found: a new prop was in the source, in a hand-built `dist`,\nand absent from the types the docs app compiled against, three times in a row.\n\nIt is also a publishing hazard rather than only a nuisance. `release.yml` runs\n`turbo run build` immediately before `changeset publish`, so a component edited\nwithout touching any file inside `packages/ui` could ship the previous version of\nitself to npm, with a green build and a passing test run, since the tests import\nthe same stale `dist`.\n\n`globalDependencies` rather than per-package `inputs`: `registry/` is the source\nfor `packages/ui` AND is read directly by the docs codegen (`build-registry.ts`,\n`build-docs-data.ts`), so more than one package''s hash depends on it. Invalidating\ntokens and icons too is a few seconds of rebuild against silently shipping the\nwrong bytes.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQHPBAABCAA5FiEEmTLsOhbjX1ndSoeT9vAKBAaqrIkFAmqFoYQbFIAAAAAABAAO\nbWFudTIsMi41KzEuMTIsMiwxAAoJEPbwCgQGqqyJ7YsMAKjI5pEKg+c17qDc7ML+\nEoIIAIcItexcZZt3Z9gSn/842MMsv59sLxuvXH5oj24AeOK