orm for VeloBits skills\n\n- Changed installation command from URL format to namespaced format in documentation and code.\n- Updated references in skill documentation to reflect the new installation commands.\n- Enhanced clarity on how the agent skill resolves by namespace and its absence from the component index.","tree":{"sha":"c00ddacdbdcc36290425c0411382c0508c7e8008","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/git/trees/c00ddacdbdcc36290425c0411382c0508c7e8008"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/git/commits/fb97a241bd528e1d3a0277dcdf33bc3ed9547590","verification":{"payload":"tree c00ddacdbdcc36290425c0411382c0508c7e8008\nparent 1154fb904d6aebaeebe50ae90c2919560a8cf57e\nauthor Saurabh Yadav <sauraj.contact@gmail.com> 1787137421 +0530\ncommitter Saurabh Yadav <sauraj.contact@gmail.com> 1787137421 +0530\n\nrefactor: update installation commands to use namespaced form for VeloBits skills\n\n- Changed installation command from URL format to namespaced format in documentation and code.\n- Updated references in skill documentation to reflect the new installation commands.\n- Enhanced clarity on how the agent skill resolves by namespace and its absence from the component index.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQHPBAABCAA5FiEEmTLsOhbjX1ndSoeT9vAKBAaqrIkFAmqFjY0bFIAAAAAABAAO\nbWFudTIsMi41KzEuMTIsMiwxAAoJEPbwCgQGqqyJTlgMALadXAuI4KkcCnCq2JxR\nEQ0oPO5EspXi5/qLc+hS++Tv0XVSOBFCEpMuu4qHCvk3OguBcJop8u/9vhy3Em43\nE6SbnETm+XuPNaqjXagfgiEKJ4Zch56QG67ne/mwiCyva+fXe32736iVs4BfDDwR\nEYf2tCJSAVKXbEaK+gv6hEqrqEVluzHwquHIZMCdnzlSRuDk48B+tX8XhhbrkDC8\nkz1GbGKQ3/tjwtA2xzw2rMibrV1pgvrO/1PE2zAz4FbrRRi1P811QibLBCYeenSC\nWGW5IO+z+Jz89qo6z0eq+BK+oz2IA4FE8ry4eGeIZcStKPCoNdCxXvLcy+Ix79eG\noX0oltX07iwkBtflf4Ly1iL+tiLL48N/rswVbDB1bqkgHO1+YGPMEWI7C0VpSwDQ\nw8YjgLDwAPaMuOMjzJ6nnBk6DFgaefFX5hBn564azB3ooygmmAONm2OJKFMNsD4A\nbh/VUuVD+Tq1c8j0DYJ+4Y3BJXB5Mfrh/OtxFORvBoZ1wQ==\n=ru4y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T11:03:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50881320?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/itsSauraj","id":50881320,"login":"itsSauraj","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwODgxMzIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VeloBits/velobits-UI/commit/fb97a241bd528e1d3a0277dcdf33bc3ed9547590","node_id":"C_kwDOTuZyj9oAKGZiOTdhMjQxYmQ1MjhlMWQzYTAyNzdkY2RmMzNiYzNlZDk1NDc1OTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VeloBits/velobits-UI/commit/1154fb904d6aebaeebe50ae90c2919560a8cf57e","sha":"1154fb904d6aebaeebe50ae90c2919560a8cf57e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/commits/1154fb904d6aebaeebe50ae90c2919560a8cf57e"}],"sha":"fb97a241bd528e1d3a0277dcdf33bc3ed9547590","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/commits/fb97a241bd528e1d3a0277dcdf33bc3ed9547590"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50881320?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/itsSauraj","id":50881320,"login":"itsSauraj","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwODgxMzIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/commits/1154fb904d6aebaeebe50ae90c2919560a8cf57e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T11:00:01Z","email":"sauraj.contact@gmail.com","name":"Saurabh Yadav"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T11:00:01Z","email":"sauraj.contact@gmail.com","name":"Saurabh Yadav"},"message":"fix(docs): scroll the docs chrome natively again, not with ScrollArea\n\nPutting ScrollArea on the sidebar and the three \"On this page\" columns made them\nscroll harshly and shift, and the cause is in Radix rather than in the styling.\n\nThe viewport''s overflow is not conditional:\n\n    overflowY: scrollbarYEnabled ? ''scroll'' : ''hidden''\n\n`scroll`, not `auto`. And `scrollbarYEnabled` is flipped by an effect inside\n`ScrollAreaScrollbar` on mount, so it is true as soon as a scrollbar renders,\nwhether or not anything overflows. `type=\"auto\"` does not help: it governs when\nthe BAR is visible, not the viewport overflow, and no prop separates the two.\n\nSo every one of those columns became a scroll container with nothing to scroll on\nmost pages. The wheel is captured, the page stays still, and it lurches when the\nchain finally reaches the document. A table of contents with four entries is the\nworst case, and the docs are full of them.\n\n`overflow-y-auto` becomes a scroller only when it needs to be, which is the right\nbehaviour for content whose length is decided by the page. Reverted to it, with\nthe reason recorded at the call site so this is not re-attempted as a tidy-up.\n\nScrollArea itself is unchanged and still correct for what it is for: a box that\nalways overflows and owns its height. Its own page still demonstrates it on both\naxes. The component docblock, the component page''s notes and the changeset now all\nsay where it does not belong, because \"use the design system''s scrollbar\neverywhere\" is the obvious next thought and it is wrong.\n\nVerified: format, lint, typecheck 7/7, build 4/4, tests 1014 icons + 500 ui + 453\ntokens. Confirmed in the built HTML: zero scroll-area viewports on an ordinary\ncomponent page, two on the scroll-area page, and lg:overflow-y-auto back on the\nsidebar.","tree":{"sha":"4be6490a8cb95d098fb742855e69336558ee700d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/git/trees/4be6490a8cb95d098fb742855e69336558ee700d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/git/commits/1154fb904d6aebaeebe50ae90c2919560a8cf57e","verification":{"payload":"tree 4be6490a8cb95d098fb742855e69336558ee700d\nparent 864a916d819ff14bca92e516bec93cd9116d0cb2\nauthor Saurabh Yadav <sauraj.contact@gmail.com> 1787137201 +0530\ncommitter Saurabh Yadav <sauraj.contact@gmail.com> 1787137201 +0530\n\nfix(docs): scroll the docs chrome natively again, not with ScrollArea\n\nPutting ScrollArea on the sidebar and the three \"On this page\" columns made them\nscroll harshly and shift, and the cause is in Radix rather than in the styling.\n\nThe viewport''s overflow is not conditional:\n\n    overflowY: scrollbarYEnabled ? ''scroll'' : ''hidden''\n\n`scroll`, not `auto`. And `scrollbarYEnabled` is flipped by an effect inside\n`ScrollAreaScrollbar` on mount, so it is true as soon as a scrollbar renders,\nwhether or not anything overflows. `type=\"auto\"` does not help: it governs when\nthe BAR is visible, not the viewport overflow, and no prop separates the two.\n\nSo every one of those columns became a scroll container with nothing to scroll on\nmost pages. The wheel is captured, the page stays still, and it lurches when the\nchain finally reaches the document. A table of contents with four entries is the\nworst case, and the docs are full of them.\n\n`overflow-y-auto` becomes a scroller only when it needs to be, which is the right\nbehaviour for content whose length is decided by the page. Reverted to it, with\nthe reason recorded at the call site so this is not re-attempted as a tidy-up.\n\nScrollArea itself is unchanged and still correct for what it is for: a box that\nalways overflows and owns its height. Its own page still demonstrates it on both\naxes. The component docblock, the component page''s notes and the changeset now all\nsay where it does not belong, because \"use the design system''s scrollbar\neverywhere\" is the obvious next thought and it is wrong.\n\nVerified: format, lint, typecheck 7/7, build 4/4, tests 1014 icons + 500 ui + 453\ntokens. Confirmed in the built HTML: zero scroll-area viewports on an ordinary\ncomponent page, two on the scroll-area page, and lg:overflow-y-auto back on the\nsidebar.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQHPBAABCAA5FiEEmTLsOhbjX1ndSoeT9vAKBAaqrIkFAmqFjLEbFIAAAAAABAAO\nbWFudTIsMi41KzEuMTIsMiwxAAoJEPbwCgQGqqyJlFgMAKbbEeAoyKQ/bbHKRihP\n4ZkjhDaeHxuhEZwTWrVkEso0kpUzSBsqoXWFLY4CXqoEx4oUnpYRlfUrMOFctjz/\ndxm051kknNMn3k3d4w2YWrlbN0jNDPKN4tQTYc8Sd1VuWOsn0Mk30jhxw1dP+xJa\nizbeGb+Pi7EJKasnndFMuQIPlQ8UcskQuwe7UmcUBdBhIRL1pPYfWUCmUknvtMNy\nq2WElfRk+9HATzcvXQ+pOuA1Ko/InKjdm6sfc3Tv5slG7PMQZqAADjc5QU/4Dkfl\nHuNC16pA9G9ATYnnbK2mjYEkdVXwtm1256USwFtRLVJ2sSQoVhKFyorSaFXgYKwW\n/LUSPrZjCDPQlMn8BBoNTgBUmzIPtz0+DhZB4gWDx1nrJ4j75ZqTqRyv5W4Rhtqc\nQN5KZ9xh3ASEDdtiehNN8aFRj/MrlmaTn1vyb7bznG7M68K2hdHuL2uK9C0nMg9L\ncT052NI7mrWvK3ggjz4jpSXaFjcw4Ni4aA8zU4h72uBCMQ==\n=Ouzu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T11:00:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.g