"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50881320?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/itsSauraj","id":50881320,"login":"itsSauraj","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwODgxMzIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/commits/c19e0b124677664d17c43bd1328ceff4c293e557/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T06:43:53Z","email":"sauraj.contact@gmail.com","name":"Saurabh Yadav"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T06:43:53Z","email":"sauraj.contact@gmail.com","name":"Saurabh Yadav"},"message":"feat(docs): show each example with CLI imports and npm imports\n\nAn example''s import lines are the one part of it that differs between the two\ndistributions, and the Code tab only ever showed one of them. It showed\n`@velobitsio/ui`, which is right for the npm package and wrong for everyone who\ninstalled with the CLI: that half has one file per component and no barrel, so\nthere is nothing to import a name from under that specifier. The tab was\nconfidently correct for one audience and confidently wrong for the other, with\nnothing on the page saying which.\n\nThe Code tab now nests shadcn CLI / npm, CLI first to match the Installation tabs\ndirectly above it.\n\nBoth variants come from the same file, so they cannot disagree about anything but\nthe imports. The CLI variant is derived at build time:\n\n- `importSpecifierFor` joins `registry-layout.ts`, which is already the single\n  source for where the CLI writes each file. The specifier a consumer types is a\n  function of the target the CLI is stamped with, so the two cannot drift.\n  `cn` correctly resolves to `@/lib/utils` rather than the velobits folder.\n- Which file exports a given name is parsed from the sources, not tabulated.\n  A barrel import of `{ Card, CardHeader, CardFooter }` becomes one line against\n  `@/components/ui/velobits/card`; a mixed one splits per owning file and sorts.\n  215 exports map, and 143 of them are actually imported by the 47 examples.\n- `@velobitsio/icons` and `@velobitsio/tokens` are deliberately NOT rewritten.\n  The registry items declare them as npm dependencies, so a CLI consumer installs\n  those from npm and imports them exactly as an npm consumer does. Rewriting them\n  would document an install that does not happen.\n- Long lines wrap the way Prettier wraps them, since generated string content is\n  not reachable by `prettier --write`.\n\nA name that cannot be attributed to a file fails the build rather than rendering\na plausible wrong path. That guard immediately earned itself: it caught\n`readFileSync(file.path)` in this change resolving against the wrong directory,\nbecause the root script and the workspace script run from different cwds. The\nfirst version also swallowed that read in a try/catch and `continue`d, which\nturned a missing file into \"no registry item exports Accordion\" three steps\nlater. It is now `join(root, file.path)` with no catch, matching the read already\nin this file.\n\nVerified: format, lint, typecheck 7/7, build 4/4, size 6/6, package:check 10/10,\ntests 1014 icons + 500 ui + 453 tokens. The Code tab is client-mounted so it is\nabsent from the prerendered HTML; confirmed instead in the built client chunk,\nwhich carries the \"shadcn CLI\" label and 43 distinct installed paths.","tree":{"sha":"99069faa0528a870afa0ca498e9c1769e0b8fc22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/git/trees/99069faa0528a870afa0ca498e9c1769e0b8fc22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/git/commits/c19e0b124677664d17c43bd1328ceff4c293e557","verification":{"payload":"tree 99069faa0528a870afa0ca498e9c1769e0b8fc22\nparent e43b28ba9636e8da10dc9f421d5043b7323af401\nauthor Saurabh Yadav <sauraj.contact@gmail.com> 1787121833 +0530\ncommitter Saurabh Yadav <sauraj.contact@gmail.com> 1787121833 +0530\n\nfeat(docs): show each example with CLI imports and npm imports\n\nAn example''s import lines are the one part of it that differs between the two\ndistributions, and the Code tab only ever showed one of them. It showed\n`@velobitsio/ui`, which is right for the npm package and wrong for everyone who\ninstalled with the CLI: that half has one file per component and no barrel, so\nthere is nothing to import a name from under that specifier. The tab was\nconfidently correct for one audience and confidently wrong for the other, with\nnothing on the page saying which.\n\nThe Code tab now nests shadcn CLI / npm, CLI first to match the Installation tabs\ndirectly above it.\n\nBoth variants come from the same file, so they cannot disagree about anything but\nthe imports. The CLI variant is derived at build time:\n\n- `importSpecifierFor` joins `registry-layout.ts`, which is already the single\n  source for where the CLI writes each file. The specifier a consumer types is a\n  function of the target the CLI is stamped with, so the two cannot drift.\n  `cn` correctly resolves to `@/lib/utils` rather than the velobits folder.\n- Which file exports a given name is parsed from the sources, not tabulated.\n  A barrel import of `{ Card, CardHeader, CardFooter }` becomes one line against\n  `@/components/ui/velobits/card`; a mixed one splits per owning file and sorts.\n  215 exports map, and 143 of them are actually imported by the 47 examples.\n- `@velobitsio/icons` and `@velobitsio/tokens` are deliberately NOT rewritten.\n  The registry items declare them as npm dependencies, so a CLI consumer installs\n  those from npm and imports them exactly as an npm consumer does. Rewriting them\n  would document an install that does not happen.\n- Long lines wrap the way Prettier wraps them, since generated string content is\n  not reachable by `prettier --write`.\n\nA name that cannot be attributed to a file fails the build rather than rendering\na plausible wrong path. That guard immediately earned itself: it caught\n`readFileSync(file.path)` in this change resolving against the wrong directory,\nbecause the root script and the workspace script run from different cwds. The\nfirst version also swallowed that read in a try/catch and `continue`d, which\nturned a missing file into \"no registry item exports Accordion\" three steps\nlater. It is now `join(root, file.path)` with no catch, matching the read already\nin this file.\n\nVerified: format, lint, typecheck 7/7, build 4/4, size 6/6, package:check 10/10,\ntests 1014 icons + 500 ui + 453 tokens. The Code tab is client-mounted so it is\nabsent from the prerendered HTML; confirmed instead in the built client chunk,\nwhich carries the \"shadcn CLI\" label and 43 distinct installed paths.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQHPBAABCAA5FiEEmTLsOhbjX1ndSoeT9vAKBAaqrIkFAmqFUKsbFIAAAAAABAAO\nbWFudTIsMi41KzEuMTIsMiwxAAoJEPbwCgQGqqyJxucMAJ7o9h1gKnv2zwEmY5t/\n5a32sXISZz/MLq53ivw801h7xk9yOjWQDiWBmtKK0ivkGUTcQ+MQQSxcg2ccSpgP\nFoJvGkRotfQshIo6tj1lf2apVTVPe9cM25s42ZAXmKj+CJuNNVckZbVyBHlfnUOf\nzMshLNmKa4sdNvBw6h4jIU5HVhjpb0DWMuidcPhTuNjkIqQKf3+PrH2o3VY/jzKU\n9QvjhJJqx+XyPDB3g+ikRdzTSoPplpt7OYHNqXpnoTjJ1bRRhrAiCHeeUMTa1uXA\nJ6RCDYGcJf5LQsgC+v1lp6UrttRR5Eh6UNmrGAyHlkbLgW+Mo/tgel0p73BoEIDJ\nRHJAjpRnRemgrHg7/R+VWalr080PGneNU3icAo960bM3e7aI49blYYuLtAHgHt1X\nc1CCcw0cOBsXrp1ZdsTtl5Q1EOigpxBIu6Z2i