nts","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VeloBits/velobits-UI/commit/7dd394cdf03583c50d1e9bddcbe2025fea244182","node_id":"C_kwDOTuZyj9oAKDdkZDM5NGNkZjAzNTgzYzUwZDFlOWJkZGNiZTIwMjVmZWEyNDQxODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VeloBits/velobits-UI/commit/d92d8cb80d69920de512d61139f8fdc2db6ff474","sha":"d92d8cb80d69920de512d61139f8fdc2db6ff474","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/commits/d92d8cb80d69920de512d61139f8fdc2db6ff474"}],"sha":"7dd394cdf03583c50d1e9bddcbe2025fea244182","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/commits/7dd394cdf03583c50d1e9bddcbe2025fea244182"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50881320?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/itsSauraj","id":50881320,"login":"itsSauraj","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwODgxMzIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/commits/d92d8cb80d69920de512d61139f8fdc2db6ff474/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T13:02:36Z","email":"sauraj.contact@gmail.com","name":"Saurabh Yadav"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T13:02:36Z","email":"sauraj.contact@gmail.com","name":"Saurabh Yadav"},"message":"fix(release): parse the username out of npm whoami, not npm''s warnings\n\nThe preflight captured `who=$(npm whoami … 2>&1)`. The `2>&1` is right for the\nfailure path — when whoami fails the reason is on stderr and is the only useful\noutput — but on SUCCESS it swallows npm''s chatter into the same variable, and\nsetup-node writes `always-auth` into the temporary .npmrc it generates, so npm\nwarns about an unknown config on every invocation.\n\nSo $who was not \"velobits-team\". It was that warning paragraph with the username\non the end, and every comparison downstream ran against prose.\n\nThe visible result was an error that disproved itself:\n\n  error: npm user ''npm warn Unknown user config \"always-auth\"…\n  velobits-team'' is NOT a member of the ''velobitsio'' org\n  Members seen: { \"velobits-team\": \"owner\" }\n\nIt denied the membership while printing it. Worse than the cryptic E404 this\npreflight exists to replace, because that one was at least not self-contradictory\n— this blocked a release with a claim the same message refuted two lines later.\n\nNow the capture keeps `2>&1` for the failure path, then strips npm''s own\n`warn|notice|error` prefixes and trailing CR and takes the last non-empty line,\nwhich is the identity. Empty after filtering is its own error rather than a\nsilent comparison against \"\".\n\nTested against the exact output from run 31802390368: contaminated CI output,\nclean output, CRLF, several stacked warnings, and warnings-only all parse to\n`velobits-team` or fail loudly. Re-running the membership check with the parsed\nvalue resolves it as owner.\n\nThis unblocks the preflight only. The publish still fails afterwards: the token\nreads (whoami, org ls and access list all succeed) but cannot write, so it needs\nreissuing with publish rights.","tree":{"sha":"ace662babb95924dde2c949575014718b725c35a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/git/trees/ace662babb95924dde2c949575014718b725c35a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VeloBits/velobits-UI/git/commits/d92d8cb80d69920de512d61139f8fdc2db6ff474","verification":{"payload":"tree ace662babb95924dde2c949575014718b725c35a\nparent edb84e9c09693573496a32ddaf7ce07ff88e6191\nauthor Saurabh Yadav <sauraj.contact@gmail.com> 1786712556 +0530\ncommitter Saurabh Yadav <sauraj.contact@gmail.com> 1786712556 +0530\n\nfix(release): parse the username out of npm whoami, not npm''s warnings\n\nThe preflight captured `who=$(npm whoami … 2>&1)`. The `2>&1` is right for the\nfailure path — when whoami fails the reason is on stderr and is the only useful\noutput — but on SUCCESS it swallows npm''s chatter into the same variable, and\nsetup-node writes `always-auth` into the temporary .npmrc it generates, so npm\nwarns about an unknown config on every invocation.\n\nSo $who was not \"velobits-team\". It was that warning paragraph with the username\non the end, and every comparison downstream ran against prose.\n\nThe visible result was an error that disproved itself:\n\n  error: npm user ''npm warn Unknown user config \"always-auth\"…\n  velobits-team'' is NOT a member of the ''velobitsio'' org\n  Members seen: { \"velobits-team\": \"owner\" }\n\nIt denied the membership while printing it. Worse than the cryptic E404 this\npreflight exists to replace, because that one was at least not self-contradictory\n— this blocked a release with a claim the same message refuted two lines later.\n\nNow the capture keeps `2>&1` for the failure path, then strips npm''s own\n`warn|notice|error` prefixes and trailing CR and takes the last non-empty line,\nwhich is the identity. Empty after filtering is its own error rather than a\nsilent comparison against \"\".\n\nTested against the exact output from run 31802390368: contaminated CI output,\nclean output, CRLF, several stacked warnings, and warnings-only all parse to\n`velobits-team` or fail loudly. Re-running the membership check with the parsed\nvalue resolves it as owner.\n\nThis unblocks the preflight only. The publish still fails afterwards: the token\nreads (whoami, org ls and access list all succeed) but cannot write, so it needs\nreissuing with publish rights.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQHPBAABCAA5FiEEmTLsOhbjX1ndSoeT9vAKBAaqrIkFAmp/EewbFIAAAAAABAAO\nbWFudTIsMi41KzEuMTIsMiwxAAoJEPbwCgQGqqyJ8IoL/390YbvG6hqgFh8Zg5En\nP4qnmc+YB8rF/l4o1k8rOmfLZDyAxAgvb/EvNZ7fBylEg21XwlZPQbTG3tDxsFGO\nsu6PTiyJ/A3Q9geeugJEl+EH5TfaIqLsgrCMLqqpDfEH3gfg8YdbA8zhZu5MdMjV\nXJKT99tyI2VQybUm1OrwjmYmoO5f1XBxmruJTb+EUbUkhPZkwB5KeFQpf9R+3tRO\nHfQC+v60WA7pWUP9LFSyrMnmzIMJ/DeR58BBCPAmt8GcaXDp2y/A9dtO0ERXu0Qy\notlUAhcdNs9PSzul5FfPhSEaQuCwCRcxtWY7sxGHOESsGdXGENILdaKIxvUYrRrh\nOepz5bb5+eh9aiBNE5CJGIuqgS/EFNT1vWZwDMcgwOiKKPr2seKVL75b65+yv3Ip\nMHQi/G4lu1G7uHJLN5iseu/m8EnKduf62dviuWxoxruYIZ3Dq9fmHnhw2VqfxCKM\nQy/9XlLQOuqkdk8SQ2aPC/vqlrlutgdCpGNTMAR14EHHjw==\n=VioL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T13:02:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50881320?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/itsSauraj","id":50881320,"login":"itsSauraj","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwODgxMzIw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsSauraj/starred