r":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/bac6ae971706f4974c608828026015e6c51481d0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T06:09:59Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T06:10:08Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"docs(core): one dense sentence, and the invariant rather than its history\n\nThe comment rule in CLAUDE.md — why not what, never the past, one dense\nsentence beats a paragraph — governed every file here and nothing enforced\nit. This is the source half of the pass.\n\nWhere a measured fact would not fit a sentence it moved rather than went:\nthe `relatedTarget === null` reasoning now sits on the guard that reads it,\nand the `aria-hidden` decision on `createGuard`, where the markers are\nbuilt. `attach-focus-containment.ts` opened with 623 words of detached\nJSDoc attached to nothing; it is 118 now.\n\nNo executable line is touched — asserted by stripping every comment range\nfrom both revisions of all 76 changed files and diffing the remainder.","tree":{"sha":"7c2db9a51b166eff1d08150dbebed46a3c31d355","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/7c2db9a51b166eff1d08150dbebed46a3c31d355"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/bac6ae971706f4974c608828026015e6c51481d0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/bac6ae971706f4974c608828026015e6c51481d0","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKGJhYzZhZTk3MTcwNmY0OTc0YzYwODgyODAyNjAxNWU2YzUxNDgxZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/0c74580ccaf2dfc9a6feddd5b41c8a06ffad3b33","sha":"0c74580ccaf2dfc9a6feddd5b41c8a06ffad3b33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/0c74580ccaf2dfc9a6feddd5b41c8a06ffad3b33"}],"sha":"bac6ae971706f4974c608828026015e6c51481d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/bac6ae971706f4974c608828026015e6c51481d0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/0c74580ccaf2dfc9a6feddd5b41c8a06ffad3b33/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T05:20:54Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T05:20:54Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"fix(playground): the contained panel stops blocking the list it sits over\n\nThree defects in one example, all of them the same shape: the card claimed a\nnon-modal panel leaves the region behind it usable, and by keyboard or by mouse\nit did not.\n\n**The only way to choose a row was to close the panel.** Each row carried a\n\"Details\" button at its end, and the panel takes 62% of the card from the right\n— `elementFromPoint` puts all three of those buttons underneath it. The row is\nthe button now, so the target is the invoice name, which is in the strip the\npanel leaves; the end-of-row control is gone rather than duplicated.\n\n**`containFocus` made Escape the only exit.** It wraps Tab inside the dialog,\nwhich suits a panel behaving like a modal, and this one sits over a list the\nreader is meant to keep using. With a single focusable child the wrap put Tab\nand Shift+Tab both back on Close — sixteen presses, measured, without leaving.\nDropped; the opening focus still lands on Close through `focusOnOpen`, which is\nwhat the arrow keys needed, not the containment.\n\n**The selected row was a background colour and nothing else.** `aria-current`\ncarries it now, since the row''s own name never changes to say which one the\npanel is showing.\n\nThe list answers ↑/↓ itself, through the library''s own utilities — the first\nuse of `isKeyClaimedByPopup` and `matchesHotkey` anywhere in the playground,\nthough `src/index.ts` names this exact case as why they are exported: a surface\ndriving its own key inherits none of the dialog''s listeners and a second copy of\nthe rule drifts. One `arrowDelta` serves both the panel and the list, so the two\ncannot disagree about what a held modifier means.\n\nFocus restoration is left alone. Closing returns to the row that opened the\npanel rather than the one it ended on, which is correct: the library restores\nonly when focus was still inside at close, and leaves it where the reader put it\notherwise — verified both ways.\n\nPinned by a new `contained` smoke flow, ten checks, because no other gate\nrenders the playground and every claim here is geometry or focus.\n\nVerified: check, type-check:registry, 583 unit, 386 component (cold cache, three\nengines), build + verify:package, playground build, smoke green in both themes.","tree":{"sha":"d1347106e9b835714d2c008447c068aacc57c5de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/d1347106e9b835714d2c008447c068aacc57c5de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/0c74580ccaf2dfc9a6feddd5b41c8a06ffad3b33","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/0c74580ccaf2dfc9a6feddd5b41c8a06ffad3b33","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKDBjNzQ1ODBjY2FmMmRmYzlhNmZlZGRkNWI0MWM4YTA2ZmZhZDNiMzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/33ad32fc26ae0e974d7c01ab9ccfebdc154f9de5","sha":"33ad32fc26ae0e974d7c01ab9ccfebdc154f9de5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/33ad32fc26ae0e974d7c01ab9ccfebdc154f9de5"}],"sha":"0c74580ccaf2dfc9a6feddd5b41c8a06ffad3b33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/0c74580ccaf2dfc9a6feddd5b41c8a06ffad3b33"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/33ad32fc26ae0e974d7c01ab9ccfebdc154f9de5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T03:50:39Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T03:50:39Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"docs: the changelog entry covers the tail, and one comment finds its file again\n\nThe sweep''s entry was written before its last three commits, so the migration\nguide stopped short of the constants, the dead anchors, the inverted name and\nthe trimmed ids. It carries them now — none is a public break (\n`DEFAULT_DIALOG_ANIMATION` is internal, the ids are test-side), but the entry is\nthe record of what moved and it was incomplete.\n\nIt also states what the sweep left broken rather than quietly repairing it: two\nlinks in `CHANGELOG.md` name `src/core/modal-director.ts` and\n`src/core/__tests__/modal-store.test.ts`, which no longer exist. Three more\nlinks in that file were already dead before any of this started, which is the\nargument for leaving all five: the file''s own header says entries are left as\nwritten, and a record of what was true on a date outlives the paths it names.\n\n`dialog-manager.test.ts` pointed a reader at `complib-bridge.ct.tsx` for the\nDOM half of the `dialog:close` branch. That file has never existed on this\nbranch — the coverage is in `dialog-manager.ct.tsx`, three tests of it — so the\npointer now names a file someone can open.\n\nVerified: check clean, doc budgets pass.","tree":{"sha":"ab7409472a796940dafb32e7105fae6adc2b00fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/ab7409472a796940dafb32e7105fae6adc2b00fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/33ad32fc26ae0e974d7c01ab9ccfebdc154f9de5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/33ad32fc26ae0e974d7c01ab9ccfebdc154f9de5","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKDMzYWQzMmZjMjZhZTBlOTc0ZDdjMDFhYjljY2ZlYmRjMTU0ZjlkZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/cd7b114c1aa82abefa10eb6968513ed60b8c247d","sha":"cd7b114c1aa82abefa10eb6968513ed60b8c247d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/cd7b114c1aa82abefa10eb6968513ed60b8c247d"}],"sha":"33ad32fc26ae0e974d7c01ab9ccfebdc154f9de5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/33ad32fc26ae0e974d7c01ab9ccfebdc154f9de5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/cd7b114c1aa82abefa10eb6968513ed60b8c247d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T03:41:17Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T03:41:17Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"refactor(tests): a dialog id does not need to say \"dialog\"\n\nThe generated test id is `dialog-<id>`, so an id ending in `-dialog` came out as\n`dialog-basic-dialog`. Not a regression — it read `modal-basic-modal` before —\nbut the sweep is the moment to stop carrying it.\n\nSixteen ids lose the suffix, and the prefix is what named the scenario anyway:\n`basic`, `non-modal`, `scroll-lock`, `two-managers`, `click-outside`,\n`controlled`, `dismiss-while-preparing`, `dom-ev`, `esc-gap`, `lookup`,\n`no-provider`, `over`, `preparing`, `reactive`, `reopen`, `under`, `variant`,\n`wait`. Checked against all 277 ids in the tree first: no trimmed name collides\nwith one that already exists.\n\n**Two are kept deliberately.** `my-dialog` is the placeholder in the JSDoc,\n`README` and `API.md` examples — it is written to read like a name a caller\nwould choose, and `my` is not one. `some-dialog` plays the same role in\n`registry.test-d.ts`. Neither is ever stamped into a test id, so neither carries\nthe redundancy the rest were trimmed for.\n\nVerified: check clean; 583 unit and 386 component tests pass; the playground\nbuilds and smoke is green.","tree":{"sha":"b3b2d8f4df5dbc01dfced8bdeddf00a45168aa5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/b3b2d8f4df5dbc01dfced8bdeddf00a45168aa5e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/cd7b114c1aa82abefa10eb6968513ed60b8c247d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/cd7b114c1aa82abefa10eb6968513ed60b8c247d","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKGNkN2IxMTRjMWFhODJhYmVmYTEwZWI2OTY4NTEzZWQ2MGI4YzI0N2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/8feb2f0d1e55a54cba7ac87eab76911fc288c149","sha":"8feb2f0d1e55a54cba7ac87eab76911fc288c149","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/8feb2f0d1e55a54cba7ac87eab76911fc288c149"}],"sha":"cd7b114c1aa82abefa10eb6968513ed60b8c247d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/cd7b114c1aa82abefa10eb6968513ed60b8c247d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/8feb2f0d1e55a54cba7ac87eab76911fc288c149/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T23:00:12Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T23:00:12Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"refactor: five constants the word boundary protected, and one inverted name\n\n`_` counts as a word character, so the token rule that renamed `MODAL_ID`\nrefused to match it inside `FAILURE_MODAL_ID` — correctly, by its own contract,\nand wrongly for the job. Five constants came through the whole sweep untouched,\ntwo of them in the library:\n\n  DEFAULT_MODAL_ANIMATION -> DEFAULT_DIALOG_ANIMATION   (utils/animation-utils)\n  BUILDS_A_MODAL          -> BUILDS_A_DIALOG            (harness-isolation)\n  CONFIRM_MODAL_ID / FAILURE_MODAL_ID / SSR_MODAL_ID -> *_DIALOG_ID\n\nNothing failed over them: a constant is only ever compared to itself, so the old\nname was internally consistent and every gate stayed green. Found by reading\nwhat was left rather than by running anything.\n\n`dialogFailure` is `failureDialog`. The rename map turned `failureModal` into a\nname with its words the wrong way round — it is the failure dialog, not the\ndialog''s failure — and it was the only inversion the map produced; the other\ntwenty read `<what>Dialog` as they did before.\n\nAnd two story descriptions said \"Dialog\" in prose where it meant the node the\nhook returns, one sentence after using *dialog* as the ordinary noun. Backticked\nand named as the return value.\n\nVerified: check clean; 583 unit and 386 component tests pass; the playground\nbuilds and smoke is green.","tree":{"sha":"6e4ef5decb74476ea99f5574f4a815157877b923","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/6e4ef5decb74476ea99f5574f4a815157877b923"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/8feb2f0d1e55a54cba7ac87eab76911fc288c149","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/8feb2f0d1e55a54cba7ac87eab76911fc288c149","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKDhmZWIyZjBkMWU1NWE1NGNiYTdhYzg3ZWFiNzY5MTFmYzI4OGMxNDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/580550ac93e7f921846228ac946786470beddc39","sha":"580550ac93e7f921846228ac946786470beddc39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/580550ac93e7f921846228ac946786470beddc39"}],"sha":"8feb2f0d1e55a54cba7ac87eab76911fc288c149","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/8feb2f0d1e55a54cba7ac87eab76911fc288c149"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/580550ac93e7f921846228ac946786470beddc39/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T20:50:27Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T20:50:27Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"refactor: the last of it — dead anchors, example names and the README''s own record\n\nThe residue a token sweep leaves, found by inventorying every remaining\n`modal` and judging each one rather than trusting that the earlier passes had\nbeen exhaustive.\n\n**Three markdown anchors were dead links.** `#modalregistry`,\n`#usemodal-base-primitive` and `#declaring-your-modals-in-one-place` point at\nheadings that were renamed in phases 1–3, so the in-page navigation had been\nbroken since. Nothing tests these, which is why they survived seven commits: an\nanchor that resolves to nothing scrolls nowhere and reports nothing. All\nin-page links in the six documents now resolve.\n\nThe user-land example names in `API.md` (`useConfirmModal`, `ModalOverlay`, the\n`modal_hidden` analytics call), the playground''s `modalLayout` class and\n`reactiveModal`, Solid''s `setModals` beside its own `dialogs`, and the\n`wcag-audit` skill''s `modalTag` — none load-bearing, all reading as the old\nword in documents whose job is to be read.\n\n**The README''s naming-policy passage is updated rather than swept**, because it\nis a record of past renames and the sweep had turned it into a hybrid that never\nexisted: `DialogInfo.modalType` names a field on a type that was called\n`ModalInfo` at the time. It says `ModalInfo.modalType` again, and this rename\njoins the list as the fourth — the one that took the hook itself, on the grounds\nthe rest of the sweep rests on: the library drives a `<dialog>`, and *modal* is\none of that element''s two variants, so `useModal` was named after half of what\nit does.\n\nVerified end to end: check clean; 583 unit and 386 component tests on a cold\ncache; `yarn build` + `verify:package` green (extensions, entry isolation both\nways, the React binding compiled and the Solid one not, the SSR path); the\nplayground builds and smoke passes in both themes.","tree":{"sha":"522ba215bac20acf73afc84c4aa5207e486c8ca2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/522ba215bac20acf73afc84c4aa5207e486c8ca2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/580550ac93e7f921846228ac946786470beddc39","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/580550ac93e7f921846228ac946786470beddc39","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKDU4MDU1MGFjOTNlN2Y5MjE4NDYyMjhhYzk0Njc4NjQ3MGJlZGRjMzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/c5f4fe008350aec310f2bc46b22ed4c0c4986e52","sha":"c5f4fe008350aec310f2bc46b22ed4c0c4986e52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/c5f4fe008350aec310f2bc46b22ed4c0c4986e52"}],"sha":"580550ac93e7f921846228ac946786470beddc39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/580550ac93e7f921846228ac946786470beddc39"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/c5f4fe008350aec310f2bc46b22ed4c0c4986e52/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T20:43:26Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T20:43:26Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"refactor: the prose says dialog, and the adjective survives\n\nThe last layer, and the one no map could do: 1,443 occurrences of the bare word\nin comments, JSDoc, test titles and the four `CLAUDE.md` files, where the same\nsix letters are a noun in `''closes an open modal''` and an adjective in\n`''a modal dialog whose Escape is a request''`. The noun moved; 106 adjective\nuses stayed.\n\n`src/CLAUDE.md`''s vocabulary section is rewritten rather than swept, because it\nis the passage that *states* the rule and the rule is what changed. It used to\nsay \"`dialog` is the element, `modal` is the unit of state\" — a distinction this\nrefactor removes — and it now says the element and the record are one concept,\nwith a note on the three places the adjective hides.\n\n**Three defects, all of them a pattern eating the adjective**, and the reason\nthis pass audited against the pre-sweep tree rather than `HEAD` — `HEAD` already\ncontained phases 1–5, so a defect introduced there read as original text:\n\n- **`aria-modal` had become `aria-dialog`**, seven sites, from phase 5c''s\n  trailing `-modal` rule whose guard covered `non` and nothing else. The\n  attribute does not exist under that name.\n- **The CSS `:modal` pseudo-class had become `:dialog`** in eleven places. Five\n  were Playwright selectors and **two of those were passing vacuously**:\n  `expect(locator(''dialog:modal'')).toHaveCount(0)` holds just as well for a\n  selector matching nothing, so the assertion outlived its meaning. The other\n  three failed, which is how it surfaced.\n- **The logger''s prefix collided with a namespace.** `dialog:` is the storage\n  prefix, so `''dialog:modal''` was the long spelling of `''modal''`, and stripping\n  it unconditionally was safe while no namespace began with it. Three now do, so\n  `setLogLevel(''dialog:lifecycle'')` was read as `''lifecycle''` and matched\n  nothing. `candidates()` tries both spellings; two tests pin it, including that\n  a sub-namespace still does not enable its siblings.\n\nAlso restored: `modal only` on the body scroll lock (it is the modal variant''s\nalone — a non-modal dialog leaves the body scrollable), `modal branch` on the\nvariant narrowing, and the platform''s *modal state* in the passage about\nHTML-AAM.\n\n`CHANGELOG.md` gets the sweep''s one entry and none of its edits. Its own header\nsays entries are left as written, and renaming a symbol inside a 2026-05 entry\nwould make it name something that did not exist for another three months.\n\nVerified: check clean; 583 unit (two new) and 386 component tests pass on a cold\ncache; the playground builds and smoke is green in both themes.","tree":{"sha":"4643a117a7f730b3d4cbe7b64a8ee110387d37c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/4643a117a7f730b3d4cbe7b64a8ee110387d37c3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/c5f4fe008350aec310f2bc46b22ed4c0c4986e52","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/c5f4fe008350aec310f2bc46b22ed4c0c4986e52","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKGM1ZjRmZTAwODM1MGFlYzMxMGYyYmM0NmIyMmVkNGMwYzQ5ODZlNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/7fb3e85ec8792a98cbbc221b35747bdc7b4b207a","sha":"7fb3e85ec8792a98cbbc221b35747bdc7b4b207a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/7fb3e85ec8792a98cbbc221b35747bdc7b4b207a"}],"sha":"c5f4fe008350aec310f2bc46b22ed4c0c4986e52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/c5f4fe008350aec310f2bc46b22ed4c0c4986e52"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/7fb3e85ec8792a98cbbc221b35747bdc7b4b207a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T20:22:49Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T20:22:49Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"refactor(playground)!: the playground says dialog — directories, routes and tokens\n\nThe playground is the library''s worked example, so a name it keeps is a name the\nlibrary still teaches.\n\n  entities/modal-template/  -> entities/dialog-template/\n  pages/modal-actions/      -> pages/dialog-actions/   (and the route with it)\n  widgets/code-viewer''s CodeModal / useCodeModal -> CodeDialog / useCodeDialog\n\n**A second playground route changes**: `/modal-actions` is now `/dialog-actions`,\nafter `/slide-modal` -> `/slide-dialog` earlier in the sweep. Both were linked\nfrom the sidebar, which is where smoke discovers its routes, so nothing in the\nrepo points at the old spelling — but an outside link to either stops resolving.\nSay the word and they get redirects.\n\n**The CSS custom properties move too**: `--modal-bg`, `--modal-text`,\n`--modal-border`, `--modal-shadow`, `--modal-spacing*`, `--modal-radius` and\n`--modal-control-border` become `--dialog-*`. `design-system-layering.test.ts`\nnames the permitted families in its own failure message, so its allow-list moved\nwith them rather than being left to describe a family that no longer exists.\n\nAnd the ~150 dialog ids the stories open by — `basic-modal`, `my-modal`,\n`ghost-modal`, `stacked-modals`, `delete-item-modal`, `modal-variant` — with the\ngenerated `dialog-<id>` test ids that read them.\n\nThree patterns did the hyphenated work, each written around the adjective:\na leading `modal-` that refuses to start after a hyphen (so `non-modal-first` is\nuntouched), a trailing `-modal` with a `(?<!non)` guard, and `--modal-` for the\ncustom properties. `aria-modal` is the platform''s attribute and never moved.\n\nVerified: check clean; 581 unit and 386 component tests pass; the playground\nbuilds and smoke is green.","tree":{"sha":"93243e7131558385bca21cedb0ce9c25a0df1413","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/93243e7131558385bca21cedb0ce9c25a0df1413"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/7fb3e85ec8792a98cbbc221b35747bdc7b4b207a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/7fb3e85ec8792a98cbbc221b35747bdc7b4b207a","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKDdmYjNlODVlYzg3OTJhOThjYmJjMjIxYjM1NzQ3YmRjN2I0YjIwN2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/eb0b88ea7260f7f03757efe657bafeec1cb9ef5c","sha":"eb0b88ea7260f7f03757efe657bafeec1cb9ef5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/eb0b88ea7260f7f03757efe657bafeec1cb9ef5c"}],"sha":"7fb3e85ec8792a98cbbc221b35747bdc7b4b207a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/7fb3e85ec8792a98cbbc221b35747bdc7b4b207a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/eb0b88ea7260f7f03757efe657bafeec1cb9ef5c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T20:16:28Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T20:16:28Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"refactor(core)!: the node the hook returns is Dialog, not Modal\n\n`useDialog` handed back a field called `Modal` — the last place the public\nsurface still asked a caller to render something named for one of the two\nvariants:\n\n  const dialog = useDialog({ … });\n  return <>{dialog.Dialog}</>;   // was dialog.Modal\n\n`UseDialogReturn.Modal` -> `.Dialog`, with the 134 reads of it, the\n`const { Modal: X } = useDialog(…)` rename-destructures in the stories, and the\nprose that names the field.\n\n**The pattern for this one had to exclude the hyphen and the noun after it.**\n`Modal` alone is not safely renameable: `Non-Modal Dialogs` is a heading,\n`Modal dialogs (top layer) are unaffected` is a sentence about the variant, and\n`Modal vs non-modal, as a discriminated union` is the distinction itself. A\nboundary that treats `-` as a word character keeps the first; the guard on a\nfollowing `dialog`/`dialogs` was written for the second and did not hold, so\nthirteen sites were read back and restored by hand — the four `Modal dialog`\nlabels in the scroll-lock stories, `Modal variant only` on the runtime option,\nand the three `Modal vs non-modal` contrasts.\n\nThat is the whole argument for doing the bare word last and by hand: a map\ncannot tell a noun from an adjective, and here the same six letters are both.\n\nVerified: check clean; 581 unit and 386 component tests pass; the playground\nbuilds and smoke is green.","tree":{"sha":"cff937b572d3e8fecb908922f4c43e48109a8add","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/cff937b572d3e8fecb908922f4c43e48109a8add"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/eb0b88ea7260f7f03757efe657bafeec1cb9ef5c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/eb0b88ea7260f7f03757efe657bafeec1cb9ef5c","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKGViMGI4OGVhNzI2MGY3ZjAzNzU3ZWZlNjU3YmFmZWVjMWNiOWVmNWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/88bbb0163ba6065ae34176060c403ca59b209c21","sha":"88bbb0163ba6065ae34176060c403ca59b209c21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/88bbb0163ba6065ae34176060c403ca59b209c21"}],"sha":"eb0b88ea7260f7f03757efe657bafeec1cb9ef5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/eb0b88ea7260f7f03757efe657bafeec1cb9ef5c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/88bbb0163ba6065ae34176060c403ca59b209c21/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T20:09:27Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T20:09:27Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"refactor(core): the internals say dialog\n\nNothing exported changes here — this is the layer underneath, renamed so a\nreader following a call down from `useDialog` does not cross back into the old\nword halfway:\n\n  createModalStore / ModalStore        -> createDialogStore / DialogStore\n  createModalRuntime / ModalRuntime    -> createDialogRuntime / DialogRuntime\n  createModalDirector / ModalDirector  -> createDialogDirector / DialogDirector\n  ModalDomContext / ModalLifecyclePass -> Dialog*\n  resolveModalOptions / buildModalOptions -> resolveDialogOptions / build*\n  finalizeModalClose / teardownModal   -> finalizeDialogClose / teardownDialog\n\nwith the files under them: `modal-store.ts`, `modal-runtime.ts`,\n`modal-director.ts` and `solid-modal.*` become `dialog-*`.\n\nThe test harnesses too, since they are how the behaviour is named when it is\nbeing asserted: `ModalVariantHarness`, `StackedModalsHarness`,\n`FocusUnderAnotherModalHarness`, `MultiModalHarness` and the rest, plus the\n`Modal1` / `ModalA` stand-ins the stacking stories open in sequence.\n\nUntouched on purpose, here and everywhere else: `nonModal`, `isNonModal`, every\n`NonModal*Harness`, `showModal` and `modality`. Those are the adjective, and the\nsecond is the platform''s own method name.\n\nWhat is *not* done yet is the bare word in prose — comments, and the test titles\nthat read `''closes an open modal''`. That needs judgement rather than a map,\nbecause `''a modal dialog whose Escape is a request''` and `''the modal branch''`\nare correct English about the variant and must survive. It is the last commit of\nthe sweep.\n\nVerified: check clean; 581 unit and 386 component tests pass; the playground\nbuilds and smoke is green.","tree":{"sha":"4ead31381fb5575e90b7436a5fa1f089750ce660","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/4ead31381fb5575e90b7436a5fa1f089750ce660"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/88bbb0163ba6065ae34176060c403ca59b209c21","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/88bbb0163ba6065ae34176060c403ca59b209c21","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKDg4YmJiMDE2M2JhNjA2NWFlMzQxNzYwNjBjNDAzY2E1OWIyMDljMjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/3683c31db60e8bc9316d3550c7da4d70f5bcd020","sha":"3683c31db60e8bc9316d3550c7da4d70f5bcd020","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/3683c31db60e8bc9316d3550c7da4d70f5bcd020"}],"sha":"88bbb0163ba6065ae34176060c403ca59b209c21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/88bbb0163ba6065ae34176060c403ca59b209c21"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/3683c31db60e8bc9316d3550c7da4d70f5bcd020/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T20:02:45Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T20:02:45Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"refactor(core)!: the DOM events say dialog\n\nThe two events the manager dispatches on `document`, and the constants that name\nthem:\n\n  MODAL_OPEN_EVENT  = ''modal:open''  -> DIALOG_OPEN_EVENT  = ''dialog:open''\n  MODAL_CLOSE_EVENT = ''modal:close'' -> DIALOG_CLOSE_EVENT = ''dialog:close''\n\nThe event *strings* change, not just the constants, so a listener registered by\nhand — `document.addEventListener(''modal:open'', …)`, which is what an analytics\nhook or a microfrontend outside the import graph does — stops firing. That is\nthe one part of this sweep a type-check cannot catch for a consumer, which is\nwhy it is its own commit. The `DocumentEventMap` augmentation moves with them,\nso anyone using the constant keeps their typed detail for free.\n\nVerified: check clean; 581 unit and 386 component tests pass; the playground\nbuilds and smoke is green.","tree":{"sha":"835e3633e651cf533f6f2e3397fdbcf2b698d1b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/835e3633e651cf533f6f2e3397fdbcf2b698d1b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/3683c31db60e8bc9316d3550c7da4d70f5bcd020","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/3683c31db60e8bc9316d3550c7da4d70f5bcd020","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKDM2ODNjMzFkYjYwZThiYzkzMTZkMzU1MGM3ZGE0ZDcwZjViY2QwMjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/b116725258403e53066facad4559f86d9a793b4a","sha":"b116725258403e53066facad4559f86d9a793b4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/b116725258403e53066facad4559f86d9a793b4a"}],"sha":"3683c31db60e8bc9316d3550c7da4d70f5bcd020","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/3683c31db60e8bc9316d3550c7da4d70f5bcd020"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/b116725258403e53066facad4559f86d9a793b4a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T19:58:20Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T19:58:20Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"refactor(core)!: Dialog across the type surface, and the DOM contract with it\n\nThe exported vocabulary, under the same rule — dialog is the noun, modal is the\nadjective:\n\n  ModalPhase / ModalVariant / ModalAnimation  -> Dialog*\n  ModalHandle / ModalRenderArgs / ModalInfo   -> Dialog*\n  ModalId / RegisteredModalId / ModalRegistry -> Dialog*\n  ModalContract / ModalLookup / ModalSnapshot -> Dialog*\n  ModalFailure / ModalErrorSource             -> Dialog*\n  ModalOpenEventDetail / ModalCloseEventDetail-> Dialog*\n  ModalOutlet (+ its context)                 -> DialogOutlet\n  StackModal                                  -> StackDialog\n\n**The DOM contract moved in the same commit, and not by choice.** Renaming the\n`modalId` parameter caught `element.dataset[''modalId'']`, which is not an\nidentifier at all — it is the other spelling of the attribute `data-modal-id`,\nand the two are one contract that the DOM keeps in two casings. Nine component\ntests went red saying so. Splitting them across two commits was the mistake; the\nattributes come along:\n\n  data-modal-id  -> data-dialog-id      (a documented styling hook)\n  data-modal-z   -> data-dialog-z\n  data-modal-type / data-modal-container -> data-dialog-*\n\nAnything selecting on `dialog[data-modal-id=\"…\"]` in a stylesheet needs the new\nspelling; the CHANGELOG entry at the end of the sweep will say so in one place.\n\n**The generated test id moved too**, for the same reason and found the same way:\n`dialogAttributes` stamps `data-testid=\"modal-${id}\"`, so every test asking for\n`modal-<id>` was reading a prefix the rename had not reached. It is `dialog-`\nnow — 146 literals across the suites, plus the five selector strings that build\nit by hand inside a template literal or a `querySelector`, which no pattern over\n`getByTestId(` would have found.\n\nVerified: check clean; 581 unit and 386 component tests pass (chromium, firefox,\nwebkit); the playground builds and smoke is green.","tree":{"sha":"571b300af031b7a6020a578602800cce9541b3eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/571b300af031b7a6020a578602800cce9541b3eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/b116725258403e53066facad4559f86d9a793b4a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/b116725258403e53066facad4559f86d9a793b4a","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKGIxMTY3MjUyNTg0MDNlNTMwNjZmYWNhZDQ1NTlmODZkOWE3OTNiNGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/b1a00a37a7f86f31a20d7bde48c01cafe5469504","sha":"b1a00a37a7f86f31a20d7bde48c01cafe5469504","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/b1a00a37a7f86f31a20d7bde48c01cafe5469504"}],"sha":"b116725258403e53066facad4559f86d9a793b4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/b116725258403e53066facad4559f86d9a793b4a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/b1a00a37a7f86f31a20d7bde48c01cafe5469504/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T19:43:59Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T19:43:59Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"refactor(core)!: the template hooks are dialogs, and so are the template families\n\nSame rule as the primitive: dialog is the noun, modal is the adjective. A\ntemplate hook that opens a non-modal panel whenever `nonModal: true` is passed —\nand both of these do, because `TemplateCommonOptions` ends in `& ModalVariant` —\nwas named for one of its two variants.\n\n  useMessageModal            -> useMessageDialog\n  useSlideModal              -> useSlideDialog\n  UseMessageModalOptions     -> UseMessageDialogOptions\n  UseMessageModalReturn      -> UseMessageDialogReturn\n  MessageModalRenderContext  -> MessageDialogRenderContext\n  MessageModalType           -> MessageDialogType\n  UseSlideModalOptions       -> UseSlideDialogOptions\n  UseSlideModalReturn        -> UseSlideDialogReturn\n  SlideModalRenderContext    -> SlideDialogRenderContext\n\nThe playground''s four vanilla template families move with them, because their\nnames mirror the hooks'' and splitting the two would have left\n`Templates.MessageModal` sitting beside `useMessageDialog` in one file for the\nlength of a commit: `MessageModal`, `SlideModal`, `PanelModal` and `FormModal`\nbecome `MessageDialog`, `SlideDialog`, `PanelDialog` and `FormDialog`, with\ntheir directories under `entities/modal-template/ui/vanilla/`.\n\n**One playground route changes**: `/slide-modal` is now `/slide-dialog`. It is a\nURL, so an existing link to it stops resolving — say the word and it gets a\nredirect, but nothing in the repo points at the old spelling.\n\n`useMessageDialog` keeps taking `nonModal`, which is the argument against\nsplitting each template into a modal-named hook and a bare one. The variant is\nalready a discriminated union, and it discriminates finer than a pair of names\ncould: the modal branch offers `dismissOnBackdropClick` and\n`role: ''alertdialog''`, the non-modal branch replaces the first with\n`dismissOnClickOutside` and refuses the second, because an alertdialog is modal\nby definition and the APG requires `aria-modal`. Two hooks would each have to\nre-encode that, or lose it. Modality stays one option, in one place, and it now\nsits under a hook whose name does not contradict it.\n\nVerified: check clean (types, registry, lint, format, typedoc, doc examples);\n581 unit and 386 component tests pass; the playground builds and smoke is green\nin both themes — run against a freshly built preview, because the long-running\ndev server on :3000 answers `/api` with a 500 from a typedoc model it cached\nbefore the files moved. Command-line typedoc passes on the same tree; the dev\nserver needs a restart, nothing else does.","tree":{"sha":"d499d149c318a30823c085c4b131960d24f5d2d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/d499d149c318a30823c085c4b131960d24f5d2d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/b1a00a37a7f86f31a20d7bde48c01cafe5469504","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/b1a00a37a7f86f31a20d7bde48c01cafe5469504","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKGIxYTAwYTM3YTdmODZmMzFhMjBkN2JkZTQ4YzAxY2FmZTU0Njk1MDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/304cf06a977f7c4942a8c60c17b7b52d35c28aeb","sha":"304cf06a977f7c4942a8c60c17b7b52d35c28aeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/304cf06a977f7c4942a8c60c17b7b52d35c28aeb"}],"sha":"b1a00a37a7f86f31a20d7bde48c01cafe5469504","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/b1a00a37a7f86f31a20d7bde48c01cafe5469504"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/304cf06a977f7c4942a8c60c17b7b52d35c28aeb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T19:32:32Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T19:32:32Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"refactor(core)!: the primitive hook is useDialog\n\nThe library drives one thing: a native `<dialog>`. Every rendering path ends\nthere — `bindDialog` takes an `HTMLDialogElement` by type, the React binding\nrenders the element, Solid calls `document.createElement(''dialog'')` — and the\nlifecycle is the element''s own `show()` / `showModal()` / `close()`. A hook\nnamed `useModal` that returns a non-modal dialog whenever `nonModal: true` is\npassed was naming the wrong thing, and naming it wrongly.\n\nThe rule this sweep applies, so the rest of it needs no case-by-case argument:\n\n  **dialog is the noun — the element. modal is the adjective — one of its two\n  variants.**\n\nThat is why `nonModal` and `showModal()` are untouched here and stay untouched:\nthey are the adjective, and the second is the platform''s own word.\n\nThis pass takes the primitive and its type surface:\n\n  useModal            -> useDialog\n  UseModalOptions     -> UseDialogOptions\n  UseModalBaseOptions -> UseDialogBaseOptions\n  UseModalReturn      -> UseDialogReturn\n  useModalActions     -> useDialogActions\n\nwith the files and story directories under them (`use-modal.tsx` ->\n`use-dialog.tsx`, `__tests__/use-modal/` -> `__tests__/use-dialog/`,\n`use-modal-actions/` -> `use-dialog-actions/`), applied token-exact rather than\nby substring so `nonModal`, `isNonModal`, `NonModal*` and `showModal` come\nthrough unchanged.\n\n`fuzzy-match.test.ts` needed reading rather than replacing. Its fixtures query\nthe literal `''useModal''`, so the queries were spelled from the word *modal* and\nthe expected ranges were indices into an eight-letter name. Two of them had\ngone vacuous rather than red — `fuzzyMatch(''m'', ''useDialog'')` scores nothing,\nbecause `useDialog` has no `m`, so a test comparing a boundary hit to a mid-word\nhit was comparing zero to zero. Requeried against the new name, and the boundary\nhalf moved to `createDialogManager`, which holds the letter on a camelCase\nboundary and survives the later phases.\n\n`CHANGELOG.md` is deliberately excluded from the sweep. It is the migration\nguide, kept by date, and an entry describes what was true when it was written —\nrenaming a symbol inside a past entry makes it name something that did not exist\nat that date. The new entry lands at the end of the sweep.\n\nVerified: type-check, type-check:registry, lint, format, typedoc and the doc\nexamples all clean; 581 unit and 386 component tests (chromium, firefox, webkit,\ncold cache) pass; the playground builds and the smoke run is green.","tree":{"sha":"59d7120076808b2d0134914939d8550f0d0eee1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/59d7120076808b2d0134914939d8550f0d0eee1d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/304cf06a977f7c4942a8c60c17b7b52d35c28aeb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/304cf06a977f7c4942a8c60c17b7b52d35c28aeb","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKDMwNGNmMDZhOTc3ZjdjNDk0MmE4YzYwYzE3YjdiNTJkMzVjMjhhZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/278f14f6ded51468c28e4ce8230221a2417d2a93","sha":"278f14f6ded51468c28e4ce8230221a2417d2a93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/278f14f6ded51468c28e4ce8230221a2417d2a93"}],"sha":"304cf06a977f7c4942a8c60c17b7b52d35c28aeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/304cf06a977f7c4942a8c60c17b7b52d35c28aeb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/278f14f6ded51468c28e4ce8230221a2417d2a93/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T18:58:57Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T18:58:57Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"chore(deps): update @types/react-dom and @tanstack/react-router versions","tree":{"sha":"8ac2ba44122805af634eb9555559721c461bff79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/8ac2ba44122805af634eb9555559721c461bff79"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/278f14f6ded51468c28e4ce8230221a2417d2a93","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/278f14f6ded51468c28e4ce8230221a2417d2a93","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKDI3OGYxNGY2ZGVkNTE0NjhjMjhlNGNlODIzMDIyMWEyNDE3ZDJhOTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/0ed058b3591f8e9b28f207a27729e3d80bdf33f2","sha":"0ed058b3591f8e9b28f207a27729e3d80bdf33f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/0ed058b3591f8e9b28f207a27729e3d80bdf33f2"}],"sha":"278f14f6ded51468c28e4ce8230221a2417d2a93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/278f14f6ded51468c28e4ce8230221a2417d2a93"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/0ed058b3591f8e9b28f207a27729e3d80bdf33f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T11:56:09Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T11:56:09Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"docs(playground): the documents catch up with the deleted MUI layer\n\nThree files claimed something that stopped being true when `ui/mui/` went,\nand one of them said it twice.\n\n`playground/CLAUDE.md` described the templates as two flavours spelling the\nsame component names \"so that example ports by changing one import\". There is\nno second flavour to port to. The Templates section now says what the split\nactually is: the catalogue is markup to lift into a project, the two\n/ui-integrations cards write theirs out by hand, and an example may still\nimport a template — three do — but it is no longer the default. The intro,\nthe FSD exemption''s example path, the architecture tree, both route-table\nrows and the two \"Managing Template Components\" steps follow from that.\n\n`src/CLAUDE.md` named `MuiButton` as the `data-loading` seam. It points at\n`ui-integrations/examples/mui-form.tsx` now, where the mapping is one visible\nline rather than a wrapper.\n\nAnd one fix the documents themselves forced. The example first destructured\n`data-loading` out of the action props to feed MUI''s `loading`, which maps\nthe flag and **removes the attribute from the DOM** — but `data-loading` is\nthe documented styling contract (`button[data-loading=''true''] { … }`) and the\nonly form the library ships the state in. A browser check of both cards\ncaught it: the vanilla button carried the attribute mid-submit and the MUI\none carried nothing. The props are spread whole now and `loading` is derived\nbeside them, which is also the better lesson — the attribute is the source,\nthe prop is the derivation.\n\nVerified against a served build: both dialogs open with their computed name,\nan invalid submit is refused with its message, the running state reaches the\nDOM on both, the payload comes back through `onClose`, /ui-templates offers\nVanilla and Shared only, and no console errors.","tree":{"sha":"96c6baa20eb7154238f8d9f841d74c7ff548d56b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/96c6baa20eb7154238f8d9f841d74c7ff548d56b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/0ed058b3591f8e9b28f207a27729e3d80bdf33f2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/0ed058b3591f8e9b28f207a27729e3d80bdf33f2","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKDBlZDA1OGIzNTkxZjhlOWIyOGYyMDdhMjc3MjllM2Q4MGJkZjMzZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/d2e3cd39fd6e5f3f66eadb2e5c90d02eaf147e96","sha":"d2e3cd39fd6e5f3f66eadb2e5c90d02eaf147e96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/d2e3cd39fd6e5f3f66eadb2e5c90d02eaf147e96"}],"sha":"0ed058b3591f8e9b28f207a27729e3d80bdf33f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/0ed058b3591f8e9b28f207a27729e3d80bdf33f2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/d2e3cd39fd6e5f3f66eadb2e5c90d02eaf147e96/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T11:48:17Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T11:48:17Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"refactor(playground): the vanilla form example is plain elements over the template stylesheet\n\nThe MUI card''s counterpart, and the same reasoning: the page''s subject is\nthe diff between the two files, and both were spending it on this repo''s own\ncomponents instead of on the library.\n\nIt is `<div>`, `<label>` and `<input>` carrying the form-modal CSS module''s\nclasses now. The input keeps the spread rather than named props — enumerating\n`id`/`type`/`value`/`onChange` is how a wrapper drops `onBlur`, `name`,\n`aria-invalid` and `aria-describedby`, losing blur-time validation and the\nerror association with nothing failing — and the error element keeps the id\n`field()` pointed `aria-describedby` at.\n\nTwo of the eight components turned out not to be wrappers, and both are kept\nas imports rather than copied out:\n\n`Content` calls `useScrollRegion`. A scroller with no focusable child is\nkeyboard-unreachable (WCAG 2.1.1); Chromium and Firefox add the Tab stop and\nWebKit does not, so it is declared, and only while the content actually\noverflows — which takes a measurement. Inlining it would have meant either\ndropping the accessibility or hand-rolling an overflow observer in an example\nabout dialogs. It is called in the component body, since the `render`\ncallback runs inside another render pass and is no place for a hook.\n\n`Footer` wraps `ButtonRow`, which carries its own stylesheet and owns the\ngap for every vanilla family — the comment there records that one rule copied\nthree ways became three different gaps and a footer with no `display: flex`\nat all. So the footer is two classes, and the outer one is not decoration.\n\nThe vanilla templates stay on disk: three other examples use them, and the\n/ui-templates catalogue still shows them.","tree":{"sha":"c83ef564de1dc7ac6fc7bf8b006d0d1c3bc240df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/c83ef564de1dc7ac6fc7bf8b006d0d1c3bc240df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/d2e3cd39fd6e5f3f66eadb2e5c90d02eaf147e96","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/d2e3cd39fd6e5f3f66eadb2e5c90d02eaf147e96","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKGQyZTNjZDM5ZmQ2ZTVmM2Y2NmVhZGIyZTVjOTBkMDJlYWYxNDdlOTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/5b3f92c5d70fe8d79df99064276fd81b342d16a6","sha":"5b3f92c5d70fe8d79df99064276fd81b342d16a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/5b3f92c5d70fe8d79df99064276fd81b342d16a6"}],"sha":"d2e3cd39fd6e5f3f66eadb2e5c90d02eaf147e96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/d2e3cd39fd6e5f3f66eadb2e5c90d02eaf147e96"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/5b3f92c5d70fe8d79df99064276fd81b342d16a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T11:45:27Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T11:45:27Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"refactor(playground)!: the MUI form example is written against MUI, not against a template layer\n\nThe card on /ui-integrations was built from `entities/modal-template/ui/mui`,\nso a reader met the playground''s own components before meeting the library.\nThe interesting line in that file is where the library''s DOM contract touches\na component kit''s props, and an indirection sat exactly on top of it.\n\nIt is raw `Box` / `Stack` / `Typography` / `Alert` / `Button` now, and the\nseam is one destructure:\n\n    const { ''data-loading'': isSubmitting, ...submitProps } = action(''submit'', …)\n    <Button loading={isSubmitting} {...submitProps}>\n\nwhich is the whole of what a wrapper was doing. MUI 9 takes `loading`\nnatively, and it disables the button itself, so the wrapper''s second\n`disabled` was belt-and-braces. The comment records what the destructure\ncosts elsewhere: `action()` re-runs every React render, so the rest spread\ncaptures this pass — under Solid the same line would freeze getters that are\ngetters precisely for a fine-grained renderer.\n\nThe MUI half of the template layer served that one example, so it goes with\nit: `ui/mui/` deleted, its ten `?raw` entries dropped from the code viewer,\nand the Material UI tab removed from /ui-templates.\n\nFour pieces of prose said something that stops being true, and they are the\npart worth reading twice — the vanilla blurb and the page description both\nclaimed the two flavours spell the same names \"so examples port across by\nchanging one import\", the Shared blurb counted three tabs, and a code comment\nexplained a branch that no longer exists. The catalogue is now described as\nwhat it is: reference UI to copy, while the examples write their markup out\nby hand.","tree":{"sha":"47392b94991ff709aa7722a149ee363fe5462427","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/47392b94991ff709aa7722a149ee363fe5462427"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/5b3f92c5d70fe8d79df99064276fd81b342d16a6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/5b3f92c5d70fe8d79df99064276fd81b342d16a6","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKDViM2Y5MmM1ZDcwZmU4ZDc5ZGY5OTA2NDI3NmZkODFiMzQyZDE2YTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/c6cac4c96ca96bda46147ca431ac9f9ff296ba51","sha":"c6cac4c96ca96bda46147ca431ac9f9ff296ba51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/c6cac4c96ca96bda46147ca431ac9f9ff296ba51"}],"sha":"5b3f92c5d70fe8d79df99064276fd81b342d16a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/5b3f92c5d70fe8d79df99064276fd81b342d16a6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/c6cac4c96ca96bda46147ca431ac9f9ff296ba51/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T11:21:22Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T11:32:38Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"feat(core)!: a modal''s contract, and the matrix worklist taken to zero (#4)\n\n* fix(core): route every dismissal through onDismissRequest, not only the key\n\nA controlled surface — one whose `open` is a prop — cannot let its dialog\nclose itself: the boolean upstream is still true and the next render puts it\nback. `onDismissRequest` exists for exactly that, and it covered one of the\nthree doors. `attachClickOutside` and each binding''s backdrop handler called\n`store.close(DISMISS_REASON)` themselves, so a controlled modal answered\nEscape correctly and reopened itself on a backdrop click — and a modal that\ndraws no actions defaults to `dismissOnBackdropClick: true`, which is the\narrangement most likely to meet it.\n\nThe gap was structural. `canDismiss` is the one predicate every dismissal\npath shares, but the *last step* it replaces had no such home: it lived as a\nprivate `answerDismissKey` in `attach-keydown.ts`, reachable only by the\nthree listeners in that file. It is `answerDismiss` in `utils/dismiss-gate.ts`\nnow, beside the predicate, and all five paths end there — so a fourth binding\ngets the behaviour by calling it rather than by remembering to.\n\nThe handler is told which door through the new `DismissCause` root export\n(''dismiss-key'' | ''backdrop-click'' | ''click-outside''), since one owner\nanswering three of them could otherwise only guess. Additive: a handler that\nignores the argument behaves exactly as before. The return value still only\nmeans something on the dismiss key, whose non-modal listener captures — a\npointer path prevents nothing, so a declined click is a dialog left open.\n\nEvery gate above the last step is untouched: which key, an action claiming\nit, a popup answering first, where the pointer landed, `prepare`, a running\naction, which dialog is in front.\n\nProven on all three bindings — the two pointer doors as component tests, the\nseam itself as unit tests. The matrix row now depends on all three dismissal\noptions instead of `dismissKey` alone.\n\n* feat(core): a modal''s contract declares the payload it opens with\n\n`requestOpenAndWait<TId extends RegisteredModalId>` narrowed its result off\nthe id and left the request it took at `unknown` — one call, one declared id,\ntyped on the return and untyped on the argument. The reason on\n`OpenRequest.payload` was that the registry is keyed by string and cannot\ncheck a payload against a modal''s contract; that was true when it was written\nand stopped being true when `ModalRegistry` landed, since the overload beside\nit already proves the id is known at the type level.\n\nA contract may now declare a third thing, and `PayloadOf<TId>` reads it the\nway `DataOf` and `ReasonOf` read theirs. `data` is what a modal closes with,\n`payload` is what it opens with — the distinction `OpenRequest` already drew\nin prose, now in the contract. The fallbacks differ for that reason: `DataOf`\nanswers `void` for an undeclared modal, `PayloadOf` answers `unknown`, since\n`void` would be a claim about a stranger''s message.\n\n`requestOpen` is one generic signature rather than an overload pair — the\nshape `close` uses, for the reason recorded there: a failing first overload\nfalls through to the permissive one, so the check would evaporate exactly\nwhen it is wrong. `requestOpenAndWait` needs its pair for the return, so both\nhalves constrain the payload identically and neither rescues what the other\nrejected; the fixture asserts that, because it is the one way this could have\nbeen decorative.\n\n`onOpenRequest` still hands its handler `unknown`, deliberately and not by\nomission: `PayloadOf` types the asking side, where both call sites belong to\nthe project, and the receiving side is where a message from outside arrives —\na parameter annotated with a declaration nobody checked at run time would\nread as a guarantee never made. The declaration is now the type to parse to.\n\nNothing changes for a project that declares no payloads.\n\n* feat(manager): register/unregister events, and an open that says whether it landed\n\nA modal joins the registry when its component mounts, so an imperative\n`dialogManager.open(id)` from a service, a router guard or a deep link can\narrive before the dialog behind a code-split route exists. That is the\nordinary case rather than a typo, and it did nothing quietly: a `log.warn`,\nand warnings are silent until `setLogLevel`. Every other door already\nanswered — `openAndWait` resolves `[Error, null]`, `requestOpenAndWait`\nrefuses with `not-registered` — this one did not.\n\n`open` returns whether a dialog was there to open, and `subscribe` carries\nthe two registry moments beside the two screen ones. `ModalLookup.exists`\nanswered \"now\" and nothing answered \"tell me when\", which is what made an\nopen-when-it-arrives impossible to write without polling.\n\nBoth emissions are ordered against the facts they report. `register` fires\nafter the entry is in the map, so the dialog is openable by the time a\nlistener hears it — a listener told a moment early would find nothing to\nopen, which is the whole value of the event. `unregister` fires after the\n`close` an unmount-while-open also emits: the dialog leaves the screen and\nthen leaves the registry. There is no DOM twin of the pair; `modal:open` and\n`modal:close` exist so another bundle can hear a dialog on screen, and a\nregistry belongs to one manager.\n\nNo pending-open queue is shipped, and that is a decision rather than a\nsmaller first step: a held open needs an expiry, and how long a deep link\nshould wait for a route is the application''s question — the same reason\nnothing here auto-dismisses. A test writes the ten-line version, because a\nclaim that something can be built in user-land is worth one demonstration\nthat it can.\n\n* feat(core): portal can name its host, not only document.body\n\n`portal: true` was `createPortal(node, document.body)`, hardcoded — and the\nbody is the right answer only for a page whose styling is global. A dialog\nportaled out of a themed container, a design-system root or a\nmicrofrontend''s mount point loses whatever that ancestor provided: custom\nproperties, a scoping class, a cascade layer. Silently, since the dialog\nstill renders and only looks wrong. Everything else here is careful with\nroots — the stylesheet is adopted per `getRootNode()`, shadow DOM has a\nmatrix row, two managers on one page have a lock ledger — and the portal had\none destination.\n\n`PortalTarget` is `boolean | (() => Element | null)`, and the second form is\na getter rather than an element for the reason `getDialog` is one: the option\nis read where the dialog is placed, and a caller naming a node at hook-call\ntime would be naming one its own tree has not rendered. It is asked at each\nplacement, so a host that mounts late is found — React re-reads it per\nrender, Solid once, since that binding mounts the node itself and there is\nnothing left to move.\n\nA getter answering `null` falls back to the default host and warns rather\nthan un-portaling: by then the arrangement is chosen and the placement CSS\nwith it, so rendering inline would position the dialog against the wrong\nthing. Visible under `setLogLevel` beats an invisible dialog.\n\n`resolvePortalHost` takes the default host as an argument rather than reading\n`document.body` itself, which keeps the decision a pure function of its\ninputs and unit-testable — and the React binding calls it only on the\nportaled branch, because the argument is what a server pass cannot evaluate.\nPortaling has never server-rendered; the default and contained paths do, and\n`verify:package` asserts it.\n\n`umbra/vanilla` keeps a plain `boolean`: there `portal` selects the placement\nand never moves the element, since reparenting the caller''s markup would take\nits ids, stylesheet scope and listeners with it. Accepting a host it could\nonly ignore is the silently-dropped option the type is there to prevent.\n\n`portal: true` and `portal: false` behave exactly as before.\n\n* docs: findings and suggestions from the core review\n\nNotes from a pass over the library core, kept in the branch rather than in a\nconversation. Two halves: what was found and fixed here (the four commits\nbefore it), and what stays addressable — each point with its evidence, its\ncost and a recommendation.\n\nThe conclusion worth keeping: the core is missing no subsystem. What the pass\nfound were asymmetries — a principle implemented on one path and not on its\nsiblings — which is a compliment rather than a verdict.\n\nThree things in it are new information rather than a summary:\n\nThe doc budget is at exactly 13500 of 13500 words, so the next word added to\nany CLAUDE.md fails the gate whatever it says. The routing rule is good and\nworked as designed, but with no headroom it stops discriminating between \"this\nfact does not belong here\" and \"there is no room left\".\n\nThe back button is the library''s one refusal with no `why` recorded anywhere —\ntimers, live regions, `aria-modal` and UI all have their matrix row. By the\nrepo''s own standard the missing decision is the defect.\n\nAnd the environment note, because it nearly turned three false failures into\nreported facts: `cdn.playwright.dev` is blocked here, the container''s Chromium\nis a different build from the one `@playwright/test` wants, and the three\nfocus-visibility tests fail on that mismatch alone — on `origin/main` too.\nCI is green for the right reason (it runs inside the official Playwright\nimage). The whole suite passes 377/377 against the correct build, which is\ndownloadable from a host the policy does allow.\n\n* fix(core): six findings from reviewing this branch against main\n\nA review pass over the four commits below, run against the four that landed on `main` beside them.\nEach item was probed rather than read.\n\n**The Solid and vanilla backdrop paths were asserted by nothing.** Reverting both to\n`store.close(DISMISS_REASON)` — reintroducing the exact defect `answerDismiss` exists to prevent, on\ntwo bindings of three — left all 382 component tests passing; the same mutation on React fails two.\nBoth bindings have their own backdrop-with-`onDismissRequest` test now, and both fail when reverted.\nSolid also has the portal-host assertion it had none of.\n\n**A portal host was re-read on every React render.** A container that changed identity under an open\ndialog made React mount a fresh, closed `<dialog>` that `syncOpenSequence` will not show outside\n`''opening''`: the modal vanished with its store still reporting `''open''` and nothing left to dismiss.\nThe host is held for a portal era now, re-read only when `portal` flips between portaled and not.\nThe repair was first written as a lifecycle step and reverted — by the repo''s own test for what is\ncore, only React can replace its own node, so the cause belongs in React rather than the director.\n\n**`PortalTarget` promised what neither binding delivers.** \"Asked each time the dialog is placed, so\na host that arrives late is picked up\" is false on Solid, which resolves once at mount, and was true\non React only through the accident that stranded it. The contract says what both do now — the host\nmust exist when the modal is placed — and names what qualifies. The React story used its own sibling\nas a host and passed on a second-render coincidence; it mounts the host first.\n\n**A duplicate id emitted `register` twice against one `unregister`**, so the membership count the\npair exists to support drifts. The displaced registration is reported leaving, before the new one\narrives.\n\n**`createOpenRequest(undefined, context)` did not compile against a declared payload** — the\nbuilder''s own `@example`, safe there only because the example names an undeclared id. A context-only\noverload returns `OpenRequest<never>`, which fits every contract.\n\n**A second file in `type-fixtures/` was not compiled at all**: `tsconfig.registry.json` named one\nfile, so a fixture added beside it looked like a gate and was not one. Discovered by a glob now.\n\nTwo more about where a fact lives. `PortalTarget` had been inserted between `ModalPhase`''s doc\ncomment and `ModalPhase`, so a public root export lost its documentation to the declaration above\nit. And the review note was holding two compatibility facts whose home is the matrix — the back\nbutton, now a `no-by-design` platform row with its `why`, and one-id-one-instance, now an answer in\nthe `id` row rather than a silence.\n\n* feat(playground): demonstrate the surfaces this branch added, and retire the review note\n\nThree cards, because a surface nothing demonstrates is one a reader takes on faith — and the\nplayground''s own rule is that an example not placed on a page does not exist.\n\n**\"An open that lands on nothing\"** (`/imperative`) — `open()` answering `false`, and the `register`\nevent closing the gap. The waiter it shows waits for the **`open`** event rather than retiring on\n`register`, and that is the lesson rather than a detail: the version that unsubscribes on `register`\nfails, and React''s development double-mount is enough to show it — the first registration is torn\ndown and replaced, so the open lands on a modal about to unmount and the second finds nobody\nlistening. Found by driving the card, not by reading it.\n\n**\"A payload the contract declares\"** (`/imperative`) — `ModalContract.payload` and `PayloadOf`,\nbeside the card that asks with a payload typed into a textarea. The contrast is the point: that one\nis genuinely `unknown` and parses, this one is asked and answered inside the project, so the\ncompiler checks the ask and no type argument is written anywhere.\n\n**\"Closing every one of them\"** (`/stacking`) — the loop over `lookup().getOpen()` that stands in for\na `closeAll()` the library does not ship, since every caller wants a different filter. Its controls\nare **inside** the dialogs. Written on the card first, which was unusable: three modals in the top\nlayer make the page under them inert, so the button could not be pressed at all. The top-layer rule\nis in CLAUDE.md and this is what ignoring it looks like.\n\n`decouverte-et-suggestions.md` is removed, now that each of its findings has the home the repo keeps\nthat kind of fact in: the back button and one-id-one-instance in the matrix, `portal: boolean` on the\nvanilla binding in the `portal: true` row''s `why`, the documentation budget resolved on `main`, and\nthe three demonstrations above.\n\n`onOpenRequest` receiving `unknown` stays open, and stays a decision. `data` has one producer — the\nmodal''s own `handle.close` — so believing it on the receiving side is honest; `payload` has two, and\nthe second is the door''s whole purpose: a microfrontend, a relay, another bundle, none compiled here.\nTyping the handler would state a guarantee exactly where it cannot be kept, and `PayloadOf` is a root\nexport, so the receiving side already has the name to parse to.\n\n* refactor(test): one shared noop, and one empty function that was hiding a branch\n\n`() => {}` appeared 26 times, 24 of them a stub argument in a test — `{ onKeyDown: () => {} }`,\nwhich reads as something somebody meant to fill in rather than as a deliberate nothing. They share\n`src/__tests__/noop.ts` now, beside the other harness helpers.\n\n**Not exported from the root**: the library has no site for it, because a step that attaches nothing\nreturns `undefined` and the caller checks, which is what the `attach*` contract already says.\nShipping one would be exporting something the library does not run on.\n\nThe helper''s doc carries the one case it must not be used for — where the *identity* is the subject.\nA test asserting that a changed callback rebuilds a lifecycle step is asserting that two functions\ndiffer, and one shared reference would make it compare equal and quietly assert the opposite. That\nhazard is not live here (the pass those tests diff against holds `undefined`, and all 579 unit tests\nstill pass), but the next reader deserves the warning rather than the discovery.\n\nTwo things the sweep separated. `templates/__tests__/shared.test.ts` had a local `noop` that returns\na node — a `render` stub, never a noop; it is `renderNothing` now. And the single\n`return () => {};` was an early return handing back a canceller with nothing to cancel: the waiter\nit lived in subscribes before it opens now, for the reason `openAndWait` registers its resolver\nfirst, which leaves one return path and no empty function to name.\n\n* feat(core)!: a modal''s contract declares what each reason closes with\n\n`ModalRegistry` entries said `{ data, reason }` — one payload for every reason\na modal has. Five of the six declared entries carrying a payload had more than\none reason, and each paid for it at the call site with a fabricated default for\na state that cannot occur: `result.data ?? 0` after `reason === ''sent''` never\nmeant \"sent zero items\".\n\nAn entry now declares `closesWith`, taking either the bare reasons or a payload\nper reason, and a declared payload is required — `close(''confirm'', data)` must\nbe given it, a bare `action(''confirm'')` is rejected. Without the requirement,\ncorrelation only forbids a mistake nobody makes and every `??` survives.\n\n`data`/`reason` are gone rather than kept beside it: two keys for one act is\nwhat the vocabulary table forbids, and the additive form needed a precedence\nrule. `payload` became `opensWith` so the pair is named by direction.\n\nThe internals did not move. `CloseResult` stays the flat plain object its doc\ninsists on; a union keyed by `reason` is opaque at a generic boundary, so the\ncorrelation is stated only in the registered-id overloads every entry point\nalready had. `DataOf` must keep ending in `infer` — narrowing that union\nsilently stops the manager''s facade from implementing its own interface.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `ModalRegistry` entries use `closesWith` and `opensWith`;\n`data` and `reason` are no longer read.\n\n* fix(core): close the three holes the contract left open\n\nThree defects the review found, each confirmed against the compiler rather\nthan taken on report — and one it claimed that is not real: `close()` inside\nan action handler was already rejected.\n\n`action(''confirm'', { hotkey })` auto-closed with nothing, because\n`ActionOptions.onAction` is optional. The options branch now requires it where\nthe reason declares a payload — the shape `bindDialog`''s twin already had.\n\n`DataOf` matched `closesWith` against `Readonly<Record<string, …>>`, which an\n`interface` never satisfies for want of an index signature: a contract declared\nthrough a named interface answered `void` while `ReasonOf` read it correctly.\nIt reads through `keyof` now, which both shapes answer.\n\n`dialogManager.close(id, reason)` accepted a reason whose contract requires a\npayload and closed without one, handing `onClose` a result its own type forbids\n— and this branch had just removed the runtime guards that used to absorb it.\nIt takes `PayloadFreeReasonOf` now.\n\nDocs that named the old keys followed.\n\n* test(core): say why the interface fixture must stay an interface\n\nIt has no index signature, which is the whole subject — as a `type` it is the\nneighbouring entry again and the assertion passes while proving nothing. A pass\nthat removes unnecessary interfaces would have converted it silently.\n\n* refactor(tests): the worklist says which of ten open cells were work\n\n`yarn todo` printed ten and had printed nine or ten for eleven days. The\nfile''s history says which half of that was real: `✓ untested` went 16 to 0\nand stayed, `~` sat at six for ten days, and not one of the four caveats was\never removed — all four arrived attached to a feature branch.\n\nSo the list was not growing so much as never finishing, and it could not\nfinish: three different things printed under one heading — work, decisions\nalready taken, and answers somebody else has to ship.\n\n`⏸ blocked` is the state that was missing, and it owes a `recheck`: what to\nlook at, and the ISO date someone last did. Two cells were it all along and\nsaid so themselves — the WebKit half of the Tab recovery is \"left open only\nto be re-measured\", the TypeScript 6 pin \"is blocked on typedoc rather than\non this repo\". `no-platform` could not carry them; it means never, and both\nchange when somebody else releases. `worklist()` returns them in a second\nlist nobody is expected to burn down.\n\nFour more cells were decisions wearing a `~` or a `?`, each already argued in\nthe cell that carried it: `portal: true` on the controller and a fragment\nswapped underneath it are `✗ by design`, and the `ModalRegistry` and Solid\n`phase` caveats are notes. No judgement is reversed here — the state catches\nup with the sentence beside it.\n\nA caveat is now `{ question, nextStep }`, both gated. That is what stops the\nratchet, and it is the shape a refusal''s `why` already had: an author who\ncannot say what would close it has written a note.\n\nEvery open cell carries a `since`, and there is deliberately no threshold on\nthe count — the count is what hid the plateau, since six `~` for ten days\nreads exactly like six closed and six opened. `yarn todo` sorts oldest-first\nand prints the age instead.\n\nTwo things fell out. `openTail` is shared by all three axes, because the\nplatform and WCAG loops rendered `why` and nothing else, so a caveat on one\nof those rows reached `yarn todo` and never reached `API.md` — the exact\nhiding it is rendered to prevent on a binding cell. And `bindingCells`\nreplaces the react/solid/vanilla triple written out in four places, one of\nthem the gate that exists to catch a fourth binding.\n\nNothing the library does changed: 10 open becomes 4 open and 2 on watch.\n\n* fix(core): a raise puts the caret back on every engine, not on the engine''s guess\n\nA raise is `close()` + `showModal()`, the only mechanism the top layer\noffers. The dialog that held the keyboard got it back — `raiseDialog` reads\nthe active element before the round-trip and restores it after. The one that\ndid not was left on whatever `showModal()` picks: Chromium the first\nfocusable, WebKit the field. So a policy installed while a second dialog was\nin front handed the front dialog back to its confirm button and lost the\nfield someone was typing in.\n\nThe coordinator already remembered the right answer and was having it\noverwritten. `lastFocusInside` tracks every `focusin` inside the dialog, and\nthe focus `showModal()` takes on the way back fires one — indistinguishable\nat the listener from a person clicking. It landed on the memory a fraction\nbefore anything could read it, so there was nothing left to restore from, and\nthe reclaim''s \"focus is inside me, nothing to do\" guard was then satisfied by\nthe wrong control.\n\n`isRaisingDialog()` publishes the round-trip as a window and `remember`\ndeclines to record inside it. A synchronous counter is enough because\n`close()`, `showModal()` and `focus()` dispatch `focusin` before they return;\nanything arriving later is somebody''s actual doing.\n\nThe reclaim now reads focus-inside-but-not-where-I-remember as the signature\nof a move the library made. Sound only because every other way focus travels\ninside is recorded, so the memory is re-synced by the time anything asks. Two\nstates are deliberately not divergence: focus on the `<dialog>` element\nitself, which a dead-space click produces and which is never recorded —\nreading it as divergence would yank the keyboard off a state\n`focus-containment.ct.tsx` pins — and a memory that has left the DOM, since\nfalling through with one sends the restore to the `focusOnOpen` button,\nre-honouring an opening choice over wherever the user had got to.\n\nThe assertion that used to accept either answer now pins one. \"keeps the\nkeyboard when something opens over it\" read `toContain([''shadow-confirm'',\n''shadow-note''])`, because pinning a control pinned an engine and broke CI. It\npins `shadow-note` now and passes on Chromium, Firefox and WebKit. Checked\nthe other way too: with the window disabled, Chromium returns\n`shadow-confirm` and the test fails.\n\nWhat stays the engine''s is the case with no memory to restore: a dialog\nnobody had focused anything in comes back on whatever `showModal()` picks,\nand there is nothing truer to put there.\n\nMatrix cell `~` → `✓`; `yarn todo` from 4 open to 3.\n\n* fix(manager): a late policy install lifts what the order needs, not everything\n\n`prioritize` over dialogs already on screen re-showed every open modal\ndialog. The top layer is untracked until a policy exists — `syncStackOrder`\nis dormant before then — so the first plan compared the wanted order against\nan empty `current`, and `planRaises` returns everything when it has nothing\nto keep. Each entry is a real `close()` + `showModal()`.\n\nThis was tried once before and abandoned, because the measurement said it\nchanged nothing. That reading was wrong, and the way it was wrong is worth\nkeeping: `close()` queues its event. The harness counted native `close`\nevents with a synchronous read straight after the install, which returns an\nempty array about half the time — the raises had happened and the events had\nnot been delivered yet. Reading zero, twice, looked like evidence that\nnothing was reachable here.\n\nRe-measured on the arrangement the old note said had never been tried —\nthree dialogs, opened high, mid, low, against a policy wanting the reverse —\nand polling for the queued events instead of reading once: three round-trips\nagainst an empty `current`, two when seeded from the stack as it stands. The\nsaved one is `mr-low`: it is at the top and belongs at the bottom, and\nre-showing the two above it puts it there without touching it. That is\n`planRaises`'' rule — keep the longest prefix of the wanted order that is\nalready a subsequence of the real one — finally given a real `current`.\n\nThe seed is only sound before the first policy, which is the only place it\nruns: nothing has raised anything yet, so the top layer is the open order,\nand that is what the snapshot already carries, ranked by `openSequence`\nbecause no policy has ranked it. Reading the DOM would be a second source for\na fact the manager holds. A dialog at phase `''opening''` is excluded by the\nsame test `syncStackOrder` makes — it is not in the top layer, and seeding it\nwould claim a position the platform has not given it.\n\n`a late install lifts only what the order needs` pins both numbers and the\nresulting paint order. Checked the other way: with the seed removed it\nreports three and fails.\n\nMatrix cell `~` → `✓`; `yarn todo` from 3 open to 2.\n\n* fix(core): an exit animation the caller asked for is no longer skipped\n\n`{ duration: 0, exitDuration: 900 }` — instant in, animated out — lost its\nexit entirely. The close path short-circuits when transitions are disabled,\nso it does not wait for a `transitionend` that a `prefers-reduced-motion`\nrule will never fire. That check was measured once per open, reading\n`getComputedStyle(dialog).transitionDuration` while the element still carried\nthe entrance style. An entrance of `0` computes to `0s`, which is\nindistinguishable from `transition: none !important` — so the dialog was\nfiled as having no transitions at all, and the exit was dropped along with\nany observable `''closing''` window.\n\nThe exit''s own duration is the only one that answers the exit''s question, and\nit is on the element by the time the phase is `''closing''`: the binding writes\nthe phase''s style during render, so the effect runs after it.\n`syncCloseSequence` re-measures there. The open pass stays — it costs nothing\nand keeps the answer this open''s rather than the first open''s — and both\nreadings still catch what the check is chiefly for, since a reduced-motion\nrule computes to `0s` at either moment.\n\nThis surfaced from the other end. The matrix carried a caveat saying the\n`''closing''` window was not assertable in a component test, \"transitions being\noff in a harness\". They were not off: the harness asked for a zero-length\nentrance, and the library concluded from that that it had none. The premise\nwas the bug.\n\nThe assertion is now in `phase reaches the render callback, and agrees with\nthe hook return` and passes on Chromium, Firefox and WebKit; with the\nre-measure removed it reads `closed` where it expects `closing` and fails.\n\nCaveat dropped rather than reworded; `yarn todo` from 2 open to 1.\n\n* docs(tests): the reconcileOpen note had the wrong pair written on it\n\nThe last open cell said the `phase`-versus-`isVisible` half of\n`reconcileOpen` was proven on React only, that \"the controller never\npublishes that phase here\", and that the two forms of the decision differ on\n`[''closing'', false]`. Two of those three are now false, and one was never\ntrue.\n\nThe controller publishes `''closing''` now — the exit-measurement fix is why.\nThe vanilla reconcile harness asks for `{ duration: 0, exitDuration: 120 }`,\nthe same shape that lost its exit everywhere else, so the sequence read\n`opening,open,closed` and the window the decision turns on did not exist. It\nreads `opening,open,closing,closed`, and the CT test pins that.\n\nThe differing pair is `[''closing'', true]`, not `[''closing'', false]`. The flag\ngoing back up mid-exit is the case the guard exists for — `reconcile-open.ts`\nsays so in its own comment, \"how a call site that raised the prop mid-exit\ngets its dialog back\", and `reconcile-open.test.ts` spells it out over all\neight inputs: with the guard dropped, `open: false` still answers `''none''`,\nbecause a closing dialog is not open and the prop agrees. The two forms never\ndisagreed on the pair the note named. Measured rather than re-read: removing\nthe guard leaves every assertion in that harness green.\n\nAnd `[''closing'', true]` is not reachable end-to-end from a snapshot surface,\nwhich is a fact about the surface rather than a gap in it. Raising the flag\nis not a store event, so no notification lands while the phase is `''closing''`\nand the flag is up — a subscriber-side recorder was written to try, and\nrecords nothing because there is nothing to record. The case is exhaustive at\nthe unit level, where it belongs.\n\nSo the entry is a note, not an open question: there is no next step, which\nunder the new `caveat` shape is exactly the test for one.\n\n`yarn todo` prints 0 open and 2 on the watch list.\n\n* docs(tests): both watch-list cells re-measured, both unchanged\n\nThe two blocked cells carry the date someone last looked, which is the only\nthing this repo owns about an answer that is somebody else''s to ship.\n\nWebKit still swallows a forward Tab from the dialog element. Measured the way\nthe cell means it — `attachFocusContainment` neutered so the engine answers\nalone, then the dead-space-click test run on all three: Chromium and Firefox\nreach the content natively, WebKit leaves focus on the `<dialog>`. The\nunconditional recovery is still earning its place.\n\ntypedoc is still 0.28.20 and still peers on `5.0.x || … || 6.0.x`. The\n`typescript@6.0.3` pin is that range, not a stale entry.\n\nNo cell changed state; only `recheck.measured`.\n\n* chore: re-measure coverage, and classify the one module that made it drop\n\n`registered-types.ts` arrived on this branch with no entry in `.c8rc.json`,\nso it counted as 119 uncovered statements and took unit coverage from 96.73%\nto 94.63%. It has no runtime at all — every declaration in it is a type,\nstated in an overload and never implemented against — so it belongs in the\ntype-only group beside `core/types.ts` and `core/registry.ts`. That is the\nexclude list working as intended: it is spelled one module at a time so a new\none shows up as a gap until somebody decides which kind it is.\n\nRe-measured after: unit 96.66%, component 91.61% over 55 files, both on\n2026-08-25. Unit is where it was before the branch. Component is 0.89 down,\nwhich is the new binding surface — the portal host, the registry narrowing in\n`bind-dialog` — arriving faster than its component tests.\n\nREADME and CLAUDE.md rewritten by `yarn coverage:update`, badges included.\n\n* docs: three findings from the review of this branch\n\n**`raiseDialog` lost its JSDoc to its own new neighbours.** This branch\ninserted `raiseDepth` and `isRaisingDialog` between the block describing\n`raiseDialog` — close-and-re-show, the three consequences, `@returns` — and\nthe function itself, and TypeScript attaches only the immediately preceding\nblock. Hover showed nothing and typedoc had nowhere to hang the prose. The\ntwo declarations move above it, which also reads in dependency order: the\nstate, the window it publishes, then the function that opens it.\n\n**Two comments above `portalEra` said opposite things.** One claimed a\ncaller whose host moves is followed; the other, and the code, and\n`PortalTarget`''s own contract all say the host is held for the portal era and\nre-read only when `portal` flips. The first was prose left from before the\nper-render re-read was corrected — a maintainer trusting it would assume\nmoving-host support the library deliberately refuses.\n\n**API.md taught the deferred-open shape the playground exists to correct.**\nThe `openWhenRegistered` snippet retired its subscription on `register`,\nwhich is the version that fails: React''s development double-mount tears the\nfirst registration down, so the open lands on a modal about to unmount and\nthe second registration finds nobody listening. It retires on `open` now,\nwith the reasoning beside it and a pointer to the playground demo — this is\nthe page someone integrating a deep link is on, so the failing form was the\none most likely to be copied.\n\nDocs only; no behaviour changed. 581 unit, 386 component on all three\nengines.","tree":{"sha":"0f3115aeda2a6e85ee8240a2863572a128b28496","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/0f3115aeda2a6e85ee8240a2863572a128b28496"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/c6cac4c96ca96bda46147ca431ac9f9ff296ba51","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/c6cac4c96ca96bda46147ca431ac9f9ff296ba51","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKGM2Y2FjNGM5NmNhOTZiZGE0NjE0N2NhNDMxYWM5ZjlmZjI5NmJhNTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/47247055030a05b7ac6e81712bd2fea4a3f71725","sha":"47247055030a05b7ac6e81712bd2fea4a3f71725","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/47247055030a05b7ac6e81712bd2fea4a3f71725"}],"sha":"c6cac4c96ca96bda46147ca431ac9f9ff296ba51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/c6cac4c96ca96bda46147ca431ac9f9ff296ba51"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/47247055030a05b7ac6e81712bd2fea4a3f71725/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T00:56:09Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T00:56:09Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"docs: every word budget carries 10% of headroom\n\nThe four `CLAUDE.md` files were meeting their budgets exactly — 13 499 words against a 13 500\nceiling — and the last few sessions each ended hunting a dozen words to make a paragraph fit.\nMeeting a ceiling is not the same as having room under one: the cost lands on whoever writes next,\nevery time, and it is paid by trimming prose that is already dense.\n\n12 149 words now, and no file above 87% of its own budget. The cuts are duplication rather than\ncontent: the store module''s two modes and mutation rules were written out in full in both\n`src/CLAUDE.md` and `src/store/CLAUDE.md`; the two-kinds-of-binding passage ran in the root and\nagain in `src/`; the three forwarded button props were in the root, `src/` and the README; the\n`attach*` list restated the JSDoc its own section says not to restate. Where prose was the only\ncopy it was compressed, not dropped.\n\nThe norm is on `doc-budget.test.ts` and in the root file''s opening lines, because a buffer nobody\nknows about gets spent silently: land at 90%, and spend the headroom on writing rather than on\nfitting.\n\nCarries one content change from the commit before it — `openAndWait`''s `[Error, null]` branch now\nhas three causes rather than two.","tree":{"sha":"e1663ae81d39805e485c2b21c740bf0d1643b03a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/e1663ae81d39805e485c2b21c740bf0d1643b03a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/47247055030a05b7ac6e81712bd2fea4a3f71725","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/47247055030a05b7ac6e81712bd2fea4a3f71725","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKDQ3MjQ3MDU1MDMwYTA1YjdhYzZlODE3MTJiZDJmZWE0YTNmNzE3MjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/a771d9a88b0393cbcc211eefcf90d65032c89691","sha":"a771d9a88b0393cbcc211eefcf90d65032c89691","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/a771d9a88b0393cbcc211eefcf90d65032c89691"}],"sha":"47247055030a05b7ac6e81712bd2fea4a3f71725","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/47247055030a05b7ac6e81712bd2fea4a3f71725"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/a771d9a88b0393cbcc211eefcf90d65032c89691/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T00:55:42Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T00:55:42Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"fix(core): a resolver registered during the exit is refused, not answered\n\n`openAndWait` registers its close resolver before requesting the open, which is the whole point of\nthe method. But `beginOpen` is a no-op unless the modal is `''closed''` and it queues no reopen, so a\ncall arriving mid-exit attached to the close already in flight: nothing opened, and the caller was\nhanded a reason somebody else''s interaction produced. A service acting on `reason === ''confirm''`\nacts twice.\n\nThe rule belongs to the store, so it lives there — `addCloseResolver` settles that resolver with\n`[Error, null]` instead. All three awaiting doors inherit it in one place: the hook''s `openAndWait`,\n`dialogManager.openAndWait`, and `requestOpenAndWait`, whose accepted outcome then carries the error\nbranch on `closed`.\n\nRefusing rather than queueing a reopen keeps this consistent with `open()`, which resolves\nimmediately in the same situation and is pinned by its own test.\n\nThe click path was never exposed — swept at 0/20/60/120/200 ms against the playground''s deploy flow,\nand the top layer blocks the page through a modal dialog''s exit. What was exposed is programmatic\ncallers and non-modal panels, where the page stays live while one slides away.\n\nAlso: `src/core/registry.ts` is 72 lines of types and no runtime, and never went into `.c8rc.json`''s\ntype-only group — it read as 0% and pulled unit coverage down to 95.44%, against 96.77% excluded.","tree":{"sha":"3a7d5db932fd3b3b05457ccf143ce887abaff6ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/3a7d5db932fd3b3b05457ccf143ce887abaff6ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/a771d9a88b0393cbcc211eefcf90d65032c89691","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/a771d9a88b0393cbcc211eefcf90d65032c89691","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKGE3NzFkOWE4OGIwMzkzY2JjYzIxMWVlZmNmOTBkNjUwMzJjODk2OTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/53d1a868929ee0f5ecd13f5c3f8e95f8ed3b7e32","sha":"53d1a868929ee0f5ecd13f5c3f8e95f8ed3b7e32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/53d1a868929ee0f5ecd13f5c3f8e95f8ed3b7e32"}],"sha":"a771d9a88b0393cbcc211eefcf90d65032c89691","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/a771d9a88b0393cbcc211eefcf90d65032c89691"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/53d1a868929ee0f5ecd13f5c3f8e95f8ed3b7e32/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T00:38:55Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T00:38:55Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"fix(test): a worktree under .claude/ was read as a second copy of the suite\n\n`.claude/worktrees/<branch>/` is a whole checkout of this repo living inside it, with its own\n`node_modules` — and both gates walk the tree by an unanchored pattern. Playwright''s `src/**`\nmatched it and threw `Requiring @playwright/test second time` on the first file it loaded; the doc\nbudget counted four extra `CLAUDE.md`s. Neither named a worktree, and nothing in the repo was wrong.\n\n`testIgnore` excludes it, and the budget walker skips `.claude/worktrees` by path rather than by\nname — `.claude` itself stays walked, because a `CLAUDE.md` added there is one a session loads and\nshould want a budget. `.gitignore` covers prettier and oxlint, both of which read it, and oxlint\nneeded reaching: it discovers nested configs before applying its own `ignorePatterns`, so it had\nrefused to start over an `options.typeAware` that is only legal in a root config. Four candidate\nentries were each removed and re-run to see it fail; the two that did not are not here.","tree":{"sha":"34feeca61f06a361c1c1c873f0f7eb76f443b499","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/34feeca61f06a361c1c1c873f0f7eb76f443b499"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/53d1a868929ee0f5ecd13f5c3f8e95f8ed3b7e32","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/53d1a868929ee0f5ecd13f5c3f8e95f8ed3b7e32","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKDUzZDFhODY4OTI5ZWUwZjVlY2QxM2Y1YzNmOGU5NWY4ZWQzYjdlMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/322ddb01bf2f35cf554042f4b96e135ecaf56a4d","sha":"322ddb01bf2f35cf554042f4b96e135ecaf56a4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/322ddb01bf2f35cf554042f4b96e135ecaf56a4d"}],"sha":"53d1a868929ee0f5ecd13f5c3f8e95f8ed3b7e32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/53d1a868929ee0f5ecd13f5c3f8e95f8ed3b7e32"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/322ddb01bf2f35cf554042f4b96e135ecaf56a4d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T00:38:39Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T00:38:39Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"fix(playground): the select popup was white in dark mode, and its labels were on it\n\n`background: inherit` on a `<span>` wrapper resolves to transparent, which reads fine on the closed\ncontrol and is the whole defect on the open one: `appearance: none` takes the select out of the UA''s\nthemed painting, so Chrome canvases the option popup with the control''s own background-color.\nTransparent renders white there, and the options inherit the dark theme''s white ink — measured\n#FFFFFF on #FFFFFF, two of the wizard''s three steps invisible. `color-scheme: dark` reaches the\nelement and does not override an author background.\n\nThe recipe moves out of inline styles at the call site into `shared/ui/SelectionDropdown`, so it is\nfixed once and the next select inherits it. The guard is a component test, because the thing that\nbroke is not in the page: it asserts both backgrounds are opaque, and that the two schemes differ —\nthe second because a token that fails to resolve falls back identically in both.","tree":{"sha":"fc846c312ab13373a2aed8f75a302522a758a925","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/fc846c312ab13373a2aed8f75a302522a758a925"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/322ddb01bf2f35cf554042f4b96e135ecaf56a4d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/322ddb01bf2f35cf554042f4b96e135ecaf56a4d","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKDMyMmRkYjAxYmYyZjM1Y2Y1NTQwNDJmNGI5NmUxMzVlY2FmNTZhNGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/c1fda285b41711b3e4cd96dc7f76c0ce6b052046","sha":"c1fda285b41711b3e4cd96dc7f76c0ce6b052046","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/c1fda285b41711b3e4cd96dc7f76c0ce6b052046"}],"sha":"322ddb01bf2f35cf554042f4b96e135ecaf56a4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/322ddb01bf2f35cf554042f4b96e135ecaf56a4d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/c1fda285b41711b3e4cd96dc7f76c0ce6b052046/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T02:57:42Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T02:57:42Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"feat(core): dialogManager.openAndWait, and a close surface that reads its types off the id\n\nThe registry typed the id; every door that handed back a close still said `string`. A service\nwith no component to hold a hook had to roll its own await over `subscribe`, which is a broadcast\nover every dialog on the page — one event type serves them all, so `reason` there could never be\nnarrower than `string`. `dialogManager.openAndWait(id)` resolves the same `[error, result]` tuple\na hook does, typed by the registry, and answers `[Error, null]` for an unregistered id instead of\nwaiting forever.\n\n`OpenRequestOutcome` is generic, so an accepted request''s `closed` carries the modal''s contract.\n`close` takes `ReasonOf<NoInfer<TId>>`, so a wrong reason is reported against the reason rather\nthan solved by widening the id. `ModalLookup`''s four queries take `ModalId`.\n\nBoth awaiting doors are declared as overload pairs — narrow on `RegisteredModalId`, loose on\n`ModalId` — because a loose implementation cannot satisfy a generic declaration and the repo bans\nthe cast that would hide it.\n\nThe playground''s deployment service and the README''s framework-free example were the two callers\nwritten the old way; neither has a listener to unsubscribe now, and `decision` is\n`''cancel'' | ''confirm'' | ''dismiss''` where it was `string`.","tree":{"sha":"eee16968722a7e910b3d14524ea8b0dd80cb7879","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/eee16968722a7e910b3d14524ea8b0dd80cb7879"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/c1fda285b41711b3e4cd96dc7f76c0ce6b052046","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/c1fda285b41711b3e4cd96dc7f76c0ce6b052046","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKGMxZmRhMjg1YjQxNzExYjNlNGNkOTZkYzdmNzZjMGNlNmIwNTIwNDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/ea1eef86bda7131bcbc369198fa28fa861d77e1c","sha":"ea1eef86bda7131bcbc369198fa28fa861d77e1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/ea1eef86bda7131bcbc369198fa28fa861d77e1c"}],"sha":"c1fda285b41711b3e4cd96dc7f76c0ce6b052046","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/c1fda285b41711b3e4cd96dc7f76c0ce6b052046"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/ea1eef86bda7131bcbc369198fa28fa861d77e1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T02:16:09Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T02:43:50Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"feat(playground): declare all 38 modals in one registry, and loosen the design to allow it\n\nAdopting the registry in the playground is what settled its design. The first\nshape made an augmented registry exhaustive — declare one modal and an undeclared\nid is an error everywhere. That produced 247 errors here, 244 of them in the\nlibrary''s own CT harnesses, which /stories renders: the playground compiles a few\nhundred modal declarations it does not own, and no app hosting a third-party\npanel could adopt it either.\n\nSo `ModalId` is `keyof ModalRegistry | (string & {})`. An undeclared id still\nworks and adoption is one modal at a time. What an entry buys is its contract,\nnot exhaustiveness, and the price is that a mistyped id is no longer an error.\n\nTwo mechanical findings behind that. `(string & {})` in the union kills literal\ninference, so per-id reason checking died with it — and an overload pair does not\nbring it back, because a failing first overload falls through to the permissive\none instead of erroring. One generic signature does:\n\n  close<TId extends ModalId>(id: TId, reason?: ReasonOf<TId> | DismissReason)\n\nwhich is also the first time that reason has been checked at all; the old\nsignature typed it `string`. Every hook needed the registered overload too, not\njust `useModal`: the template hooks declare their own signatures over it, so a\nmodal opened through them read `void` for its payload — and `bindDialog` had none\neither, though the matrix already claimed it narrowed with the rest. `useLookup`\nstill took a bare `string` on both bindings.\n\nplayground/src/app/modal-registry.ts lists 38 modals with their reasons and\npayloads, and 34 call sites dropped their type arguments to read from it. That\nsecond half is what makes it a single source: naming the generics selects the\nother overload, so the registry is never consulted and the two can disagree in\nsilence — verified, a call site could claim an unrelated payload and nothing\nobjected. Four payload types local to a component are exported so they can be\nnamed.\n\nDeclaring them found three real mismatches. deployment-service.ts closes\ndeploy-failure with ''retry'' against a modal declaring <void, ''acknowledge''>; the\nold `close(id, reason?: string)` accepted anything, so it compiled and the reason\nwas wrong at runtime. The other two were mine: deploy-confirm written as\n''cancel'' | ''deploy'' when its actions are cancel and confirm, and deploy-failure\nas ''close''.\n\nOne limit the example now teaches rather than hides: `openAndAwaitClose` resolves\n`string`, because it listens on `subscribe`, a broadcast over every dialog whose\none event type cannot carry a per-id reason. The typed await lives on the hook,\nand a service with no component cannot hold one.\n\nFull detail in CHANGELOG.md under 2026-08-21.","tree":{"sha":"9628d16efc28ec56e1ad6af436e09a760f628154","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/9628d16efc28ec56e1ad6af436e09a760f628154"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/ea1eef86bda7131bcbc369198fa28fa861d77e1c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/ea1eef86bda7131bcbc369198fa28fa861d77e1c","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKGVhMWVlZjg2YmRhNzEzMWJjYmMzNjkxOThmYTI4ZmE4NjFkNzdlMWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/18ea17e77359a701396e83bb529fdfd4742980e6","sha":"18ea17e77359a701396e83bb529fdfd4742980e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/18ea17e77359a701396e83bb529fdfd4742980e6"}],"sha":"ea1eef86bda7131bcbc369198fa28fa861d77e1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/ea1eef86bda7131bcbc369198fa28fa861d77e1c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/18ea17e77359a701396e83bb529fdfd4742980e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T01:00:18Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T01:00:18Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"feat(core): ModalRegistry, so a project can name its modals once\n\nAn id was the last untyped string in the library. `dialogManager.open(''confrim'')`\ncompiled and did nothing, and a helper resolving `Promise<string>` let\n`=== ''delete''` past the checker when the modal''s reasons were ''confirm'' |\n''cancel''. A project declares its modals in one interface now:\n\n  declare module ''umbra'' {\n    interface ModalRegistry {\n      ''confirm-delete'': { data: { id: string }; reason: ''confirm'' | ''cancel'' };\n    }\n  }\n\nAn entry names what `CloseResult` already calls them — `reason` and `data` —\nrather than a second spelling of either. Every door narrows: open, close,\nrequestOpen, requestOpenAndWait, lookup, getZIndex, register, unregister.\n`useModal` gains an overload that reads the contract off the id, so a declared\nmodal needs no type arguments at all, and the per-call-site\n`useModal<TData, TReason>` form is untouched.\n\nNothing changes for a project that never opts in, and one detail guarantees it:\n\n  export type ModalId = [keyof ModalRegistry] extends [never] ? string : keyof ModalRegistry;\n\nThe brackets are load-bearing. A naked `keyof ModalRegistry extends never`\ndistributes over `never` and evaluates to `never`, so the fallback would be\nunreachable and every call site in every project that had not opted in would stop\ncompiling.\n\nProven at compile time in two configurations, because one file cannot hold both:\ndeclaration merging is global, so an augmented registry inside the main project\nwould hide the fallback the empty case asserts. `registry.test-d.ts` covers the\nempty state inside `yarn type-check`; `yarn type-check:registry` compiles\n`type-fixtures/` alone for the augmented one.\n\nThree limits, recorded rather than discovered twice. Declaring one modal declares\nthem all — an undeclared id is then an error everywhere, including inside the\nlibrary''s own tests, which is how the consequence surfaced; a computed id opts out\nwith `as ModalId`. Naming the id as a type argument is a convenience and not a\nsecond check: a type argument failing the registered overload falls to the next,\nwhere it reads as `TData`, so `useModal<''typo''>()` is legal — the id *value* is\nchecked either way. And typing the public doors reached the library''s own\nplumbing: five internal sites hold an id that genuinely is a registered one and\nwere typed `string`, so they take `ModalId` now rather than five casts the repo\nbans anyway.\n\n`ModalRegistry` is also the first interface in the public surface, and\napi-model.ts mapped only variables, functions and type aliases — so typedoc''s\nreflection was dropped and the build failed on a category listing an export the\nmodel could not see. Interfaces read as types on that page and are mapped as such.\n\nFull detail in CHANGELOG.md under 2026-08-21.","tree":{"sha":"582a51e49007559bed8e96e6b5bb1243a3eed01c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/582a51e49007559bed8e96e6b5bb1243a3eed01c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/18ea17e77359a701396e83bb529fdfd4742980e6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/18ea17e77359a701396e83bb529fdfd4742980e6","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKDE4ZWExN2U3NzM1OWE3MDEzOTZlODNiYjUyOWZkZmQ0NzQyOTgwZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/691c1f2ff298d5f12706830dde27da85f10f21d4","sha":"691c1f2ff298d5f12706830dde27da85f10f21d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/691c1f2ff298d5f12706830dde27da85f10f21d4"}],"sha":"18ea17e77359a701396e83bb529fdfd4742980e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/18ea17e77359a701396e83bb529fdfd4742980e6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/691c1f2ff298d5f12706830dde27da85f10f21d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T15:48:38Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T15:48:38Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"fix(playground): an example in French, and card prose running to 98 characters\n\nA visual pass over the routes, in both themes at desktop and phone.\n\n`open-request` was written in French — its dialog title, body, both buttons, the\nbanner and every log line — on a site that is otherwise entirely English. So was\nthe CT harness behind it, which also renders on /stories. Twenty strings\ntranslated. Two component assertions read the French back (`acceptée (mfa1)`)\nand were updated with them.\n\nCard descriptions had no measure. PageLayout holds its prose to --app-measure,\nand a card in a one-column grid held its to nothing: 98 characters to the line\nagainst the header''s 67, measured on /interop at 1440px. Cards take the measure\nnow, and so do section descriptions, which had been carrying a hardcoded 680px —\na third prose width on the same page. All three read 67ch.\n\nThat had a second effect worth naming: narrower prose wraps taller, so cards in a\nrow even out on their own. The dead space inside /imperative''s lightest card fell\nfrom roughly 280px to nothing, with no layout change.\n\nLeft alone deliberately: cards in a row still match height, because SurfaceCard\nis height: 100% so every Result box lines up across the row. Where a three-line\ncard sits beside one holding two inputs, that trade shows. `align-items: start`\nwas tried and does nothing — the card sizes itself, not the row — and reordering\ncards to balance pixels would break the order they teach in.\n\nFull detail in CHANGELOG.md under 2026-08-21.","tree":{"sha":"ac00d9868d2b6f59aa3e80bf36b548364ba6d684","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/ac00d9868d2b6f59aa3e80bf36b548364ba6d684"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/691c1f2ff298d5f12706830dde27da85f10f21d4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/691c1f2ff298d5f12706830dde27da85f10f21d4","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKDY5MWMxZjJmZjI5OGQ1ZjEyNzA2ODMwZGRlMjdkYTg1ZjEwZjIxZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/14eb8876702b917fc588b0a41f131299973bc751","sha":"14eb8876702b917fc588b0a41f131299973bc751","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/14eb8876702b917fc588b0a41f131299973bc751"}],"sha":"691c1f2ff298d5f12706830dde27da85f10f21d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/691c1f2ff298d5f12706830dde27da85f10f21d4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/14eb8876702b917fc588b0a41f131299973bc751/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T15:28:24Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T15:28:24Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"refactor(playground): drop two duplicate examples, and cut the card prose by a third\n\n/ui-integrations existed to pair each template family against its Material UI\ntwin. With three of the four twins gone, the vanilla halves stopped being halves\nof anything — and measured against the routes that own those subjects, two were\nduplicates outright.\n\n  vanilla-slide    a strict subset of slide-presets: one direction: ''right''\n                   against four directions, align, nonModal and portal\n  vanilla-message  what delete-item-modal already teaches — same useMessageModal,\n                   same action(''cancel'', { hotkey }) beside an async\n                   action(''delete''), same simulateApiCall, same failure alert\n\nThe panel wizard is not a duplicate: it is the only worked example of the\npanel-modal family anywhere, so it moved to /showcases, where a three-step flow\nbelongs. What is left on /ui-integrations is the form pair and nothing else,\nwhich is the page''s whole claim.\n\nThe card descriptions were essays. Measured across every page: 3,130 words, 18 of\nthem over 60 and one at 142. A card is a doorway — it says what you are looking\nat and why to click — and a 142-word paragraph asks the reader to finish the\nlesson before starting it. Rewritten to 2,249 words, longest 60, nothing over 60\nwhere 18 were. The median is unchanged at 32: the short ones were already right\nand were left alone, and what came down is the tail. Nothing was deleted that the\nexample''s own source does not carry, and the code viewer is one click away.\n\nThe same measurement ruled two things out: no sentence appears on more than one\nroute, and no four-word phrase is used three times. The prose was long, not\ncopy-pasted.\n\nFull detail in CHANGELOG.md under 2026-08-21.","tree":{"sha":"4b70a6c6cb4f62dc4bebbca284484b1c945d7a3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/4b70a6c6cb4f62dc4bebbca284484b1c945d7a3d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/14eb8876702b917fc588b0a41f131299973bc751","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/14eb8876702b917fc588b0a41f131299973bc751","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKDE0ZWI4ODc2NzAyYjkxN2ZjNTg4YjBhNDFmMTMxMjk5OTczYmM3NTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/685452872426d53475eca8c17bd3bb63ab68c9bd","sha":"685452872426d53475eca8c17bd3bb63ab68c9bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/685452872426d53475eca8c17bd3bb63ab68c9bd"}],"sha":"14eb8876702b917fc588b0a41f131299973bc751","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/14eb8876702b917fc588b0a41f131299973bc751"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/685452872426d53475eca8c17bd3bb63ab68c9bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T13:10:53Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T13:10:53Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"refactor(playground): /advanced becomes four routes that name what they hold\n\nOne route held a third of the playground — 11 examples and 2,199 lines, in four\nsections that were four unrelated subjects. The size was never the problem.\n\"Advanced\" describes a difficulty rather than a topic, so nothing could ever be\nsaid not to belong there, which is how it filled up and how it would fill up\nagain after any trim.\n\n  /stacking    who is in front, and who owns the keyboard\n  /imperative  opening and rendering from outside the component\n  /interop     foreign observers, and a render with no document\n  /showcases   whole flows, assembled\n\nThree notes on where the lines fell. ModalOutlet went to /imperative rather than\nto a templates page: it is the same decoupling asked about the render instead of\nthe open, and it keeps its own section there. The interop route is not called\n`without-react` — the SSR example runs react-dom/server, so that name would have\nbeen false; what those two share is meeting something that is not your React\ntree. And /microfrontends stays its own route, because the frame is the widest\nthing here and four bindings sharing one registry is a peer of stacking, which\nplayground/CLAUDE.md already argued.\n\n/warzone leaves the sidebar and keeps its route. A menu entry that rewards a\nclick with nothing teaches every visitor that one item is not for them.\n\nNine code samples had stopped being reachable. Cutting Material UI to one pair\ntook MUI_GROUPS down to the surviving family, and the atoms those families used\nwent with it — registered in the viewer, listed on no page, invisible in the way\nthe playground''s own docs warn about. The three the form pair renders are back\nunder the MUI tab; four that render nothing moved to the Shared tab, where the\nrule already put them. 213 registered, 213 reachable.\n\nThe DRY pass mostly did not happen, measured rather than assumed. The\ncreateResultStore + useStore preamble repeats in 17 examples because each is read\nand copied on its own and `useStore` is a library export those files exist to\nshow — the factory''s JSDoc says to call it at module scope for that reason. The\nshell carries 38 inline styles against the examples'' 136, and its most repeated\none appears four times. Removing what is left would buy indirection.\n\nFull detail in CHANGELOG.md under 2026-08-21.","tree":{"sha":"2e32dbd8d34fad69cdd06a036222b894169e717e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/2e32dbd8d34fad69cdd06a036222b894169e717e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/685452872426d53475eca8c17bd3bb63ab68c9bd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/685452872426d53475eca8c17bd3bb63ab68c9bd","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKDY4NTQ1Mjg3MjQyNmQ1MzQ3NWVjYThjMTdiZDNiYjYzYWI2OGM5YmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/3490c61042a9016f7b764e9e9ed8afb5fb851a1f","sha":"3490c61042a9016f7b764e9e9ed8afb5fb851a1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/3490c61042a9016f7b764e9e9ed8afb5fb851a1f"}],"sha":"685452872426d53475eca8c17bd3bb63ab68c9bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/685452872426d53475eca8c17bd3bb63ab68c9bd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/3490c61042a9016f7b764e9e9ed8afb5fb851a1f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T08:23:35Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T08:23:35Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"feat(core): phase on the render args, and the churn it removes\n\nThe render callback decides what is on screen and was the one place unable to\nask whether it still is. `ModalRenderArgs` carries `phase` now, and so does the\nhook return, on both hook bindings — a getter on Solid, like every other live\nvalue.\n\nThis reverses a `no-by-design` in the compatibility matrix, whose reason was\nthat `isVisible` and `isPreparing` are the two answers a caller needs. They are\nnot: `isVisible` is true for `open` and `closing` alike, so nothing but `phase`\nseparates a panel that is leaving from one that is up — and the render callback\ncarried neither of them anyway. The row is `works`, with Solid''s cost kept as a\ncaveat rather than dropped: a `phase` read inside JSX subscribes that expression\nto every transition.\n\nThree playground modals reverted while still on screen. An action stops running\nthe moment its handler resolves, and the panel is painted for the whole exit\nafter that — 18 frames, measured — so \"Publishing…\" became \"Ready to publish\"\nmid-exit and two status lines read Idle against a dialog still up. Two of the\nthree now hold with `phase === ''closing''` and no state at all; the third keeps\none piece, because the header names *which* action ran and a phase cannot say.\n\nThe new test proves the field arrives and agrees with the hook return, and\nclaims no more: `''closing''` has no observable duration in a component test,\ntransitions being off in a harness, so `runCloseSequence` finalizes with no exit\nto wait on. The window is measured in a real browser instead.\n\nMaterial UI is cut to the one pair that carries the claim. Four pairs proved the\nsame thing four times; the form modal is where it is literally true, both files\ncalling one `useForm` and one `useModal` and disagreeing only in markup. The\nmessage, slide and panel twins are gone with the template families only they\nused — 24 files, ~2,000 lines, and the vendor chunk from 273 kB to 225 kB. The\nvanilla panel wizard stays: it is the only worked example of the panel-modal\nfamily anywhere. `focusRingRoom` and `useScrollRegion`''s `regionSx` and\n`scrollbarWidth` do not — every consumer was MUI.\n\nBoth form cards open with the shell''s own button now. A comparison whose two\ncards differ before the modal opens is not making its point; that MUI''s button\ntakes `action()`''s props is proven in the footer, where it matters.\n\nThe oxlint bump brought `react/set-state-in-effect`, red on three effects that\ngenuinely synchronise with an external system — the CSS cascade in one, the\nmanager in two harnesses. Suppressed with reasons, the directive on the line\nimmediately above: a two-line comment between them targets the comment.\n\nFull detail in CHANGELOG.md under 2026-08-21.","tree":{"sha":"9eb3b962615b9e7c754396884ef66671139c3d0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/9eb3b962615b9e7c754396884ef66671139c3d0c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/3490c61042a9016f7b764e9e9ed8afb5fb851a1f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/3490c61042a9016f7b764e9e9ed8afb5fb851a1f","node_id":"C_kwDOTvVQm9oAKDM0OTBjNjEwNDJhOTAxNmY3Yjc2NGU5ZTllZDhhZmI1ZmI4NTFhMWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins/umbra/commit/afc1cc16380f835b22a74c7ec2bc9932989cc35b","sha":"afc1cc16380f835b22a74c7ec2bc9932989cc35b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/afc1cc16380f835b22a74c7ec2bc9932989cc35b"}],"sha":"3490c61042a9016f7b764e9e9ed8afb5fb851a1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/3490c61042a9016f7b764e9e9ed8afb5fb851a1f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/francisdesjardins","id":2743830,"login":"francisdesjardins","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDM4MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/commits/afc1cc16380f835b22a74c7ec2bc9932989cc35b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T07:13:22Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T07:13:22Z","email":"me@francisdesjardins.ca","name":"Francis Desjardins"},"message":"fix(playground): a running Confirm that read as a dead black box\n\nAn action sets `disabled` while it runs, so the vanilla primary button took the\ndisabled chrome — `opacity: 0.5` plus a 50%-alpha fill — while it was busy, not\nunavailable. Composited on `#121212` the amber landed at `#442b0f`, and the\nspinner, drawn in `--color-primary-ink` `#0f172a` because that ink was picked\nagainst the *full* amber, sat on it at roughly 1.3:1. Invisible, on a fill dark\nenough to read as black.\n\nThe dimming splits from the cursor: `not-allowed` stays on every disabled\nbutton, `opacity: 0.5` and the faded fill go to `:not(.loading)`. A running\naction keeps full-strength chrome and the spinner is back at 5.5:1. Measured in\nboth schemes at 390px and 1440px; the genuinely-disabled case still fades.","tree":{"sha":"9e22f7c216dc9f4c51045fc8a766ee3ad428d559","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/trees/9e22f7c216dc9f4c51045fc8a766ee3ad428d559"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francisdesjardins/umbra/git/commits/afc1cc16380f835b22a74c7ec2bc9932989cc35b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2743830?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francisdesjardi