est crossing four\nservices was four unrelated rows in a list and the waterfall stopped at the\nfirst hop. And nothing carried the trace *out* of a service, so past the first\nhop there was usually nothing to read anyway.\n\n**Projects are the services.** One per microservice and per microfrontend, each\nwith its own DSN and issue stream. `trace_sharing` joins them — per project, off\nby default, and only within one organization. Joining is a disclosure: it lets a\ntrace opened in one project show rows belonging to another, and a shared\ninstance where every project was visible from every other by default would be a\ndecision nobody made.\n\n**The trace page assembles the whole request.** Every transaction sharing the id\nfrom every project allowed in, parented by `parent_span_id`, indented by hop.\n\"Where the time went\" totals each service above the waterfall, because the first\nquestion about a slow distributed request is *which one*. A hop whose caller was\nnever instrumented appears at the top level rather than vanishing — a partially\ninstrumented estate is the normal state of one.\n\n**The Python SDK carries the trace out.** `httpx`, `requests` and `urllib` are\npatched at init: an outbound call becomes an `http.client` span and takes the\nheader with it. Nothing is imported to patch it — whatever the process already\nimported gets instrumented, so a service that does not use `requests` does not\npay its import cost. It never traces its own delivery.\n\n**The browser SDK takes several clients on one page.** It was a module\nsingleton, so a second microfrontend''s `init()` silently replaced the first\nteam''s reporting entirely. Now `init()` returns a client; each reports to its own\nproject, and they share the page''s trace, because one page view split into two\nwaterfalls is the problem this feature exists to remove, reproduced inside a\ntab. Network spans and uncaught errors belong to the page''s first client —\nnothing about a fetch or a `window.onerror` says which bundle it came from, and\na stated rule beats a guess. `tracePropagationTargets` names the other origins\nallowed to receive the header.\n\n**One bug the tests could not have found.** Every tree test passed while a real\ntwo-service request rendered flat: a downstream transaction''s `parent_span_id`\nnames the **client span** in the caller, not the caller''s transaction, and the\nindex only held transaction ids. The tests had built the link the way the tree\nwanted rather than the way the wire carries it. Found by running two services\nagainst the stack, and now pinned by a test that constructs the real shape.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"de83c3f66e5fbfcd087d502c89fb19835189eda5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/de83c3f66e5fbfcd087d502c89fb19835189eda5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/6c790ce6be2ff242895ff4726388618fcac05e52","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/6c790ce6be2ff242895ff4726388618fcac05e52","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKDZjNzkwY2U2YmUyZmYyNDI4OTVmZjQ3MjYzODg2MThmY2FjMDVlNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/af15622e0fdcbbfc463d9fcc37b1eb9ff7b6612b","sha":"af15622e0fdcbbfc463d9fcc37b1eb9ff7b6612b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/af15622e0fdcbbfc463d9fcc37b1eb9ff7b6612b"}],"sha":"6c790ce6be2ff242895ff4726388618fcac05e52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/6c790ce6be2ff242895ff4726388618fcac05e52"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/af15622e0fdcbbfc463d9fcc37b1eb9ff7b6612b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T05:59:30Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T05:59:30Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"chore: the demo makes the two new kinds of request\n\nAn XHR button, because that is what axios does and it was the shape the SDK\ncould not see; and three route-change buttons, two of which are navigations and\none of which — the query-string one — deliberately is not.\n\nBoth SDKs pinned to the published 0.3.0 rather than the checkout beside them.\nInstalling from the registry is what proves what somebody following the README\nactually receives; it is how the dropped parent span was found.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"20b24f6bede152878c4b2a8fc6831f94699519ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/20b24f6bede152878c4b2a8fc6831f94699519ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/af15622e0fdcbbfc463d9fcc37b1eb9ff7b6612b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/af15622e0fdcbbfc463d9fcc37b1eb9ff7b6612b","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKGFmMTU2MjJlMGZkY2JiZmM0NjNkOWZjYzM3YjFlYjlmZjdiNjYxMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/f4ccd00c6083b29a501a5193ea65499bc9e3aac5","sha":"f4ccd00c6083b29a501a5193ea65499bc9e3aac5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/f4ccd00c6083b29a501a5193ea65499bc9e3aac5"}],"sha":"af15622e0fdcbbfc463d9fcc37b1eb9ff7b6612b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/af15622e0fdcbbfc463d9fcc37b1eb9ff7b6612b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/f4ccd00c6083b29a501a5193ea65499bc9e3aac5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T05:35:00Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T05:35:00Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"chore: ruff formats the snippets in the README too\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1d6562a035bb8ee3d6a00ed4edf6df99360e8b76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/1d6562a035bb8ee3d6a00ed4edf6df99360e8b76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/f4ccd00c6083b29a501a5193ea65499bc9e3aac5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/f4ccd00c6083b29a501a5193ea65499bc9e3aac5","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKGY0Y2NkMDBjNjA4M2IyOWE1MDFhNTE5M2VhNjU0OTliYzllM2FhYzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/1d3c2ab9a752a46c217c14155f464bd0cd421d9e","sha":"1d3c2ab9a752a46c217c14155f464bd0cd421d9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/1d3c2ab9a752a46c217c14155f464bd0cd421d9e"}],"sha":"f4ccd00c6083b29a501a5193ea65499bc9e3aac5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/f4ccd00c6083b29a501a5193ea65499bc9e3aac5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/1d3c2ab9a752a46c217c14155f464bd0cd421d9e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T05:30:59Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T05:30:59Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"feat: the frameworks that are not FastAPI\n\n**Python was ASGI-only, which is half the language.** Flask and Django-under-\nWSGI could report the errors they caught themselves and nothing else: no\nrequest traces, so no latency, no throughput, and no way for a browser trace to\ncontinue into the server. Three integrations now:\n\n`integrations.wsgi` — every WSGI application, no framework knowledge. It times\nthe response until its iterable is *closed*, not until the callable returns,\nbecause that is when a WSGI response is actually finished; timing the call\nalone reports a streamed response as instant.\n\n`integrations.flask` — its own, rather than pointing Flask at the WSGI\nmiddleware, because from inside the framework the matched rule is available:\n`/orders/<int:id>`, the name the code is written in. Errors come from the\n`got_request_exception` signal — an integration that installs an error handler\nchanges what the application returns, and reporting must not alter behaviour.\n\n`integrations.django` — one middleware covering both its WSGI and ASGI\ndeployments, named by the resolved route, with exceptions taken from\n`process_exception` before Django turns them into a 500.\n\n**And where no framework can name the route, the path has its ids collapsed.**\n`/orders/42` becomes `/orders/{id}`. Previously anything outside Starlette fell\nback to the raw path, which meant one transaction per id ever requested and a\np95 computed over a population of one. A wrong guess merges two endpoints; no\nguess destroys the aggregate.\n\n**The browser was missing the requests axios makes.** XHR is now instrumented\nalongside fetch — same span, same trace header — because a page whose entire\nHTTP layer is invisible looks like a broken SDK rather than an incomplete one.\n\n**And a single-page app reported one transaction per visit.** Every route after\nthe first was invisible, and the one that did arrive carried the duration of\nthe whole session. Route changes now report their own `navigation` transaction\nwith their own trace, ending when the route stops fetching: a navigation has no\nload event, ending it at the URL change would measure nothing, and ending it\nwhen the reader leaves would measure how long they read. A query-string change\nis not a navigation. Errors now carry the trace of the route the reader is on\nrather than a page load an hour earlier.\n\n**The setup page asks which Python, not whether Python.** FastAPI takes a\nmiddleware class, Django a settings entry, Flask a function call — one snippet\nfor all three tells two thirds of readers the SDK is not for them.\n\nAlso: the SDK version had drifted — 0.1.0 in the code while 0.2.0 was on PyPI —\nso every event from the published package named a version that never shipped. A\ntest now holds the three in step.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e2898283d4b479e7ee2ce451398448ebef00ae04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/e2898283d4b479e7ee2ce451398448ebef00ae04"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/1d3c2ab9a752a46c217c14155f464bd0cd421d9e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/1d3c2ab9a752a46c217c14155f464bd0cd421d9e","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKDFkM2MyYWI5YTc1MmE0NmMyMTdjMTQxNTVmNDY0YmQwY2Q0MjFkOWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/8c8b4e4007f7428459d4e041f605b5892d49a218","sha":"8c8b4e4007f7428459d4e041f605b5892d49a218","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/8c8b4e4007f7428459d4e041f605b5892d49a218"}],"sha":"1d3c2ab9a752a46c217c14155f464bd0cd421d9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/1d3c2ab9a752a46c217c14155f464bd0cd421d9e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/8c8b4e4007f7428459d4e041f605b5892d49a218/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T10:44:41Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T10:44:41Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"docs: the journey, and the two questions it kept failing to answer\n\nTwo questions came back often enough to be a symptom rather than a query:\n*why does creating a project ask about an organization instead of a language*,\nand *does the Python SDK only work with FastAPI*. Both are journey problems, so\nthis writes the journey down — docs/user-journey.md, first run to first insight\n— and then fixes what walking it exposed.\n\n**The organization question is gone when there is one organization.** It is not\na choice, it is a question with one answer, and it made the first thing anybody\nmeets a concept they do not have yet. Two or more and it comes back, because\nthen it is a real decision.\n\n**The language question was never asked, and the absence needed saying.** Every\nother tool asks for a platform on this form, so its silence read as an\nomission. A project holds an application, not a runtime — the React page and\nthe Python service behind it must share a project or trace_id cannot join them\n— so the form now says one project takes every tier of one application, and\nthat the snippets come next. The platform is observed from what reports rather\nthan declared, because a project that claims Python and receives nothing is a\nlie the UI has to keep telling.\n\n**The setup page now states what each SDK does not fit.** \"Works with FastAPI\"\nreads as \"works with Python\", and somebody on Flask finds out by installing it.\nEach tier carries Fits and Not yet, and Not yet is the same size as Fits rather\nthan small print: WSGI has no middleware; outside Starlette transactions are\nnamed by raw path so /orders/41 and /orders/42 do not group; XHR is not\npatched, so axios in its default transport is invisible; an SPA reports one\ntransaction per page load, not per route.\n\nThose gaps are now `feat/sdk-frameworks` on the roadmap, which is ordered by\nwhich journey step somebody is stuck on rather than by feature list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"41c9c97390f51629518badcd559f1b4bb9177bb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/41c9c97390f51629518badcd559f1b4bb9177bb7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/8c8b4e4007f7428459d4e041f605b5892d49a218","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.gi