owers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/ae7b4802a8a04f922ea277554d4b08ccef73b569/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T18:15:39Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T18:15:39Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"fix: the suspect flag was clipped off the edge of its own column\n\nThe section landed in the 300px aside beside Latest event and Tags, and a\nfour-column table does not survive there — the difference, which is the entire\npoint of the section, was cut off the right edge.\n\nOne block per flag instead, with the comparison read as a sentence: the name\nand the gap on one line, \"on in 100% of 9 here · 23% elsewhere\" beneath it. A\ngap of 20 points or more is coloured, so the suspect is findable without\nreading both rows.\n\nFound by looking at it in a browser. The tests passed either way — they assert\nthe numbers are present, and none of them can see that a column is off-screen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"aca294723a0ba8377d261c8b0607e7e8fafbce44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/aca294723a0ba8377d261c8b0607e7e8fafbce44"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/ae7b4802a8a04f922ea277554d4b08ccef73b569","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/ae7b4802a8a04f922ea277554d4b08ccef73b569","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKGFlN2I0ODAyYThhMDRmOTIyZWEyNzc1NTRkNGIwOGNjZWY3M2I1Njk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/ff7745bf310891274005308368aada956c828fc2","sha":"ff7745bf310891274005308368aada956c828fc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/ff7745bf310891274005308368aada956c828fc2"}],"sha":"ae7b4802a8a04f922ea277554d4b08ccef73b569","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/ae7b4802a8a04f922ea277554d4b08ccef73b569"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/ff7745bf310891274005308368aada956c828fc2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T18:05:18Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T18:05:18Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"fix: a new project could not receive anything\n\nThree findings from starting the stack on an empty volume, which is the one\npath never exercised by developing against a database that already has\neverything in it.\n\n**A project was created without an ingest key.** Neither the API nor the UI\nminted one, so a new project was a row that looked finished and did nothing —\nand the next step, wiring up an SDK, had no DSN to paste. Every project is now\nborn with one, named \"Default\" so it is obvious it can be replaced: rotation\nmeans issue new, migrate clients, revoke old, and that is easier to start from\nan example than from nothing.\n\n**The demo called an SDK method that was not published.** `obsly.set_flag`\nmerged with the feature-flags work, the demo installs `obsly` from PyPI, and\nPyPI was at 0.1.1 — so 49 events arrived as `AttributeError: module ''obsly'' has\nno attribute ''set_flag''` instead of the flag evaluations they were meant to\ncarry. Published as 0.2.0, and the demo now requires it.\n\nThat is the second time installing from the registry rather than the path has\ncaught something the monorepo hid. The first was a dropped parent span.\n\n**The demo now evaluates flags**, so the suspect ranking has something real to\nrank rather than a fixture. A rollout at 25%, with the payment failure only on\nthe new path:\n\n    ConnectionError: payments.example.com returned 502\n      new-checkout   on in  100% of these vs  23% elsewhere   +77 pts\n      dark-mode      on in   56% of these vs  45% elsewhere   +10 pts\n\nThe first is the answer. The second is the control, and it ranking low is what\nsays the first means something.\n\nFirst-run registration was verified on the same empty volume: the form opened\non register, a weak password was refused with the validator''s own sentence, the\naccount created owns the install, and a second attempt got 403.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e3cf6850a949becf49cf6f80fbc5a65b442fc1e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/e3cf6850a949becf49cf6f80fbc5a65b442fc1e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/ff7745bf310891274005308368aada956c828fc2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_ad