":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-12T11:09:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/82c97af8d281490af453ef930d90274596f6bc3e","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKDgyYzk3YWY4ZDI4MTQ5MGFmNDUzZWY5MzBkOTAyNzQ1OTZmNmJjM2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/d1125b98a9ab03712f458260b102349447027abe","sha":"d1125b98a9ab03712f458260b102349447027abe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/d1125b98a9ab03712f458260b102349447027abe"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/663c087cd655972b36b223e24fce8ee8b2003084","sha":"663c087cd655972b36b223e24fce8ee8b2003084","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/663c087cd655972b36b223e24fce8ee8b2003084"}],"sha":"82c97af8d281490af453ef930d90274596f6bc3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/82c97af8d281490af453ef930d90274596f6bc3e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/663c087cd655972b36b223e24fce8ee8b2003084/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T10:59:00Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T10:59:00Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"feat: feature flags, and which one an issue implicates\n\nFR-CTX-8. Evaluated flag values captured on the event, and correlated so that\n\"is this only happening to people with X on?\" is answerable.\n\nRecording the flags is the easy half and on its own it is a list nobody reads.\nBoth halves of a rollout have a flag on; the question is which one is unusual\n*here*. So the issue page ranks each flag by how much more often it was on\ninside that issue than across the rest of the project:\n\n    new-checkout   100.0% here vs   6.8% elsewhere   +93 pts\n    dark-mode       45.0% here vs  49.4% elsewhere    -4 pts\n\nThe first is a suspect. The second is a flag that is on, which is a different\nthing, and a page that ranked by \"was it on\" would have put them side by side.\n\nThree judgements the ranking depends on:\n\n**No baseline is not a zero baseline.** A flag nobody else reported cannot be\ncompared, and scoring it against an assumed zero would rank the least-known\nflag highest — exactly backwards. It is kept and sorted last, because \"we\ncannot tell yet\" is a different answer from \"not implicated\".\n\n**Below five events there is no ranking at all.** Three failures that happen to\nshare a flag is a coincidence, and presenting it as a suspect sends somebody to\nrevert the wrong thing.\n\n**A non-boolean is dropped, never coerced.** A flag is a decision the\napplication already made; turning \"yes\" into True records an outcome nobody\nchose and then counts it as evidence.\n\nBoth SDKs gain the call, and it goes at the point of evaluation rather than\nreading the flag service back later — those differ exactly when it matters,\nduring a rollout. The log is ordered and bounded: re-evaluating moves a flag to\nthe end because the last decision is the one the code acted on, and the oldest\nis dropped at the limit because the newest is the evaluation closest to the\nfailure.\n\nThe roadmap was nine PRs stale and tracked branches rather than coverage. It\nnow carries both, including the sections with nothing behind them — source\nmaps, query language, teams, quotas, uptime, replay, profiling, user feedback —\nso the gap is a fact rather than a feeling.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7fe3d60fb22a01f3ebfbe594b2d2b62a2bc198f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/7fe3d60fb22a01f3ebfbe594b2d2b62a2bc198f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/663c087cd655972b36b223e24fce8ee8b2003084","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/