users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/7e412ff2c39d5977e3fd1c016d8de590bad187ba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T09:58:49Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T09:58:49Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"chore: publish as obsly-browser, since npm blocks the obsly scope\n\nnpm refused the `obsly` organisation name. Not a squatter — the package name\n`obsly` is free and no user account holds it — so it is npm''s own\nsimilar-name rule, which nothing on our side can satisfy.\n\nUnscoped `obsly-browser` reads naturally beside `obsly` on PyPI and leaves\n`obsly-node` and `obsly-react` available for the same family. Both are free\ntoday; a personal scope would have tied the package to a username and made any\nlater transfer a republish under a different name.\n\n`publishConfig.access` goes with the scope. It exists because a scoped package\ndefaults to restricted; an unscoped one is public by construction, so the field\nwould imply a decision nobody made.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b04f0e2d81f0f59358b9bcbc200cb0bf363fa6de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/b04f0e2d81f0f59358b9bcbc200cb0bf363fa6de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/7e412ff2c39d5977e3fd1c016d8de590bad187ba","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq0