},"message":"feat: web vitals with the distribution behind the score\n\nA p75 is one point on a distribution. Two sites can share it while a completely\ndifferent share of visitors is having a bad time, and the share is the number\nthat says how many people that is.\n\nThe demo data makes the case immediately: LCP scores \"poor\", and 68% of visits\nwere good. The problem is real and it is 31% of visits, not everyone — which is\na different conversation with a different urgency, and the single number could\nnot tell them apart.\n\nThe middle band is the remainder between the two edges rather than a third\nthreshold, so a visit can never fall into no band at all.\n\nEach vital also carries a p75 per bucket. A score is a snapshot; whether it is\ndrifting is a different question and the only one that says whether the last\ndeploy made it worse. Empty buckets are null rather than zero — drawing an hour\nwith no page loads as zero renders an outage as a perfect score.\n\nAnd the slowest individual page loads, each opening its trace. Every other\nnumber on the page is an aggregate, and an aggregate cannot be debugged; at\nsome point you need one slow load and the request behind it.\n\nThe stylesheet check earned its place again: `.bands__part` had three modifiers\ndefined and no block rule, so the segments were relying entirely on an inline\nflex-grow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"91827f377d5a7dae2d911853ecc197b2dfe2264c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/91827f377d5a7dae2d911853ecc197b2dfe2264c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/9f469b86edf426919e3b9aa80575bee49adbb7ea","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/9f469b86edf426919e3b9aa80575bee49adbb7ea","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKDlmNDY5Yjg2ZWRmNDI2OTE5ZTNiOWFhODA1NzViZWU0OWFkYmI3ZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/3fb535551d2e70a1214294ce2c616bf79f6daf8a","sha":"3fb535551d2e70a1214294ce2c616bf79f6daf8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/3fb535551d2e70a1214294ce2c616bf79f6daf8a"}],"sha":"9f469b86edf426919e3b9aa80575bee49adbb7ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/9f469b86edf426919e3b9aa80575bee49adbb7ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/3fb535551d2e70a1214294ce2c616bf79f6daf8a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T06:00:10Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T06:00:10Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"feat: a database page that answers the question the ranking provokes\n\nThe Spans page ranked queries by total time and stopped there. Ranking by total\ntime surfaces the query that runs constantly; the query that is individually\npainful is a different statement with a different fix — an index rather than a\ncache — and a page that shows one ranking and calls it \"top queries\" sends\npeople to fix the wrong thing.\n\nBoth rankings, side by side, each saying which fix it implies. On the demo data\nthey agree at the top and disagree immediately below it: `orders` is the third\nmost expensive statement and does not appear in the slowest five at all.\n\nCalls-per-request gets its own section, because the N+1 signature is invisible\nin either ranking. Each call is fast — that is exactly why the pattern survives\nreview — and the number that gives it away is how many of them happen inside\none request. The recoverable figure is every call after the first at the cost\nof a call, not the whole total, because collapsing the loop still leaves one\nquery to run.\n\nA p95 line over the window, because a single number cannot say whether it is\ngetting worse.\n\nAnd a rollup per table: a statement is the unit you fix, but a table is the\nunit you reason about when deciding where an index goes. The table name is read\nout of the statement, and anything unrecognised is left out rather than\nguessed — a wrong table name sends somebody to index the wrong thing, which\ncosts more than the row being absent.\n\nVerified against the running stack:\n\n    queries=440  per_request=3.1x  total=11751ms  p95=18.4ms\n\n    slowest (by p95):        1123.3ms  analytics_rollup\n    heaviest (by total):     9045.5ms  analytics_rollup\n                              607.6ms  orders          <- not in the slowest five\n    called once per row:     25.0x  recoverable 583ms  SELECT total FROM orders\n\nThe Spans page is deleted rather than left beside this one. It answered a\nstrictly smaller question and would have been a second place to look with a\nthird of the information.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"85042ffafa74bc5986beee0020f8efecbdf738da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/85042ffafa74bc5986beee0020f8efecbdf738da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/3fb535551d2e70a1214294ce2c616bf79f6daf8a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a