w/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/8f353d2f00eb4b9b97d7dfcbfb5481cdac6ea086","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKDhmMzUzZDJmMDBlYjRiOWI5N2Q3ZGZjYmZiNTQ4MWNkYWM2ZWEwODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/a7265380a46f9befea49989ff25e00c782b2e085","sha":"a7265380a46f9befea49989ff25e00c782b2e085","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/a7265380a46f9befea49989ff25e00c782b2e085"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/9eb5d6dc9eb16ee080d615d6bb0cdf7463b08887","sha":"9eb5d6dc9eb16ee080d615d6bb0cdf7463b08887","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/9eb5d6dc9eb16ee080d615d6bb0cdf7463b08887"}],"sha":"8f353d2f00eb4b9b97d7dfcbfb5481cdac6ea086","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/8f353d2f00eb4b9b97d7dfcbfb5481cdac6ea086"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/9eb5d6dc9eb16ee080d615d6bb0cdf7463b08887/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T05:36:13Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T05:36:13Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"feat: controls that belong here, and traces that group their repeats\n\nThree things you pointed at, and one of them was mine twice over.\n\n**The dropdowns.** Control styling was scoped to `.filters`, so every select\noutside that one wrapper — the whole page-filter bar, the alert rule form —\nrendered as a raw OS widget: Arial, the platform''s grey, and a border matching\nnothing on the page. On a dark background that is not a small difference, it is\na control that looks like it belongs to a different application.\n\nThe rules are global now, and the platform''s arrow is replaced with one drawn\nfrom currentColor so it follows the theme. The element itself is untouched:\nsame keyboard behaviour, same OS popup on mobile, same screen-reader semantics.\nA custom listbox would let the open panel be styled too, and would also mean\nrebuilding focus, type-ahead and touch behaviour the native element already\ngets right.\n\n**The tables.** Already fixed in #37 — you were looking at a stale build. The\n`.table` rules landed with that PR and the container had not been rebuilt.\n\n**The spans.** They were not grouped because nothing grouped them. Now a run of\nidentical spans collapses to one row saying how many and how much, and opens to\nshow each call. A request issuing the same query twenty-five times rendered\ntwenty-five near-identical bars and pushed the one interesting span off the\nscreen — and the repetition is itself the finding, which is what the collapsed\nrow states outright.\n\nOnly consecutive spans group. Two runs of the same query either side of an HTTP\ncall are two different events in the request''s story, and merging them across\nthe thing between them would hide the ordering that explains it.\n\nTimestamps on every call, two readings: the offset says where in the request it\nhappened, the clock time lines it up against a log line. That clock time needed\nmillisecond precision — a request finishing in 61ms rendered twenty-five rows\nall stamped with the same second, which reads as broken timestamps rather than\na fast request.\n\nTraces also say which tier they came from. A browser page load and a server\nrequest sat unlabelled in one list sorted by duration, so every page load\nfloated to the top — they are seconds, requests are milliseconds — and it read\nas the backend having got dramatically slower. A trace with no spans now says\n\"nothing instrumented\" rather than \"0 spans\", because those are the browser\npageloads and the count was describing an absence, not a measurement.\n\nTwo bugs of my own found on the way: the group key carried a position suffix\nfor React and was then compared against itself, so nothing ever grouped; and\nthe count rendered as two adjacent text nodes, which a screen reader announces\nseparately and no matcher can see.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d10d96d1ae1a3b427f9e06c0f32fd18f21f11721","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/d10d96d1ae1a3b427f9e06c0f32fd18f21f11721"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/9eb5d6dc9eb16ee080d615d6bb0cdf7463b08887","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.gith