tps://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/48dca50ae88025c158ad01841eb3207e9dbcab71"}],"sha":"a7265380a46f9befea49989ff25e00c782b2e085","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/a7265380a46f9befea49989ff25e00c782b2e085"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/48dca50ae88025c158ad01841eb3207e9dbcab71/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T04:48:54Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T04:48:54Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"feat: a shell that groups the product instead of listing it\n\nTen horizontal tabs with no way to group them, so Spans and Settings sat at the\nsame level and read as equally important. It had run out of room, and the next\nfour pages had nowhere to go.\n\nNavigation moves to a persistent sidebar, grouped by the question each page\nanswers rather than by the table it reads from. Explore is \"show me the\nrecords\" — traces, logs. Insights is \"how is this layer doing\", one page per\ntier of the stack, because a slow checkout is a browser problem, a handler\nproblem or a query problem and those are three different people''s afternoons.\n\nWeb Vitals, Performance and Spans become Frontend, Backend and Database, and\nCache joins them. The old paths redirect rather than 404, so a bookmark or a\nlink in an old incident channel still lands where it meant to.\n\nThe Database page is scoped to db spans and the Cache page to cache spans. A\nnav item called Database that lists http.client makes the whole grouping a lie.\n\nFilters move to one bar above every page instead of a period picker inside each\none. The window is a property of the question, not of the page you happen to be\non, and losing it on the way between pages is how an investigation stalls. It\nwrites to the URL, which every page already read, so the link somebody pastes\ninto a channel carries the window they were looking at.\n\nLanding goes to Issues, the way Sentry lands. The question you open an\nobservability tool to ask is what is broken, not what the averages are.\n\n\"Acme\" is retired. It was a placeholder invented when there was nothing else to\ncall the tenant, and a fake company name in the corner of every page reads as\nsomebody else''s account — the first thing it makes a person do is ask what it\nis, which is exactly what happened. The organisation is now a quiet label with\nan endpoint to rename it, and only an organisation that was never renamed is\ntouched by the migration.\n\nAlso fixes a defect that had been shipping since #32: Alerts, Releases, Web\nVitals and Cache all referenced `.page-head`, `.page-head__sub` and `.table`,\nand none of them existed. Those pages rendered with browser defaults — a 32px\nheading and a borderless table — while every test passed, because no test can\nsee a stylesheet. A missing class is silent by construction, so there is now a\nmechanical check that every className in the tsx resolves to a selector this\nstylesheet defines. It found all nine, plus `.spark`, which had been undefined\nsince the sparkline was written.\n\nThe Impeccable detector flagged two side-tab accent borders. Both are gone\nrather than suppressed: the web vitals rating now colours the measurement it\nrates, next to a badge that already names the band in words, and the inline\nnote uses a tinted ground instead of a stripe down one edge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1d64da8284d8e2f13f1d1df6e3c0b8ab5a086907","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/1d64da8284d8e2f13f1d1df6e3c0b8ab5a086907"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/48dca50ae88025c158ad01841eb3207e9dbcab71","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/48dca50ae88025c158ad01841eb3207e9dbcab71","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKDQ4ZGNhNTBhZTg4MDI1YzE1OGFkMDE4NDFlYjMyMDdlOWRiY2FiNzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/432caf21b6