","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/0f72f879cf352224171ef12e2897ae2a9cdafcad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T01:03:38Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T01:03:38Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"feat: release health — did the thing we shipped make it worse?\n\n`release` was already on every event, transaction and log. Nothing aggregated\nby it, so the tags answered no question. Every version is now a row, which is\nthe point: a bad deploy has to sit next to the good one it replaced rather than\nbeing averaged into it.\n\nIssues record the release they were first seen in, captured once at creation.\nIt is derivable from an issue''s earliest event, but only by sorting every event\nin the group — and \"what did this deploy break?\" is asked of the whole issue\ntable at once, which is exactly the scan a stored column exists to avoid.\n\nThat question is also different from \"what is broken?\", and only the first one\ntells you whether to roll back.\n\nThe number is called failure-free *requests*, not crash-free sessions. Sentry''s\ncrash-free rate is measured over sessions, which need their own protocol and\ntheir own storage. Borrowing the name for a request-based number would be worse\nthan not having it: people compare crash-free rates between tools, and they\nwould be comparing two different measurements every time. Adoption is share of\ntraffic in the window for the same reason — without sessions there is no honest\nway to state installed base, and how much traffic a version served is a fact we\ndo have.\n\nThe migration backfills first_release from each issue''s earliest event. Without\nit every historical issue shows a blank origin and the page reports \"0 issues\nintroduced\" for every past version — which is not missing data, it is missing\ndata that reads as good news. One UPDATE with a correlated subquery rather than\na loop, because this runs against a table that may already hold millions of\nrows.\n\nPerformance issues stay blank and say so: a detector files them from a\ntransaction, so they have no events to read a release from. New ones take it\nfrom the transaction; historical ones are left honestly empty rather than\nguessed at.\n\nVerified against the live stack:\n\n    version                    reqs  fail-free  errors   new  open\n    obsly-demo-shop@1.0.0         1    100.00%       1     1     1\n    obsly-demo@1.3.0            309     55.34%     168     8     8\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"87c46c532dc11db2f64e9cfd570e19226e74cab6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/87c46c532dc11db2f64e9cfd570e19226e74cab6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/0f72f879cf352224171ef12e2897ae2a9cdafcad","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","sit