nts{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/26d3bf395409e1fb5ed4ea966f451e4d4e740e2d","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKDI2ZDNiZjM5NTQwOWUxZmI1ZWQ0ZWE5NjZmNDUxZTRkNGU3NDBlMmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/2272d31e79c68d8327e8a6d5ed1d80e19651c18d","sha":"2272d31e79c68d8327e8a6d5ed1d80e19651c18d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/2272d31e79c68d8327e8a6d5ed1d80e19651c18d"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/207c12b4506c7010f212006fe20eea8c3014008c","sha":"207c12b4506c7010f212006fe20eea8c3014008c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/207c12b4506c7010f212006fe20eea8c3014008c"}],"sha":"26d3bf395409e1fb5ed4ea966f451e4d4e740e2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/26d3bf395409e1fb5ed4ea966f451e4d4e740e2d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/207c12b4506c7010f212006fe20eea8c3014008c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T00:44:07Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T00:44:07Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"feat: a demo page that reports itself, and a package that actually loads\n\nTwo things, both about the browser SDK being real rather than merely merged.\n\n**The package did not load.** TypeScript emits `import { parseDsn } from ''./dsn''`\nwith no extension, which typechecks, builds cleanly, and is then rejected by\nevery browser and by Node — only a bundler resolves it. The package declares\n`\"type\": \"module\"` and ships raw ESM, so it was broken in exactly the\nenvironment it exists for, and nothing in CI noticed because nothing in CI ever\nloaded the built artifact. Imports now carry `.js`, and CI imports `dist` and\nasserts `init` is there.\n\n**Nothing used it.** The Web Vitals page could only ever be empty, which makes\nit impossible to tell a working feature from a broken one. `/shop` on the demo\napp is a page that reports itself: traced requests into the FastAPI backend,\nthree kinds of browser error, and buttons that deliberately shift the layout and\nblock the main thread so CLS and INP are numbers rather than zeros.\n\nIt is served from the same origin as the API it calls, which is the condition\nfor attaching a trace header without turning every request into a preflighted\none — the demo demonstrates the constraint as well as the feature.\n\nVerified by driving the built SDK''s own transport against the running stack,\nrather than a payload written by hand for the occasion:\n\n    status       : 200\n    CORS         : *\n    server said  : {\"accepted\":2,\"rejected\":[]}\n\nand then reading back what landed:\n\n    pageload   /shop  op=pageload  release=obsly-demo-shop@1.0.0  2400ms\n       └─ http.client  GET /checkout/c-1        600ms\n       measurements: cls=0.142 fcp=640 inp=412 lcp=1980 ttfb=210\n\n    error: TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading ''checkout'')\n      platform=javascript  issue=12  release=obsly-demo-shop@1.0.0\n      frame: onClick at http://127.0.0.1:8200/shop:157 in_app=True\n      correlated with the page load by trace_id: True\n\nThe in-page path — PerformanceObserver, the error handlers, sendBeacon on tab\nhide — has no headless browser available here and was not exercised\nautomatically. Its logic is covered by the jsdom tests; the wiring is what a\nclick on /shop confirms.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b25ee830ab21b3c839e48d9922508e785a21c2da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/b25ee830ab21b3c839e48d9922508e785a21c2da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/207c12b4506c7010f212006fe20eea8c3014008c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","ht