/wGlKkXoqEjnccvTWidW0i3yqpYG6iRfyT8Ej9UMtt/\nvcg9mUKzx2BK/24xyv52\n=bIjs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-12T00:42:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/2272d31e79c68d8327e8a6d5ed1d80e19651c18d","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKDIyNzJkMzFlNzljNjhkODMyN2U4YTZkNWVkMWQ4MGUxOTY1MWMxOGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/590e68e1c4af5167be36b190eb157dca0d1df62d","sha":"590e68e1c4af5167be36b190eb157dca0d1df62d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/590e68e1c4af5167be36b190eb157dca0d1df62d"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/2b6c2d731e28c418d61e03c7af1857e7a4c59911","sha":"2b6c2d731e28c418d61e03c7af1857e7a4c59911","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/2b6c2d731e28c418d61e03c7af1857e7a4c59911"}],"sha":"2272d31e79c68d8327e8a6d5ed1d80e19651c18d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/2272d31e79c68d8327e8a6d5ed1d80e19651c18d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/2b6c2d731e28c418d61e03c7af1857e7a4c59911/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T00:33:43Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T00:33:43Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"feat: browser SDK — errors, web vitals, one trace from paint to query\n\nEverything so far was backend-only. An error in the browser and the request it\nmade were two unrelated facts, and the slowest part of most applications — the\npart the reader actually waits for — was not measured at all.\n\nThe browser SDK puts an `obsly-trace` header on same-origin requests and the\nPython SDK already reads it, so one waterfall now holds the whole story:\n\n    pageload     /checkout               2000.0ms   (root)\n        └─ http.client  POST /api/checkout           900.0ms\n    http.server  POST /api/checkout       700.0ms   parent = that span\n        └─ db.query     SELECT * FROM carts …        400.0ms\n\nVerified end to end against the running stack, including that the backend\ntransaction''s parent is the browser''s own fetch span rather than a coincidence\nof timestamps.\n\nWeb vitals are aggregated the way the standard defines them, because these are\nthe numbers a team gets judged on publicly:\n\n- p75, not the mean. On a distribution with a slow tail the mean reads as\n  healthy while a quarter of visits are not.\n- The thresholds are the Web Vitals definition''s, not ours. A tool that invents\n  its own bands cannot be compared against anything else anyone reads.\n- A vital nobody reported shows as \"no data\", never as a passing score. Green\n  because nothing was measured is the most dangerous reading such a page gives.\n- Pages are ranked by p75 LCP rather than by traffic; ranking by traffic just\n  repeats the traffic report.\n- Browser and backend transactions are never mixed. A server request has no\n  layout shift, and averaging the two populations describes neither.\n\nThree constraints shaped the SDK:\n\n**It must not be able to break the page.** Zero runtime dependencies, enforced\nin CI the same way the Python SDK''s are. Every observer, parse and send is\nwrapped — a reporting tool that takes down the thing it observes has done more\nharm than the bug it was reporting.\n\n**Third-party requests are left alone by default.** Adding a header to another\norigin''s endpoint turns a simple request into a preflighted one, and breaking\nsomebody''s payment provider to draw a nicer waterfall is the wrong trade.\n\n**Vitals report on visibilitychange, not unload.** On mobile a tab is often\nfrozen without ever firing unload, and those page loads would simply never be\nmeasured. sendBeacon survives the page going away.\n\nIngest gains CORS, without which no browser could reach the endpoint at all —\nand unlike a server SDK there is no way for the page to work around it. Every\nresponse carries the headers, including the rejections: without them the\nbrowser discards a response it did receive, and the page cannot tell a bad key\nfrom an outage.\n\nAlso fixes a real ingest bug the vitals tests surfaced. Python''s JSON parser\naccepts `NaN`, `Infinity` and `-Infinity` as bare tokens; Postgres rejects them\nand the payload is stored verbatim, so six characters from a hostile client\nturned the whole request into a 500. They are not JSON, so they are now\nrejected like any other malformed payload — and an item carrying one no longer\ncosts the good item beside it in the same envelope.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0c5873fcd81f7d4a68d406a1b46bbec6ab5e1a95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/0c5873fcd81f7d4a68d406a1b46bbec6ab5e1a95"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/2b6c2d731e28c418d61e03c7af1857e7a4c59911","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/2b6c2d731e28c418d61e03c7af1857e7a4c59911","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKDJiNmMyZDczMWUyOGM0MThkNjFlMDNjN2FmMTg1N2U3YTRjNTk5MTE","paren