q01/obsly/commit/ae22cb2f5f6cf6132eb3edde77a8380f573aa6b6","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKGFlMjJjYjJmNWY2Y2Y2MTMyZWIzZWRkZTc3YTgzODBmNTczYWE2YjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/a0b216a283a9c0ea2fa8c8a189896bf12e0e99c5","sha":"a0b216a283a9c0ea2fa8c8a189896bf12e0e99c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/a0b216a283a9c0ea2fa8c8a189896bf12e0e99c5"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/c58133dce4cdc660ca136b01a5286e8cd1f26a41","sha":"c58133dce4cdc660ca136b01a5286e8cd1f26a41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/c58133dce4cdc660ca136b01a5286e8cd1f26a41"}],"sha":"ae22cb2f5f6cf6132eb3edde77a8380f573aa6b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/ae22cb2f5f6cf6132eb3edde77a8380f573aa6b6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/c58133dce4cdc660ca136b01a5286e8cd1f26a41/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T19:35:36Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T19:35:36Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"feat: redact secrets server-side, before anything is written\n\nAnswering \"how does Sentry handle secrets in logs\". It does it in two layers,\nand we only had the weaker one.\n\nThe SDK strips what it knows about — Authorization headers, cookies, query\nstrings. That only covers what the SDK can see coming. This is the half that\nmatters:\n\n- Logs carry arbitrary logging.getLogger() output. An application writing\n  log.info(\"auth failed for token=%s\", token) puts that token in our database,\n  and no client-side setting prevents it.\n- An old SDK cannot be upgraded retroactively; a rule added here protects every\n  client that already shipped.\n- Anything scrubbed after storage was still stored.\n\nIt runs before normalisation, so the verbatim payload column is covered too —\nscrubbing only the extracted columns would leave the secret in the row anyway.\nOn by default, because an installation that has to remember to turn scrubbing\non is one that stores a credential the first time somebody forgets.\n\nKeys are matched on word parts plus separator-collapsed compounds, so one rule\ncovers api_key, apiKey, api-key and X-Api-Key. Values are matched by shape —\nJWTs, GitHub and Slack tokens, AWS key ids, PEM blocks, bearer headers — since\nthe shape is the giveaway whatever the key is called. Card numbers are checked\nwith Luhn first, because an order id of card length is not a card and a\nscrubber that blanks ordinary ids is one people turn off.\n\nA code review found five defects, and every one of them needed reading rather\nthan running:\n\n- The card pattern matched all-digit 16-character hex span ids. \"4000000000000010\"\n  became \"[card]\", the hex validator then dropped it to empty, and every child\n  span was orphaned — roughly one span id in fourteen thousand, silently.\n  Structural identifiers are now never value-scrubbed.\n- The depth limit failed open: at the boundary the subtree was returned\n  untouched, so a password nested thirteen levels deep was stored verbatim. A\n  deny-by-default scrubber whose deepest branch is allow-by-default is not\n  deny-by-default. It redacts at the limit now.\n- The sk- pattern required contiguous alphanumerics, so modern sk-proj- and\n  sk-svcacct- keys passed through untouched.\n- Secret-named keys replaced whole containers, and substring matching hit\n  \"author\" and \"oauth_provider\". Containers are now redacted leaf by leaf, and\n  matching is on word parts.\n- The Luhn guard was selected by \"is this the last pattern in the list\", so\n  appending any new rule would have silently turned the card rule into an\n  unconditional substitution that blanked every long number.\n\nSeven regression tests cover them.\n\n296 backend tests. Verified against the running stack with real secret formats:\n\n  body      : auth failed token=[jwt] card=[card]\n  attributes: {''api_key'': ''[redacted]'', ''order_id'': ''1234567890123456''}\n\nThe order id is Luhn-invalid and sixteen digits long, and it survived — which\nis the property that decides whether anybody leaves this switched on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fb489ecfb6fba3b96b6b0aae146ca5f7448c71e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/fb489ecfb6fba3b96b6b0aae146ca5f7448c71e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/c58133dce4cdc660ca136b01a5286e8cd1f26a41","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/c58133dce4cdc660ca136b01a5286e8cd1f26a41","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKGM1ODEzM2RjZTRjZGM2NjBjYTEzNmIwMWE1Mjg2ZThjZDFmMjZhNDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/a0b216a283a9c0ea2fa8c8a189896bf12e0e99c5","sha":"a0b216a283a9c0ea2fa8c8a189896bf12e0e99c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/a0b216a283a9c0ea2fa8c8a189896bf12e0e99c5"}],"sha":"c58133dce4cdc660ca136b01a5286e8cd1f26a41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/c58133dce4cdc660ca136b01a5286e8cd1f26a41"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.co