YlbcKP7I\nhNjuJsReI4ePHb1RQsk2\n=ecme\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-11T22:02:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/a0b216a283a9c0ea2fa8c8a189896bf12e0e99c5","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKGEwYjIxNmEyODNhOWMwZWEyZmE4YzhhMTg5ODk2YmYxMmUwZTk5YzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/2cb1ac58bb3b753539e8eab2aad07f32be85973d","sha":"2cb1ac58bb3b753539e8eab2aad07f32be85973d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/2cb1ac58bb3b753539e8eab2aad07f32be85973d"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/18c01e9fb84e28be6c3d3abe66550c4e787d1f7f","sha":"18c01e9fb84e28be6c3d3abe66550c4e787d1f7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/18c01e9fb84e28be6c3d3abe66550c4e787d1f7f"}],"sha":"a0b216a283a9c0ea2fa8c8a189896bf12e0e99c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/a0b216a283a9c0ea2fa8c8a189896bf12e0e99c5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/18c01e9fb84e28be6c3d3abe66550c4e787d1f7f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T19:18:23Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T19:18:23Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"feat: ranked charts, and a way back out of every detail page\n\nNavigation first, because the symptom was concrete: a trace had no back link\nat all. The only exit was the browser button, and a page you can only leave\nthat way feels like a dead end whether or not it technically is one.\n\nEvery detail page now carries a breadcrumb trail — Traces / this trace,\nIssues / this issue, Spans / this statement. The current page is named but not\nlinked, because a link to where you already are is a dead control, and one\ndead control teaches people the whole trail is decorative. Settings used to\nsay \"back to issues\" regardless of where you came from, which is a trail that\ntells you something untrue.\n\nA project switcher sits in the tab bar and keeps you on the same tab. Being\nthrown back to a list every time you compare two services is the friction that\nmakes people stop comparing.\n\nThen charts. Endpoints and spans each get a ranked horizontal bar chart above\ntheir table, ranked by whatever the table is sorted by — a chart and a table\nthat disagree about the same window is worse than either alone. Horizontal\nbecause the labels are SQL statements and route patterns: text that needs a\nline of its own, not a rotated tick. One series, one colour, since ranking by\na single measure and colouring each bar differently would double-encode length\nas hue. The caption says what a bar length means rather than implying it, and\na truncated list says how many it cut — a top-8 that looks like the whole list\nlies by omission.\n\nFour defects came out of a code review, and all four were things tests were\nnever going to catch:\n\n- The project switcher carried the whole sub-path, so /projects/1/issues/9\n  became /projects/2/issues/9 — project 1''s issue rendered under project 2''s\n  header — and a span link lost the query string that identifies which span it\n  is. Only the tab segment travels now.\n- Ranked bars used a raw <a href>, which full-page-reloads an SPA and ignores\n  any router basename. My test asserted the href and passed either way; it now\n  clicks the bar and asserts the destination rendered.\n- The chart keyed rows by label, and labels collide — two ops can share a\n  description, and every empty one renders as \"(no description)\". A duplicate\n  key makes React reuse the wrong node on re-sort.\n- The chart section rendered unconditionally, so an empty project got\n  \"Nothing to rank yet\" stacked on top of the \"tracing is off\" notice.\n\nThree regression tests cover the first three.\n\n243 backend tests, 67 frontend tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"98f2b68aff2fd1bafb4dc473270ebb46cea2d177","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/98f2b68aff2fd1bafb4dc473270ebb46cea2d177"},"url"