605f5e269ba11310","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/7e4f840fba6e1f518625a074605f5e269ba11310"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/07a227397d6f5364d5dbc3b316ed3cd33e1439ef","sha":"07a227397d6f5364d5dbc3b316ed3cd33e1439ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/07a227397d6f5364d5dbc3b316ed3cd33e1439ef"}],"sha":"2cb1ac58bb3b753539e8eab2aad07f32be85973d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/2cb1ac58bb3b753539e8eab2aad07f32be85973d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/07a227397d6f5364d5dbc3b316ed3cd33e1439ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T18:57:52Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T18:57:52Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"feat: clickable spans with distribution, callers and traces to open\n\nThree things, the first of which is an admission.\n\nThe magnitude bars failed. The question they prompted was \"what are these\ngraphs?\", and a mark that has to be explained is not carrying information. The\nfirst version filled the whole cell behind the number, which read as a\nhighlight rather than a quantity — cells looked arbitrarily selected and the\nbars fought the digits they were supposed to describe.\n\nThey are now a 3px rule on the baseline of the cell: unmistakably a bar,\nquiet enough that the number stays the subject, tinted neutral instead of\nbrand blue. Only the column the table is sorted by gets the strong tint,\nbecause six competing bars lead the eye nowhere. Each carries a title saying\nwhat it is a percentage of, so the answer is one hover away rather than a\nguess.\n\nSecond: spans are clickable, and the detail page is the step between \"this is\nthe problem\" and \"here is the request where it happened\".\n\n- A duration distribution, bucketed in SQL. A p50 and a p95 describe two\n  points; the shape between them says whether this is one slow tail or two\n  behaviours wearing the same statement, and those need different fixes.\n- Which endpoints call it, ranked by time contributed. The aggregate says a\n  query is expensive; this says who makes it expensive.\n- Traces to open, slowest first, each linking straight into the waterfall.\n  Sorted by time a sample list shows what happened last; sorted by duration it\n  shows the one worth opening.\n\nAn empty window returns 404 with a message about the period rather than a bare\nnot-found, because \"this span does not exist\" and \"nothing matched in the last\nhour\" are different and one of them is alarming.\n\nThird, correlation gains a link it was missing: span aggregate -> span detail\n-> a specific trace -> its waterfall, errors and logs. That chain now runs\nend to end without anybody copying an id between pages.\n\nOne test expectation was wrong rather than the code: with a 40ms outlier the\n20 buckets are 2ms wide, so 5ms lands in bucket two, not bucket zero. The\nassertion now checks the actual shape — mass low, one bucket at the top —\nwhich is the property worth asserting anyway.\n\n243 backend tests, 57 frontend tests.\n\nVerified against the running stack:\n  SELECT total FROM orders WHERE id = %s\n  calls=225  per_request=25.0  p95=2.8ms  total=545.5ms\n  callers: /report  225 calls  545.5ms\n  traces:  3.4ms of 78.1ms -> /traces/f1780cca\n  distribution: 9 non-empty buckets of 20\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dab1ca54ecdeb67e567994a14318f6c50273ec72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/dab1ca54ecdeb67e567994a14318f6c50273ec72"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/07a227397d6f5364d5dbc3b316ed3cd33e1439ef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/07a227397d6f5364d5dbc3b316ed3cd33e1439ef","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKDA3YTIyNzM5N2Q2ZjUzNjRkNWRiYzNiMzE2ZWQzY2QzM2UxNDM5ZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/7e4f840fb