iptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/873ba694a21acf73543e4d60aa5f55c60cbf5de7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T18:32:53Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T18:32:53Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"fix: drop an assertion that asserted nothing\n\n`body` is already unknown, so `as never` narrowed nothing and eslint''s typed\nrule rejected it.\n\nI missed this locally because I piped lint output through `tail -1`, which\nshowed the summary line and swallowed the error. Checking the exit code\ninstead of the last line of output is the actual fix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2c4919e8ca0df4188896c48609f5abd00de2d03e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/2c4919e8ca0df4188896c48609f5abd00de2d03e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/873ba694a21acf73543e4d60aa5f55c60cbf5de7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/873ba694a21acf73543e4d60aa5f55c60cbf5de7","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKDg3M2JhNjk0YTIxYWNmNzM1NDNlNGQ2MGFhNWY1NWM2MGNiZjVkZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/2267014ca47cfea89db5af16816c432835f9ab7b","sha":"2267014ca47cfea89db5af16816c432835f9ab7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/2267014ca47cfea89db5af16816c432835f9ab7b"}],"sha":"873ba694a21acf73543e4d60aa5f55c60cbf5de7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/873ba694a21acf73543e4d60aa5f55c60cbf5de7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/2267014ca47cfea89db5af16816c432835f9ab7b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T18:29:12Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T18:29:12Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"feat: instrument-panel UI — monospace measurements, magnitude cells, honest loading\n\nA visual direction rather than a coat of paint, built with the frontend-design\nplugin from the official marketplace. (There is no plugin called \"impeccable\"\nin any configured marketplace; frontend-design is the one that does this job.)\n\nThe brief this was designed against: Obsly is what somebody opens at 3am, and\nthe page''s single job is getting from \"something is wrong\" to \"here is the\nline of code\". The subject''s own vernacular is measurement — percentiles,\ndurations, span offsets, stack frames. Instruments are monospace, dense and\ntick-marked, so the interface now speaks the same language as the data it\nshows.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- Monospace is the voice of every measured value, and of the small labels that\n  scale them. Proportional sans is reserved for prose. Data was already\n  monospace in two places and sans in ten, which read as a dashboard about\n  numbers rather than an instrument showing them.\n- One spacing scale, tick-based, so the page has a rhythm instead of thirty\n  one-off pixel values.\n- Section labels are scale markings: 10.5px, wide tracking, muted. They were\n  competing with the content they label.\n\nThe signature is magnitude in the cell. Every measured value carries a bar of\nits own size behind it, scaled to its own column, so a table of latencies\nreads as a chart and the outlier is visible before anybody parses a digit. The\nnumber stays in front and stays exact — this is a second channel, not a\nreplacement. Each column scales independently, because a p50 and a p99 on one\nabsolute scale makes every p50 invisible. A test asserts a 10ms value against\na 1000ms maximum renders at 1% and not \"small but visible\": a dishonest bar is\nworse than no bar.\n\nLoading is a skeleton that holds the layout. Replacing a page with the word\n\"Loading\" and then swapping in a table moves everything under the cursor at\nthe moment somebody was about to click.\n\nDeliberately unchanged: the colour palette. Those surfaces and series values\nwere run through the data-viz validator, and repainting them would silently\ninvalidate every contrast check that passed. Boldness spent on type and one\nsignature element instead.\n\nQuality floor without announcing it: a visible focus ring everywhere rather\nthan only where somebody remembered one, reduced motion respected including\nthe skeleton sweep, and selection states carried by weight and aria-pressed\nrather than colour alone.\n\n53 frontend tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9cf12165f55309c9f7ee00df6cfc65f71118456c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/9cf12165f55309c9f7ee00df6cfc65f71118456c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/2267014ca47cfea89db5af16816c432835f9ab7b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafa