ttps://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/5e38a85330a167d8e634d80f39d27c2a806f385c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T17:58:17Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T17:58:17Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"fix: declare the trigram indexes on the model, not only in the migration\n\nmakemigrations --check wanted to remove them: the migration created indexes\nthe model state did not know about, so Django saw them as drift. CI caught\nwhat a hand-written migration always risks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"44a61359234bcaa5e9b6c03015dfdabdde8e616d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/44a61359234bcaa5e9b6c03015dfdabdde8e616d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/5e38a85330a167d8e634d80f39d27c2a806f385c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/5e38a85330a167d8e634d80f39d27c2a806f385c","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKDVlMzhhODUzMzBhMTY3ZDhlNjM0ZDgwZjM5ZDI3YzJhODA2ZjM4NWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/0dae473972e451876f3248c2458ac056dded76a6","sha":"0dae473972e451876f3248c2458ac056dded76a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/0dae473972e451876f3248c2458ac056dded76a6"}],"sha":"5e38a85330a167d8e634d80f39d27c2a806f385c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/5e38a85330a167d8e634d80f39d27c2a806f385c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/0dae473972e451876f3248c2458ac056dded76a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T17:55:39Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T17:55:39Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"feat: log search by level set, attribute search, and project-scoped detail pages\n\nThree things, all reported from using the thing.\n\nLevel filtering did one thing and it was the wrong one. `level=warning` meant\nwarning-and-worse, so looking at warnings alone was impossible — the errors\ndrowned them. Both readings are legitimate and people mean different ones:\n\n  levels=warning,error   an exact set, \"show me only these\"\n  min_level=warning      level-and-worse, what triage means by \"and above\"\n\nThe UI is toggles rather than a dropdown, because a single-select control can\nonly ask one of those questions. Selection is carried by weight, fill and\naria-pressed, never by colour alone. An exact set beats a minimum when both\narrive: the more specific instruction wins, and silently ANDing them returns\nnothing and looks like a broken filter. An unknown level is ignored rather\nthan matching nothing.\n\nSearch now covers attribute values as well as message and logger. Request ids\nand user ids live in attributes, and one search box should reach them.\n\nAnd it is index-backed. `body__icontains` was a sequential scan over every row\nin the window — the query that stops working first on a table that grows by a\nrow per log line, and it stops working exactly when somebody is searching it\nduring an incident. A pg_trgm GIN index turns `%foo%` into an index lookup.\nConfirmed the planner will use it:\n\n  Bitmap Heap Scan on logs_logrecord\n    -> Bitmap Index Scan on log_body_trgm\n         Index Cond: (body ~~* ''%checkout%'')\n\nOn the 93 rows currently in the table the planner still picks a sequential\nscan, which is correct — the index is for the table this becomes, not the one\nit is.\n\nicontains rather than full-text search on purpose: a log line is not prose,\nand what people paste into that box is an order id or a hostname, which\nstemming would mangle.\n\nNavigation: issue and trace detail pages now live under the project layout, so\nopening an issue no longer drops you out of the project and strands you with\nno way back except the browser button. The old flat /issues/:id and\n/traces/:id routes still resolve, so a pasted or bookmarked link keeps working.\n\n236 backend tests, 51 frontend tests.\n\nVerified against the running stack:\n  all levels 93   levels=warning 5   levels=info 87\n  levels=info,warning 92   min_level=warning 6\n  q=checkout 45   q=cart 68\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d1a26c7a813742596cc551c360c2c0a533dbd0d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/d1a26c7a813742596cc551c360c2c0a533dbd0d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/0dae473972e451876f3248c2458ac056dded76a6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/0dae473972e451876f3248c2458ac056dded76a6","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKDBkYWU0NzM5NzJlNDUxODc2ZjMyNDhjMjQ1OGFjMDU2ZGRlZDc2YTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/ec28ec75984cf7029a744afb464f193eb76b6bdf","sha":"ec28ec75984cf7029a744afb464f193eb76b6bdf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/ec28ec75984cf7029a744afb464f193eb76b6bdf"}],"sha":"0dae473972e451876f3248c2458ac056dded76a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/0dae473972e451876f3248c2458ac056dded76a6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/ec28ec75984cf7029a744afb464f193eb76b6bdf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T17:39:04Z","email":"33451925+aafaq01@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T17:39:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Merge pull request #24 from aafaq01/feat/time-ranges\n\nfeat: time windows down to seconds, with granularity that follows the window","tree":{"sha":"4fd5572a38ccd3f6887dbdb2a6c9