4447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/ec28ec75984cf7029a744afb464f193eb76b6bdf","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKGVjMjhlYzc1OTg0Y2Y3MDI5YTc0NGFmYjQ2NGYxOTNlYjc2YjZiZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/3c5ee26b98dc90d6a06594811bca370102cec0cc","sha":"3c5ee26b98dc90d6a06594811bca370102cec0cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/3c5ee26b98dc90d6a06594811bca370102cec0cc"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/d0d86c68fc0ff9356a65ea7062b318225b65c884","sha":"d0d86c68fc0ff9356a65ea7062b318225b65c884","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/d0d86c68fc0ff9356a65ea7062b318225b65c884"}],"sha":"ec28ec75984cf7029a744afb464f193eb76b6bdf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/ec28ec75984cf7029a744afb464f193eb76b6bdf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/d0d86c68fc0ff9356a65ea7062b318225b65c884/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T17:36:38Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T17:36:38Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"feat: time windows down to seconds, with granularity that follows the window\n\nThe period picker offered four choices, all of them hours or days, and every\nchart bucketed by hour regardless. An hour bucketed hourly is one bar, which\nsays nothing; five minutes bucketed hourly is the same bar. Watching a deploy\nor reproducing something was not possible at all.\n\nTwelve periods now, from 1m to 30d, and the bucket is derived from the window\nrather than fixed:\n\n  window <= 5m    second buckets\n  window <= 6h    minute buckets\n  window <= 7d    hour buckets\n  beyond          day buckets\n\nChosen so a window always has enough points to show a shape and few enough to\ndraw. Verified across every period against the running stack:\n\n  1m  -> 1s buckets, 61 points        6h  -> 60s, 361 points\n  5m  -> 1s buckets, 301 points       24h -> 1h, 25 points\n  30m -> 60s buckets, 31 points       7d  -> 1h, 169 points\n  1h  -> 60s buckets, 61 points       30d -> 1d, 31 points\n\nOnly Django''s own Trunc kinds, so the database does the bucketing. That is not\nonly for speed: a percentile has to be computed at the bucket''s own\ngranularity, because computing it coarsely and re-splitting in Python averages\npercentiles, and an average of percentiles is not a percentile of anything.\n\nThe first bucket is aligned to the grid the database truncates to. Without\nthat alignment the leading bucket is a partial one the query never fills, and\nevery chart opens with a phantom gap.\n\nOne module holds the periods, the granularity table and the bucket list, and\nevery page reads from it — five pages each had their own hardcoded list, which\nis how two pages come to disagree about what \"last 24 hours\" offers. The\npicker is one component for the same reason.\n\nAxes are unit-aware, so a five-minute window is no longer labelled \"0h ago\",\nand 86400s reads as \"24h\" rather than \"1d\" — the picker calls that window\n\"Last 24 hours\", and an axis that disagrees with the control above it looks\nlike a bug.\n\nAn unknown period falls back to the default instead of erroring: a typo in a\nquery string should show the usual window, not a 400 nobody can act on.\n\n230 backend tests, 49 frontend tests.\n\nAlso confirmed while here: the demo app already enables logs. enable_logs=True\nand the stdlib handler have been wired since the logs change; it has no\nSQLAlchemy, which is why it has no instrument() call.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4fd5572a38ccd3f6887dbdb2a6c99a1badbb1036","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/4fd5572a38ccd3f6887dbdb2a6c99a1badbb1036"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/d0d86c68fc0ff9356a65ea7062b318225b65c884","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"