6-08-11T17:15:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/3c5ee26b98dc90d6a06594811bca370102cec0cc","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKDNjNWVlMjZiOThkYzkwZDZhMDY1OTQ4MTFiY2EzNzAxMDJjZWMwY2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/a51f1b2dddd6fb6204181f20f4f4a2c9b5b14554","sha":"a51f1b2dddd6fb6204181f20f4f4a2c9b5b14554","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/a51f1b2dddd6fb6204181f20f4f4a2c9b5b14554"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/75589d734811c9828ebcfef6e18ae1caf71ae520","sha":"75589d734811c9828ebcfef6e18ae1caf71ae520","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/75589d734811c9828ebcfef6e18ae1caf71ae520"}],"sha":"3c5ee26b98dc90d6a06594811bca370102cec0cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/3c5ee26b98dc90d6a06594811bca370102cec0cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/75589d734811c9828ebcfef6e18ae1caf71ae520/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T17:08:04Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T17:08:04Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"feat: detect N+1 and slow queries, and file them as issues\n\nThe difference between a tracing tool and an observability one. A waterfall\nshows a human 25 identical queries and waits for them to notice. A detector\nnotices, and files it with the same triage workflow as an error — assign it,\nresolve it, have it reopen when it comes back.\n\nA performance issue is an Issue, not a separate table, so it inherits that\nworkflow instead of needing its own. It carries a category, a type, and the\nevidence the detector found.\n\nEvery detector answers three questions, and one that cannot answer all three\nis not worth firing:\n\n  what is wrong    the offending span\n  how bad is it    time that would be saved, not just a count\n  where to look    the transaction, and the trace it happened in\n\nThresholds are deliberately conservative — 10 repeats and 50ms for an N+1,\n1000ms for a slow query. A handful of repeats is a loop somebody wrote on\npurpose, and ten repeats of a 0.1ms cached read is not worth a human''s\nmorning. A detector that fires on a healthy application teaches people to\nignore it, and an ignored detector is worse than none: same attention, no\nreturn.\n\nDetails that decide whether anybody trusts the number:\n\n- Recoverable time excludes the one query you would keep. One of those 25 is\n  legitimate; reporting the whole total overstates the saving and loses trust\n  the first time somebody checks.\n- The same slow query on two endpoints is two issues. Different callers,\n  different fix.\n- Statements are already parameterised, so bind values cannot split one issue\n  into thousands.\n- Performance issues are filed at warning, not error. Filing a slow query\n  beside a crash is how an issue stream stops being a priority list.\n- Detection runs after storage and its failure is caught. The transaction is\n  already saved; a detector that cannot run costs an insight, not a\n  measurement.\n\nOne naming bug caught by the linter: the loop variable was called\n`transaction`, shadowing the django.db module that the @transaction.atomic\ndecorator on the next function depends on.\n\n228 backend tests, 49 frontend tests.\n\nVerified on 50 requests to the demo app, with nobody looking for either:\n\n  [n_plus_one_queries]  on /report\n      SELECT total FROM orders WHERE id = %s\n      repeats=25  total=60.2ms  recoverable=57.8ms\n\n  [slow_db_query]       on /slow\n      SELECT * FROM analytics_rollup\n      total=1101.4ms  recoverable=1101.4ms\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ceb2287bd4856e014dd6722b96c34281a5221606","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/ceb2287bd4856e014dd6722b96c34281a5221606"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/75589d734811c9828ebcfef6e18ae1caf71ae520","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at