"verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-11T11:27:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/18a920ce55f4ba34ab1f7e45958e0f9eb9944b94","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKDE4YTkyMGNlNTVmNGJhMzRhYjFmN2U0NTk1OGUwZjllYjk5NDRiOTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/266eb8a4bd9966134b8a0cbce155b0207dfd9a17","sha":"266eb8a4bd9966134b8a0cbce155b0207dfd9a17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/266eb8a4bd9966134b8a0cbce155b0207dfd9a17"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/f4e126a34e261ae461ac479f59132e61c3dfc0a9","sha":"f4e126a34e261ae461ac479f59132e61c3dfc0a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/f4e126a34e261ae461ac479f59132e61c3dfc0a9"}],"sha":"18a920ce55f4ba34ab1f7e45958e0f9eb9944b94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/18a920ce55f4ba34ab1f7e45958e0f9eb9944b94"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/f4e126a34e261ae461ac479f59132e61c3dfc0a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T11:19:24Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T11:19:24Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"feat: automatic database spans for SQLAlchemy\n\n    obsly.integrations.sqlalchemy.instrument()\n\nOne line, and every query the application runs appears inside the trace of the\nrequest that ran it — with no start_span() calls anywhere in the application.\n\nThat distinction is the whole feature. Manual instrumentation only ever covers\nthe code somebody remembered to annotate, and the queries nobody remembered\nare exactly the ones that turn out to be the problem.\n\n- Listens on the SQLAlchemy Engine class rather than an instance, so an\n  application that builds its engine later, or builds several, is covered\n  without handing each one over.\n- Parameter values are never captured. The statement is recorded as SQLAlchemy\n  hands it over, with binds still as placeholders — the values are the row\n  itself, which is where the personal data lives. A test asserts a bound email\n  address does not appear anywhere in the payload.\n- Statements are collapsed to one line. A multi-line ORM SELECT is unreadable\n  in a waterfall row, and the indentation is not what identifies the query.\n- A failing query still produces a span. It took time, and the span is the only\n  record of how long.\n- Returns False when SQLAlchemy is absent instead of raising. An optional\n  integration that breaks startup by being unavailable is worse than one that\n  is simply missing.\n- Instrumenting twice is a no-op, because a framework and an application both\n  calling it is normal.\n- Every failure path inside the instrumentation is swallowed and logged.\n  Instrumentation must never break the query it is measuring.\n\nThis needed a lower-level span API: before/after callbacks cannot hold a\ncontext manager open across them, so begin_span/end_span expose the two halves.\nThe span carries its own contextvar token rather than relying on the call\nstack.\n\nTwo things the tests caught:\n- The engines were never disposed, so sqlite finalised connections during\n  garbage collection and pytest reported unraisable exceptions. Now a fixture\n  with teardown.\n- The span was stashed on the SQLAlchemy connection, not on the integration\n  module. A module-level dict would be shared across concurrent connections and\n  hand one query''s span to another.\n\n55 SDK tests, 203 backend tests.\n\nVerified on the real full-stack-fastapi-template, which was already using\nSQLAlchemy and had no Obsly span calls in it:\n\n  /login/access-token  9.0ms  status=internal_error\n      db.query   2.5ms  SELECT \"user\".email, \"user\".is_active, …\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f55f57cabdc4e3694c42bd125752f570a0916001","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/f55f57cabdc4e3694c42bd125752f570a0916001"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/f4e126a34e261ae461ac479f59132e61c3dfc0a9","verificati