/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/4edb0b61543309a418e94eec7bc364bc75d6990c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/0e7cb9aecf3ff8e8f0c15550a26c8bcfcff3dea5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/0e7cb9aecf3ff8e8f0c15550a26c8bcfcff3dea5","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKDBlN2NiOWFlY2YzZmY4ZThmMGMxNTU1MGEyNmM4YmNmY2ZmM2RlYTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/9fbbde8fc696ef59e18d3c6cd6c4c51c2fbd0e81","sha":"9fbbde8fc696ef59e18d3c6cd6c4c51c2fbd0e81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/9fbbde8fc696ef59e18d3c6cd6c4c51c2fbd0e81"}],"sha":"0e7cb9aecf3ff8e8f0c15550a26c8bcfcff3dea5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/0e7cb9aecf3ff8e8f0c15550a26c8bcfcff3dea5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/9fbbde8fc696ef59e18d3c6cd6c4c51c2fbd0e81/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T17:23:59Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T17:23:59Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"feat: structured logs, correlated with the request that produced them\n\nErrors say what broke. Traces say where the time went. Logs say what the\napplication was saying — including on the requests that succeeded, which is\nmost of them and where the explanation for the failures usually lives.\n\nSDK:\n- obsly.logger.info(...) for new code, and ObslyLogHandler for the logging an\n  application already does. The second matters more: an SDK that only sees\n  logs written specially for it sees the least interesting ones. Attaching one\n  handler forwards every existing call site.\n- The stdlib bridge keeps the un-interpolated template as an attribute.\n  \"user %s not found\" is one line in the UI; the formatted string is ten\n  thousand distinct ones.\n- The handler never raises into the application. A logging handler that raises\n  turns every log call into a failure, so it routes through\n  logging.Handler.handleError, which is the documented place for this.\n- Off unless enable_logs is set. Logs are the highest-volume signal by a wide\n  margin — an application emits them on every request, not only the failing\n  ones.\n- Every record carries the active trace and span.\n\nServer: LogRecord, indexed on (project, -timestamp) for the viewer and on\n(trace_id, timestamp) for the correlated read. Level filtering means\nlevel-and-worse, because filtering to exactly one level hides the errors and\nnobody means that. A record with an empty body is dropped — it is a row nobody\ncan read or search.\n\nTwo bugs found by running it rather than by reading it:\n\n- The buffer only checked its own age inside add(), so the last lines of any\n  burst sat stranded until the application happened to log again. Visible in\n  the data: a successful checkout logged three lines and one was stored. Fixed\n  with a background flusher, and the end of a burst is usually the part worth\n  reading.\n- Starting that flusher before self._transport was assigned is a race the\n  thread loses on its first tick. Moved after, with a comment saying why the\n  order is not arbitrary.\n\nAlso deleted a drop guard in the buffer that could never fire: the buffer\nempties every time it reaches capacity, so it cannot grow past it, and the\nbound that matters under a burst is the transport queue. A second limiter was\ndead code pretending to protect something.\n\nThe demo app now uses ordinary logging.getLogger() calls — nothing written for\nObsly — on both the success and failure paths.\n\n203 backend tests, 49 SDK tests, 43 frontend tests.\n\nVerified against the running stack, 60 requests:\n\n  log records: 51, with a trace_id: 50\n\n  ONE REQUEST: /checkout/{cart_id}  292ms  status=ok\n      [info] demo: checkout started for cart c-1\n      [info] demo: charging card for cart c-1\n      [info] demo: checkout complete for cart c-1, total 9.99\n\nA successful request, and everything the application said while serving it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0ad21c9fa71997c8ab636ac1cd4976d4a0163465","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/0ad21c9fa71997c8ab636ac1cd4976d4a0163465"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/9fbbde8fc696ef59e18d3c6cd6c4c51c2fbd0e81","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/9fbbde8fc696ef59e18d3c6cd6c4c51c2fbd0e81","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKDlmYmJkZThmYzY5NmVmNTllMThkM2M2Y2Q2YzRjNTFjMmZiZDBlODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/38e368f08492ab21ef10bb587d739e24766b770c","sha":"38e368f08492ab21ef10bb587d739e24766b770c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/38e368f08492ab21ef10bb587d739e24766b770c"}],"sha":"9fbbde8fc696ef59e18d3c6cd6c4c51c2fbd0e81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/9fbbde8fc696ef59e18d3c6cd6c4c51c2fbd0e81"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://a