:"24b508069db87ed9954ede3d8e42735b315c4754","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/24b508069db87ed9954ede3d8e42735b315c4754"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/2aadad23525c0ea2a26ccfde9d1ca3795bc6b1eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T16:03:52Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T16:03:52Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"feat: correlate errors with the traces they happened inside\n\nErrors and traces were two tables that shared a database and nothing else.\nJoining them by timestamp is guesswork; joining them by trace_id is an index\nlookup. This is the correlation the whole data model was shaped for.\n\n- The SDK attaches the active trace and the innermost active span to every\n  captured error, so the link is recorded at the moment of failure rather than\n  inferred later. An error raised outside a transaction carries no trace, and\n  an unsampled transaction attaches none either — a link to a trace that was\n  never recorded is a dead link, which is worse than admitting there is none.\n- trace_id and span_id are stored on Event, indexed, and validated as hex of\n  exactly the right length. A junk value would silently point an error at a\n  trace that does not exist.\n- An issue now reports the transaction its latest event happened inside: name,\n  duration, status. A trace now reports the errors recorded inside it, each\n  linking back to its issue.\n- Scoped by project as well as trace_id. Two services can legitimately share a\n  trace id; their errors are still not each other''s to display.\n\nBoth directions are one click in the UI: a banner on the issue page, an\n\"Errors in this request\" list above the waterfall.\n\nAlso adds examples/fastapi-demo — a FastAPI app that fails in many different\nways on purpose, plus a weighted traffic generator. It exists because \"grouping\nseparates two bugs behind one route\" is a claim, and a stream you can look at\nis evidence. Traffic is weighted so the result looks real: two loud issues,\nseveral quiet ones, more successes than failures.\n\nRun against it, 120 requests:\n\n  10x  error    ConnectionError: payments.example.com returned 502\n   9x  error    KeyError: ''cart c-missing vanished mid-checkout''\n   7x  error    ValueError: legacy pricing table is missing column…\n   7x  error    RuntimeError: could not load order 42\n   6x  error    KeyError: ''email''\n   5x  warning  search query truncated from 80 characters\n   4x  warning  empty search query reached the index\n   2x  error    ZeroDivisionError: division by zero\n\n  events=50  transactions=92  spans=145\n  events with a trace_id: 50 of 50\n\nThe first two are the same route. Grouping separated them on frames, which is\nexactly what it is for.\n\nAnd the loop closes:\n\n  issue  ConnectionError: payments.example.com returned 502\n    -> trace /checkout/{cart_id}  131ms  internal_error\n         db.query      14.6ms  SELECT * FROM carts WHERE id = %s\n         db.query       3.1ms  SELECT * FROM items WHERE cart_id = %s\n         http.client  111.7ms  POST payments.example.com/charge\n    -> error back to issue #9\n\nThe waterfall names the culprit: the payment call, not the database.\n\n187 backend tests, 39 SDK tests, 39 frontend tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"42d593bb4a4d030475c9c7602ca309f83e77f51c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/42d593bb4a4d030475c9c7602ca309f83e77f51c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/2aadad23525c0ea2a26ccfde9d1ca3795bc6b1eb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/2aadad23525c0ea2a26ccfde9d1ca3795bc6b1eb","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKDJhYWRhZDIzNTI1YzBlYTJhMjZjY2ZkZTlkMWNhMzc5NWJjNmIxZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/d1ee16dcb5c324845136818236d3e5302c54120f","sha":"d1ee16dcb5c324845136818236d