obsly/commits/f033bfe081a24ed344e9b7217ef4e6593eb7db7c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/960b13575b3fa86ed13bacecf06e822c832ad99f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T15:00:43Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T15:00:43Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"feat: distributed tracing — spans, transactions and trace propagation\n\nErrors say what broke. Transactions say where the time went, and they are the\ndata every latency percentile is computed from.\n\nSDK:\n- start_transaction / start_span, held in contextvars rather than\n  thread-locals. An async framework runs many requests on one thread, and a\n  thread-local span would leak one request''s timings into another''s trace.\n- The ASGI middleware opens a transaction per request and names it by matched\n  route pattern, resolved after routing. \"/items/{item_id}\" aggregates;\n  \"/items/8123\" produces a row per id and a percentile computed over one\n  sample.\n- HTTP status is translated to a gRPC-style label, so \"did it work\" is one\n  field rather than a numeric range check at every call site.\n- traces_sample_rate defaults to 0. Tracing multiplies event volume by however\n  many requests a service handles, and nobody should discover that from a bill.\n- The sampling decision is made once at the head of a trace and propagated via\n  the obsly-trace header. Deciding per service produces traces with holes in\n  the middle, which read as \"that service was never called\" rather than \"we\n  chose not to record it\".\n- A malformed inbound trace header starts a new trace instead of raising. A\n  broken header from an upstream we do not control must never fail the request\n  carrying it.\n- start_span is a no-op with no active transaction, so instrumentation inside\n  a library does not depend on whether the application enabled tracing.\n- Spans per transaction are capped at 1000 and the overflow counted. A runaway\n  loop must cost a truncated trace, not the memory of the process being\n  observed.\n\nServer:\n- duration_ms is stored, not derived from two timestamps on every read.\n  Percentiles scan every row in the window, and making Postgres subtract\n  timestamps a few million times per query is the difference between a chart\n  and a timeout.\n- Span carries no created_at/updated_at. Spans arrive in bulk and are never\n  edited; two timestamp columns on the highest-volume table is storage spent\n  on nothing.\n- A negative duration is rejected — a clock that moved backwards would give a\n  p95 below the p50 and make the chart untrustworthy. Anything over an hour is\n  rejected too: that is a stuck process, not a slow request, and it drags every\n  percentile it lands in.\n- An unnamed transaction is rejected. It cannot be grouped, filtered or\n  charted, so it is a row nobody can use.\n- Spans are only inserted when their transaction was newly created, so a\n  replayed envelope does not grow the span table without adding information.\n\n156 backend tests, 35 SDK tests.\n\nVerified against the running stack with the FastAPI template tracing at 100%:\n  9 transactions stored, named by route pattern\n    /utils/health-check/    ok               0.6-1.1ms\n    /login/access-token     internal_error   106.2ms\n\nSpans are 0 in that run, and correctly so: the request is instrumented but\nnothing yet instruments the database, so there is no inner work to record.\nDatabase span instrumentation is the next change, and it is what turns a\nduration into an explanation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"91f5e96d82e3d9baff8e12310c6cfe0f892cf710","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/91f5e96d82e3d9baff8e12310c6cfe0f892cf710"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/960b13575b3fa86ed13bacecf06e822c832ad99f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/960b13575b3