,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T14:34:59Z","email":"m.aafaq.rana@gmail.com","name":"Aafaq Rana"},"message":"feat: sign in from the app instead of the Django admin\n\nThe UI borrowed the admin''s session, so using the product started with a trip\nthrough an operator tool. Obsly now has its own login, and the admin is no\nlonger on the path.\n\nSessions rather than tokens: the API and UI are same-origin behind one nginx,\nso a HttpOnly session cookie cannot be read by injected script while a token\nin localStorage can. The cost is CSRF, which Django already handles.\n\n- /api/0/me/ is AllowAny and reports {authenticated, username}. It has to be:\n  a 403 runs before the view and never sets a CSRF cookie, so a first-time\n  visitor would be unable to sign in at all.\n- Wrong password and unknown user return one identical response. Different\n  messages turn a login form into an account-enumeration oracle.\n- login() cycles the session key, so a session fixated before sign-in is\n  worthless after it.\n- logout() flushes the session server-side. Clearing only the cookie leaves a\n  session that still authenticates anyone holding a copy.\n- The login endpoint is throttled by IP at 10/min. By IP and not by username,\n  because per-username throttling lets an attacker lock a real user out on\n  purpose and does nothing about spraying one password across many accounts.\n\nA test-isolation bug found on the way: DRF keeps throttle history in the\ncache, which outlives a test. One test exhausting the login throttle made a\nlater test fail with 429, and which test failed depended on execution order —\nso it presented as flake rather than as the shared state it was. conftest now\nclears the cache around every test.\n\n138 backend tests, 20 frontend tests. Verified through nginx:\n  GET  /api/0/me/ anonymous  -> {\"authenticated\":false}, csrftoken set\n  POST wrong password        -> 401 \"Incorrect username or password.\"\n  POST correct password      -> 200, /api/0/projects/ then 200\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6dc3fdc497b2e6422232a92d92b4953a6649dc07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/trees/6dc3fdc497b2e6422232a92d92b4953a6649dc07"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/git/commits/cfb43bbdf59c510257a8c4df84e77d506e24f678","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33451925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01","id":33451925,"login":"aafaq01","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNDUxOTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aafaq01","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/cfb43bbdf59c510257a8c4df84e77d506e24f678","node_id":"C_kwDOTveDc9oAKGNmYjQzYmJkZjU5YzUxMDI1N2E4YzRkZjg0ZTc3ZDUwNmUyNGY2Nzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aafaq01/obsly/commit/0daea17d9db147a227c3f2351bb2439bac7028cd","sha":"0daea17d9db147a227c3f2351bb2439bac7028cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/0daea17d9db147a227c3f2351bb2439bac7028cd"}],"sha":"cfb43bbdf59c510257a8c4df84e77d506e24f678","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aafaq01/obsly/commits/cfb43bbdf59c510257a8c4df84e77d506e24f678"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://